 to Redefine What “Knowledge Work” Looks Like - by Renée Fishman","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/It’s Time to Redefine What “Knowledge Work” Looks Like - by Renée Fishman.md","lastModified":"2024-09-17T20:03:09.899Z","tags":[],"content":"# It’s Time to Redefine What “Knowledge Work” Looks Like - by Renée Fishman\nby [[Renée Fishman]]\n\n[It’s Time to Redefine What “Knowledge Work” Looks Like - Renée Fishman](https://mymeadowreport.com/reneefishman/2022/redefine-knowledge-work)\n\n> Renée Fishman argues for redefining \"knowledge work,\" which is traditionally seen as [[but in seat|desk-bound]], sedentary work. She criticizes this paradigm, pointing out that it doesn't suit everyone, especially those like her who need frequent movement to stay energized and [[Productivity|productive]]. Fishman explains that she works best when allowed to move, whether it's through vigorous activity or working in unconventional positions, like [[sitting on the floor]]. \n> \n> She challenges the [[societal norm]] that equates sitting still with [[Productivity|productivity]] and suggests this [[sedentary]] approach contributes to [[stress-related health issues]]. Fishman advocates greater inclusivity of different working styles, especially for those who need to move frequently, like individuals with [[ADHD]], emphasizing that the human body is designed for movement, not long periods of stillness. She calls for workplaces and schools to [[Requested Accommodations Under the ADA|accommodate]] diverse working styles, arguing that \"[[but in seat|butt in chair]]\" shouldn't be the standard for everyone.\n\nRelated:\n- [[sitting sucks]]\n- [[time at the gym]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Requested Accommodations Under the ADA","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Requested Accommodations Under the ADA.md","lastModified":"2024-09-17T20:03:09.814Z","tags":[],"content":"---\naliases:\n  - accommodate\n---\n# Requested Accommodations Under the ADA\n\nRelated:\n- [[Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA)]]\n- [[Potential Accommodations for ADHD Under the ADA]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Potential Accommodations for ADHD Under the ADA","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Potential Accommodations for ADHD Under the ADA.md","lastModified":"2024-09-17T19:52:12.395Z","tags":[],"content":"# Potential Accommodations for ADHD Under the ADA\n\n## AI suggested accommodations based on [[2023 GGC Performance Review - Charles]]\n\n1. **Time Management & Deadlines**:\n   - Request for **structured timelines** with more frequent check-ins to ensure you're on track, especially for larger, long-term projects like policy reviews or security incident responses.\n   - **Reminders** or tools to help with task prioritization, as issues with meeting deadlines or responding in a timely manner were noted.\n\n2. **Clarity in Expectations**:\n   - Ask for **clear, detailed instructions** and **written summaries** of meetings or assignments. This can help address the feedback about not meeting quality expectations or misunderstanding project goals.\n\n3. **Communication Support**:\n   - Consider asking for **communication coaching** to help with managing emotions in professional communication, as this was mentioned as an area needing improvement.\n   - Accommodations like **templates or scripts** for difficult conversations can help ensure clear, concise, and emotionally neutral communications.\n\n4. **Collaboration & Accountability**:\n   - Request a **collaborative workflow** that includes more **structured team meetings** or **status updates** to improve interpersonal relationships and ensure follow-up on commitments.\n\n5. **Task Management Support**:\n   - You could benefit from accommodations like **task management software** or tools to help with organizing tasks and ensuring the quality of deliverables.\n   - **Delegation training** to assist in delegating tasks effectively while ensuring accountability for the final quality.\n\n6. **Flexibility with Work Style**:\n   - Consider asking for **flexibility in work hours or environment**, especially if ADHD impacts your ability to focus during traditional hours or in certain settings.\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2023 GGC Performance Review - Response Action Plan","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Performance Management/Charles H. Leggett/2023/2023 GGC Performance Review - Response Action Plan.md","lastModified":"2024-09-17T19:51:01.674Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2023 GGC Performance Review - Response Action Plan\n\n### Communication and Transparency\n\nI understand that fostering trust through consistent and transparent communication is crucial. I also understand that developing a robust communication strategy to accompany technical changes ensures that end users are well-informed and prepared. Preparing these plans will build my own credibility and the credibility of the IT team as a whole. I will focus on consistent, transparent communication to build trust and reduce misunderstandings. Developing these comprehensive communication plans, including clear timelines, training sessions, and support resources, will minimize disruption and build trust within the campus community.\n\n### Reliability and Quality of Work\n\nI understand that delivering high-quality work on time improves perception of reliability and dependability. I will prioritize creating polished and timely deliverables by starting preparations early, closely following instructions, and thoroughly reviewing documents before submission. By ensuring that all deliverables are meticulously prepared, I will help to enhance our reputation for dependability and professionalism.\n\n### Collaboration and Feedback\n\nI understand that building trusted partnerships and fostering a collaborative environment can only be achieved by actively seeking feedback from internal and external stakeholders to better understand their needs and expectations. I will encourage team members to share knowledge and collaborate on projects to promote a culture of openness and mutual respect and do the same myself. I will address concerns promptly, and demonstrate a commitment to improving relationships, by acting on feedback to build trust and strengthen professional relationships. These actions will help me to enhance my own performance, contribute to the team's success, and drive continuous improvement.\n\n\nRelated:\n- [[Potential Accommodations for ADHD Under the ADA]]\n- ","bookmarked":false},{"title":"EMTech","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Groups/EMTech.md","lastModified":"2024-09-17T18:26:04.000Z","tags":[],"content":"---\ndate: 2024-07-09\ntags:\n---\n# EMTech\n## Project\n## Team\n## Tasks\n## Communications\n## Docs\n## Reference\n## Meeting Notes\n\n### ![[2024-08-07 - Management - EMTech]]\n\n### ![[2024-09-10 - Management - EMTech]]\n\n\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2024-08-07 - Wednesday","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Journal/2024/2024-08 - August/2024-08-07 - Wednesday.md","lastModified":"2024-09-17T18:26:03.987Z","tags":["#shallow"],"content":"---\nperiodicNotes: daily\naliases:\n  - 2024-08-07\ndate: 2024-08-07\nprevious: \"[[2024-08-06 - Tuesday]]\"\nday: \"[[2024-08-07 - Wednesday]]\"\nnext: \"[[2024-08-08 - Thursday]]\"\nweek: \"[[2024-W32]]\"\ntags: \nhoursSlept: 5\nhoursCoffeeTime: 2\nhoursExercised: 0.5\nhoursProjectWork: 0\nhoursDeepWork: 0\nhoursMeetings: 3\nhoursScreenTime: 6.75\nsystolic: 113\ndiastolic: 75\nreflection: true\nmigration: false\nplanning: false\ntriage: false\ntasksCoffee: false\ntasksMorning: false\ntasksAfternoon: false\ntasksEvening: false\nwindDown: false\ndaily: false\ntoday: false\nmetrics: true\n---\n# 2024-08-07 - Wednesday\n[[2024-08-06 - Tuesday|Previous Day]] | [[2024-W32|This Week]] | [[2024-08-08 - Thursday|Next Day]]\n```meta-bind-embed\n[[Daily Header]]\n```\n## Plan\n1. [[2024-08