[[IAM]]\n# Troubleshooting marroyo3 Account Last Name Change\nfrom [Help Desk](https://helpdesk.ggc.edu/incidents/137644276-email-access)\ncreated [GitHub Issue #22](https://github.com/ggc-oit/PS-Scripts/issues/22)\ndiscussion [Teams](https://teams.microsoft.com/l/message/19:meeting_NmIzNDBhZjAtNGI4MS00MGNmLWFmNzItODNlOThlMmQ4MmYy@thread.v2/1722425625694?context=%7B%22contextType%22%3A%22chat%22%7D)\n\n## Conclusion\nI found that there is no logic in [[ADPop.ps1]] to update names after they have been updated in the provisioning file(s) from our source of truth, so I updated their last name manually.\n\n## Findings\nWhen an account_create*.csv file is updated by the source of truth, the property updates should be propagated to AD.\n\nFor example, the last name is not updated:\n\nhttps://github.com/ggc-oit/PS-Scripts/blob/dbe5ae0aad23679f5c0d7f78ecf1b3935a6da472/ADPop.ps1#L202\n\nWe discovered this while troubleshooting an update to the marroyo3 account. Initially (2024-01-23), their last name was created as \"Arroyo37\". It was updated the following month (2024-02-27) to be \"Arroyo\", but AD was not updated until I did it manually today.\n\n### account_create entries for marroyo3\n```\nPS Z:\\> Get-ChildItem Z:\\*2024* | Select-String -Pattern \"marroyo3\" | Select-Object -Unique Path\n\nPath\n----\nZ:\\applied_20240116.csv\nZ:\\applied_20240117.csv\nZ:\\applied_20240118.csv\nZ:\\applied_20240119.csv\nZ:\\applied_20240120.csv\nZ:\\applied_20240121.csv\nZ:\\applied_20240122.csv\nZ:\\applied_20240123.csv\nZ:\\students_20240227.csv\nZ:\\students_20240228.csv\nZ:\\students_20240229.csv\nZ:\\students_20240301.csv\nZ:\\students_20240302.csv\nZ:\\students_20240304.csv\nZ:\\students_20240305.csv\nZ:\\students_20240306.csv\nZ:\\students_20240307.csv\nZ:\\students_20240308.csv\nZ:\\students_20240309.csv\nZ:\\students_20240310.csv\nZ:\\students_20240311.csv\nZ:\\students_20240312.csv\nZ:\\students_20240313.csv\nZ:\\students_20240314.csv\nZ:\\students_20240315.csv\nZ:\\students