ate to the Authentication methods policy - Microsoft Entra ID | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/authentication/how-to-authentication-methods-manage) (2025-09 deadline)\n- [https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/compliance/essential-eight/e8-mfa-configure-authentication-strengths](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/compliance/essential-eight/e8-mfa-configure-authentication-strengths)\n\n### Microsoft's Recommendations\n\n|                                                    |                                                  |                 |                      |              |               |                  |              |                           |                                 |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | --------------- | -------------------- | ------------ | ------------- | ---------------- | ------------ | ------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| **Authentication method**                          | GGC (as is) SSPR (2 of as many as they have set) | GGC (as is) MFA | GGC (to be) Combined | **Security** | **Usability** | **Availability** | MFA Strength | Passwordless MFA Strength | Phishing-resistant MFA Strength |\n| Windows Hello for Business                         |                                                  |                 |                      | High         | High          | High             | Yes          | Yes                       | Yes                             |\n| Microsoft Authenticator App - Push Notification    | Yes                                              | Yes             |                      | High         | High          | High             | Yes          | Yes                       |                                 |\n| Microsoft Authenticator - App Code (HOTP)          | Yes                                              | Yes             |                      |              |            