e to the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA), I will not respond to emails from other domains ([yahoo.com](http://yahoo.com/), [gmail.com](http://gmail.com/), [hotmail.com](http://hotmail.com/), etc.).\n> \n> When you email me, you should consider the email as official correspondence. As such, the email should not appear as a text message but should have proper spelling, grammar, and punctuation.\n> \n> Please address me as Dr. [Last Name], not by my first name.\n> \n> You should also check your [MyCourses](https://mycourses.ggc.edu/) (Brightspace by D2L) course site every day.\n> \n\n## Affiliate Types\n\n### Faculty\n### Staff\n\n### Emeritus\n#### Access\n1. Invitation to participate in public ceremonies of the college, including commencement and select college functions.\n2. Full library access (the same as active faculty), including remote access to electronic resources; Emeritus/a faculty should contact their institution’s library for details and credentials for remote access to electronic resources.\n3. Inclusion in the faculty/administrator listing in the college directory.\n4. Certificate with name and emeritus/a rank.\n5. If funds permit, entitlement to use university business cards and other office privileges for the purposes of college service.\n6. Eligibility to serve on project committees, and as nonvoting members of college committees as appropriate.\n##### Access Implication\n1. GGC Account\n2. Microsoft M365 A5 (or maybe lower) License\n3. Need a process to retain mailbox during [[affiliation change]] between employee and emeritus. (see [[2024-09-03 - Management - Christine 1on1#IAM - Define Emeritus Professor Status at GGC]])","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2024-09-03 - Tuesday","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Journal/2024/2024-09 - September/2024-09-03 - Tuesday.md","lastModified":"2024-09-17T12:47:31.422Z","tags":[],"content":"---\nperiodicNotes: daily\naliases:\n  - 2024-09-03\ndate: 2024-09-03\nprevious: \"[[2024-09