te - This Month]]\n> > ```","bookmarked":false},{"title":"This Week's Work","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/_LifeOS_/_Dashboard_/_Sections_/This Week's Work.md","lastModified":"2024-09-16T23:13:01.153Z","tags":[],"content":"> [!SUMMARY]+ This Week's Work\n> > [!TODO]- This Week's Projects\n> > ```meta-bind-embed\n> > [[Projects - Date - This Week]]\n> > ```\n> \n> > [!TODO]- This Week's Tasks\n> > ```meta-bind-embed\n> > [[Tasks - Date - This Week]]\n> > ```","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Agenda Items","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Agenda Items.md","lastModified":"2024-09-16T23:00:34.444Z","tags":[],"content":"# Agenda Items\n> [!QUOTE]+ Agenda Items\n> > [!todo]+ Projects\n> > ```tasks\n> > not done\n> > has tags\n> > group by tags\n> > sort by status.name\n> > ```\n> \n> > [!todo]+ Tasks\n> > ```tasks\n> > not done\n> > heading does not include Project\n> > has tags\n> > group by tags\n> > sort by status.name\n> > ```","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2023 GGC Performance Review - Charles","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Performance Management/Charles H. Leggett/2023/2023 GGC Performance Review - Charles.md","lastModified":"2024-09-16T22:45:15.747Z","tags":["#301"],"content":"# 2023 GGC Performance Review - Charles\nsee also [[2023 GGC Performance Review - Response Action Plan]]\n\n## Section 1 – Goals\n\n### Goal 1 - Update security incident response plan and convene CSIRT\nDescription: I believe USG is asking all campuses to update security incident response plans; this is also mentioned in our GLBA action items. The CSIRT needs to be planned, convened, and trained.\nManager Rating: \t2 - Partially Successful\t\nManager Comments:\tYou successfully updated the Cybersecurity Incident Response Plan in early 2024. The CSIRT has not met to my knowledge.\n### Goal 2 - Update cybersecurity program plan\nDescription: USG is also asking campuses for updated cybersecurity program plans. \nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\tYou successfully updated the Information Security Program Plan in early 2024. \n### Goal 3 - Enhance email protection\nDescription: Prevent, detect, and respond to email-based cyberattacks. \nManager Rating:\t 2 - Partially Successful\t\nManager Comments: \tThe mimecast implementation in late 2022 was bumpy. More planning for end user change management/training would have been beneficial. Change #301 was bumpy and had unintended consequences. I think some email protection progress was made in 2023 such as SPF delegation. We ended up transitioning from mimecast to Microsoft email protection in 2024. \n### Goal 4 - Conduct infrastructure review\nDescription: Include VmWare, storage/backup, and DNS\nManager Rating:\t 3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments: \tWe are shrinking our VMware footprint as advised by USG in advance of expected exponential price increases due to acquisition by Broadcom. Storage refresh recommendations were planned. DNS transitioned to new hardware. \n### Goal 5 - Continue coaching team to adopt high-level goals\nDescription: Providing proactive, preventive, and complete solutions whenever possible. Planning for user experience as part of technology projects/changes. Considering business needs/impact as art of technology projects/changes. Professional communication and responsiveness. Help ensure we close the loop on service requests.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t I think you have invested resources in coaching members of the team. Some team members are performing better than others in terms of responsiveness, planning for the end user experience, and attention to details. Your former team is keeping up with service requests. \n### Goal 6 - Continue developing trusted partnerships inside and outside\nDescription: Being perceived as a trusted partner is essentail to success in security officer role at GGC. Apply concepts from Speed of Trust.\nManager Rating:\t 2 - Partially Successful\t\nManager Comments: \tRelationships inside and outside IT could be improved based on my experiences and feedback I have received. \n\n## Section 2 - Job Duties & Knowledge\n### Job Duties & Knowledge - Function 1\nDescription: Lead and motivate a dynamic, customer-oriented team.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments: \tI think the team has made improvements under your leadership. I would like you to continue developing your performance management skills. Always partner with HR and get their buy in on performance improvement strategies.\n\n### Job Duties & Knowledge - Function 2\nDescription: Define and set priorities, provide support and direction, and hold staff accountable to incident handling and performance expectations.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t Overall, the team is moving in the right direction. \n\n### Job Duties & Knowledge - Function 3\nDescription: Ensure compliance with USG IT handbook and other standards that are in scope for this position.\nManager Rating:\t 2 - Partially Successful\t\nManager Comments: \tThe backup and recovery audit could have been more polished and timely. I received it at the last minute, and I had to address some readability and cosmetic issues. Did you take steps to ensure that this deliverable would meet expectations for quality? You make compliance a priority, and that's a positive. \n\n### Job Duties & Knowledge - Function 4\nDescription: Foster an environment of collaboration and knowledge sharing throughout the campus.\nManager Rating:\t 1 - Not Successful\t\nManager Comments: \tYour performance in 2023 affected your reputation and relationships. Dependability and responsiveness did not meet expectations. I perceive that 2023 was a challenging year for you, and it was a challenging year for others as well. All of us have personal and professional ups and downs. It is important to communicate clearly, and to the extent possible, ask for help and reassign your work to others. Effective collaboration involves reaching consensus on strategy, assignments, and timelines.\n\n### Job Duties & Knowledge - Function 5\nDescription: Train, coach, and mentor team members.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t I perceive that you have invested in coaching, training, and mentoring your direct reports.\n\n### Job Duties & Knowledge - Function 6\nDescription: Establish, document, and implement internal operating procedures.\nManager Rating:\t 3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t You updated the information security program plan and incident response plan. You are working on updating the continuity of operations plan.\n\n### Job Duties & Knowledge - Function 7\nDescription: Develop strategy, standards, and key performance indicators to ensure the highest effectiveness of information systems & security.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t I'm asking all teams to create success metrics as one of their 2024 goals.\n\n### Job Duties & Knowledge - Function 8\nDescription: Serve as the lead campus resource on cybersecurity matters.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments: \tYou successfully serve as the lead resource on cybersecurity matters.\n\n### Job Duties & Knowledge - Function 9\nDescription: Lead all aspects of the information security program including security awareness and incident response.\nManager Rating:\t 2 - Partially Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t You are capable of successfully leading the information security program including cybersecurity awareness and incident response. You led the spring 2024 cybersecurity awareness training campaign successfully, and we had a great response rate.  We had a poor response rate in Spring 2023; Amit and I brought the campaign to a successful finish in Fall 2023. You updated the information security program plan and incident response plan and will convene the CSIRT in 2024.\n\n## Section 3 - Performance Factors\n### Performance Factor 1 - Communication\nDescription: The extent to which employee is proficient and professional in oral and written communication. This includes listening, understanding, remembering, and following oral or written instructions; asking for clarification when necessary and providing information to others in a clear, complete and concise manner.\nManager Rating:\t 2 - Emerging\t\nManager Comments: \tEmotions seem to affect the effectiveness of your communications. It is important to read the room and understand how your communications are being perceived. I will work with you on professional development in 2024. \n\n### Performance Factor 2 - Customer Service\nDescription: The extent to which the employee provides a customer friendly environment and superior service to our clients, patients, coworkers, supervisors, subordinates, faculty and students. The employee resolves customer needs with confirmed satisfaction, responsiveness, and outcomes.\nManager Rating: \t2 - Emerging\t\nManager Comments:\t I would like you give equal time to planning for tech and planning for end user experiences. I can think of occasions when you wanted to schedule a technical change, but had not planned for communications. When possible, technical changes should be tested to understand dependencies, etc. The campus loses trust in us when they experience unscheduled service outages or degradations. We have implemented a 2-week window to plan communications associated with changes.\n\n### Performance Factor 3 - Organizational Development\nDescription: Delegates and directs effectively; shows respect, confidence and trust in others; sets realistic goals and performance objectives; Builds department and personnel capacity through succession planning.\nManager Rating:\t 3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments: \tIt's important to set realistic goals, monitor progress, and course correct as needed. Some members of your former team struggle with \"essential skills\" such as attention to detail and responsiveness. \n\n### Performance Factor 4 - Fiscal/Budget Management\nDescription: The effectiveness with which the individual uses and allocates financial resources and keeps expenditures within approved budget.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t\n\n### Performance Factor 5 - Initiative\nDescription: The extent to which employee is a self-starter, shares new ideas for doing things, and is willing to assume additional duties when necessary. Displays positive attitude and willingness to improve both personally and professionally in a constantly changing environment.\nManager Rating: \t2 - Emerging\t\nManager Comments:\t I think you are a self-starter, and you are willing to share new ideas for doing things. I would rate willingness to assume additional duties, positive attitude, and willingness to improve personally and professionally as mixed.\n\n### Performance Factor 6 - Innovation\nDescription: The extent to which the employee is receptive to new ideas and has the ability to adjust to change with minimum disruption to productivity. Contributes useful ideas for improved performance.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t I think innovation is a potential strength. Be sure to channel to organizational goals, priorities, and needs. Ensure that the timeline will accommodate a novel approach. If we have to stretch just to reach the finish line, it isn't the right time to increase complexity.\n\n### Performance Factor 7 - Job Knowledge\nDescription: The extent to which employee understands their job duties and responsibilities and applies the practical and technical knowledge and skills required for the position.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t\n\n### Performance Factor 8 - Strategic Planning\nDescription: The effectiveness to which the leader sets priorities, secures and utilizes resources, strengthens operations, ensures that employees and other stakeholders are working toward common goals, establishes agreement around intended outcomes/results, and assesses and adjusts the unit's directives based on the needs of the University.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t\n\n### Performance Factor 9 - Adherence to University Policies\nDescription: The extent to which the employee follows system, college/university and department-specific policies and procedures (dress guidelines, professionalism, administrative policies & procedures).\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t\n\n### Performance Factor 10 - Quality of Work\nDescription: The extent to which employee's work is consistently accurate, thorough, and is accomplished in a professional manner. Employee works efficiently and productively while effectively managing resources (labor, time, materials, etc).\nManager Rating: \t2 - Emerging\t\nManager Comments: \tIn multiple occasions in 2023, your performance and deliverables did not meet expectations or needs. The comprehensive policy review is one example. We received clear guidance on the process and the tight timeline required for SACS. Rather than following instructions, you chose to undertake an effort to replace all information security policies. You produced deliverables that may have value in some context, but did not meet expectations for this assignment. Because your deliverables did not meet expectations, I could not send them to Cabinet for review and approval. You did not contribute any revised or new policies to the APM during this review period even though multiple policies had been assigned to you. I was forced to write a new AUP and risk assessment policy at the last minute. This experience has affected my ability to depend on you, and it has reduced trust. In the future, I would like you to find a way make progress/improvements and meet expectations for your assignments. Additionally, I would like you to improve dependability and work on rebuilding trust with me and your teammates.\n\n### Performance Factor 11 - Interpersonal Relationships\nDescription: The extent to which employee cooperates, works and communicates with internal and external customers such as clients, patients, coworkers, supervisors, subordinates, faculty, and students. The employee has the ability and willingness to work effectively within a team and support others as well as accept support and feedback when needed to accomplish task or mission.\nManager Rating: \t2 - Emerging\t\nManager Comments: \tDependability and quality of work in 2023 strained our relationship and other professional relationships.\n\n### Performance Factor 12 - Reliability/Attendance\nDescription: The extent to which an employee can be relied upon regarding task completion and follow-up. The employee meets deadlines with accuracy, work quality and customer satisfaction. Employee has an acceptable overall punctuality and attendance record.\nManager Rating: \t2 - Emerging\t\nManager Comments:\t In 2023, there were times you were difficult to reach or responses were delayed. Please follow responsiveness guidelines that I shared in BLT. \n\n### Performance Factor 13 - Critical Thinking\nDescription: The extent to which the employee demonstrates proper judgment in decision-making and displays effective problem-solving skills.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t\n\n## Section 4 - Values\n\n### Value 1 -  Accountability\nDescription: We firmly believe that education in the form of scholarship, research, teaching, service, and developing others is a public trust. We will live up to this trust through safeguarding our resources and being good stewards of the human, intellectual, physical, and fiscal resources given to our care.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t I perceive that you support the mission of GGC and that you are conscientious about stewardship of resources. \n\n### Value 2 -  Excellence\nDescription: We will perform our duties to foster a culture of excellence and high quality in everything we do.\nManager Rating: \t2 - Emerging\t\nManager Comments:\t I would like to see more examples of high-quality deliverables from you. A number of deliverables did not meet expectations for quality such as the comprehensive policy review and the data backup and recovery report. When you delegate tasks to your direct report(s), you retain responsibility for the quality of the deliverable.\n\n### Value 3 -  Integrity\nDescription: We will be honest, fair, impartial, and unbiased in our dealings both with and on behalf of the USG.\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments:\t\n\n### Value 4 - Respect\nDescription: We recognize the inherent dignity and rights of every person, and we will do our utmost to fulfill our resulting responsibility to treat each person with fairness, compassion, and decency.\t\nManager Rating: \t2 - Emerging\t\nManager Comments:\t I would like you to recognize the affect your performance and behavior have on others. I would like you to consistently demonstrate consideration for me and others by communicating effectively, following through on your commitments, producing deliverables that meet expectations, and meeting deadlines.\n\n## Section 5 - Overall Summary\nManager Rating: \t3 - Successful\t\nManager Comments: \tCharles - 2023 was a challenging year. I hope it was an outlier in terms of your performance. We refocused your role on information security in mid-2024, and this gives you an opportunity to start fresh. I hope you will take advantage of it. I think you have the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experience to be an asset to GGC.\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2024 Performance Management - Charles","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Performance Management/Charles H. Leggett/2024/2024 Performance Management - Charles.md","lastModified":"2024-09-16T22:43:44.502Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2024 Performance Management - Charles\n## Section 1 - Goals\n### Goal 1 - Collaborate to complete approved IAM priorities (including SSPR and MFA)\n#### Description\n- Participate in planning for technical and end user changes\n- Prioritize user experience and user satisfaction\n#### Updates\n### Goal 2 - Lead continuous improvement of the cybersecurity program\n#### Description\n- Annually update cybersecurity program plan, incident response plan, and COOP for IT.\n- Lead cybersecurity training and awareness including twice annual cybersecurity awareness training campaigns achieving desired completion rate of 95% or higher. Identify new channels for cybersecurity awareness such as campus presentations, digital signs, etc.\n- Convene and train CSIRT.\n- Update/create APM policies upon request.\n#### Updates\n### Goal 3 - Produce deliverables for USG compliance/cybersecurity\n#### Description\nDescription: \nDescription : PCI DSS Audit\n- collaborate to convene working group (after I talk to Frank)\n- help close audit findings\n- Cybersecurity Shared Services (emerging)\n#### Updates\n### Goal 4 - Collaborate to help reinvigorate Data Governance\n#### Description\nDescription :\n- Propose action plan for next 6 months\n- Reconvene steering committee to launch vetted plan\n#### Updates\n## Section 2 - Job Duties & Knowledge\n### Job Duties & Knowledge 1\n#### Description\n- Develop, implement, and monitor a comprehensive information security and IT risk management program that ensures the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of GGC data and infrastructure.\n#### Updates\n### Job Duties & Knowledge 2\n#### Description\n- Provide guidance and counsel on information security to college leaders and other stakeholders and partner with campus colleagues to develop a strategic approach to information security that balances business needs with managing risk.\n#### Updates\n### Job Duties & Knowledge 3\n#### Description\n- Develop and lead education, training, and awareness programs for all college constituents on institutional policy, guidelines, federal and state laws and regulations, and best practices in information security.\n#### Updates\n### Job Duties & Knowledge 4\n#### Description\n- Lead the development, and implementation of the college's security and governance policies and procedures in consultation with IT leadership, technology professionals, and other stakeholders.\n#### Updates\n### Job Duties & Knowledge 5\n#### Description\n- Lead security information and event management, security operations, and other related functions.\n#### Updates\n### Job Duties & Knowledge 6\n#### Description\n- Collaborate with the ITS, audit, public safety, and academic and business units to comply with USG security policies, regulations, and college standards; collaborate with Legal Affairs and Purchasing to embed risk assessment and data security in supplier agreements and renewals.\n#### Updates\n### Job Duties & Knowledge 7\n#### Description\n- Establish and implement a process for incident management to proactively identify threats; respond, contain, and communicate suspected or confirmed incidents, and employ a 24/7/364 on-call schedule as needed. Lead and coordinate institutional responses to security incidents, provide timely reports during the incident, and propose cost-effective solutions to prevent or mitigate future incidents.\n#### Updates\n### Job Duties & Knowledge 8\n#### Description\n- Collaborate with colleagues inside and outside IT to embed cybersecurity best practices in policies and implement technical controls for endpoints.\n#### Updates\n### Job Duties & Knowledge 9\n#### Description\n- Use standard tools and processes to lead projects to successful completion through effective planning for user experiences, change management, communication, and documentation.\n#### Updates\n## Section 3 - Performance Factors\n### Performance Factor 1 - Communication\n#### Description\n The extent to which employee is proficient and professional in oral and written communication. This includes listening, understanding, remembering, and following oral or written instructions; asking for clarification when necessary and providing information to others in a clear, complete and concise manner.\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 2 - Customer Service\n#### Description\nThe extent to which the employee provides a customer friendly environment and superior service to our clients, patients, coworkers, supervisors, subordinates, faculty and students. The employee resolves customer needs with confirmed satisfaction, responsiveness, and outcomes.\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 3 - Organizational Development\n#### Description\nDelegates and directs effectively; shows respect, confidence and trust in others; sets realistic goals and performance objectives; Builds department and personnel capacity through succession planning.\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 4 - Fiscal/Budget Management\n#### Description\nThe effectiveness with which the individual uses and allocates financial resources and keeps expenditures within approved budget.\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 5 - Initiative\n#### Description\nThe extent to which employee is a self-starter, shares new ideas for doing things, and is willing to assume additional duties when necessary. Displays positive attitude and willingness to improve both personally and professionally in a constantly changing environment.\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 6 - Innovation\n#### Description\nThe extent to which the employee is receptive to new ideas and has the ability to adjust to change with minimum disruption to productivity. Contributes useful ideas for improved performance.\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 7 - Job Knowledge\n#### Description\nThe extent to which employee understands their job duties and responsibilities and applies the practical and technical knowledge and skills required for the position.\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 8 - Strategic Planning\n#### Description\nThe effectiveness to which the leader sets priorities, secures and utilizes resources, strengthens operations, ensures that employees and other stakeholders are working toward common goals, establishes agreement around intended outcomes/results, and assesses and adjusts the unit's directives based on the needs of the University.\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 9 - Adherence to University Policies\n#### Description\n The extent to which the employee follows system, college/university and department-specific policies and procedures (dress guidelines, professionalism, administrative policies & procedures).\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 10 - Quality of Work\n#### Description\n The extent to which employee's work is consistently accurate, thorough, and is accomplished in a professional manner. Employee works efficiently and productively while effectively managing resources (labor, time, materials, etc).\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 11 - Interpersonal Relationships\n#### Description\nThe extent to which employee cooperates, works and communicates with internal and external customers such as clients, patients, coworkers, supervisors, subordinates, faculty, and students. The employee has the ability and willingness to work effectively within a team and support others as well as accept support and feedback when needed to accomplish task or mission.\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 12 - Reliability/Attendance\n#### Description\n The extent to which an employee can be relied upon regarding task completion and follow-up. The employee meets deadlines with accuracy, work quality and customer satisfaction. Employee has an acceptable overall punctuality and attendance record.\n#### Updates\n### Performance Factor 13 - Critical Thinking\n#### Description\nThe extent to which the employee demonstrates proper judgment in decision-making and displays effective problem-solving skills.\n#### Updates\n## Section 4 - Values\n### Value 1 - Accountability\n#### Description\nWe firmly believe that education in the form of scholarship, research, teaching, service, and developing others is a public trust. We will live up to this trust through safeguarding our resources and being good stewards of the human, intellectual, physical, and fiscal resources given to our care.\n#### Updates\n### Value 2 - Excellence\n#### Description\nWe will perform our duties to foster a culture of excellence and high quality in everything we do.\n#### Updates\n### Value 3 - Integrity\n#### Description\nWe will be honest, fair, impartial, and unbiased in our dealings both with and on behalf of the USG.\n#### Updates\n### Value 4 - Respect\n#### Description\nWe recognize the inherent dignity and rights of every person, and we will do our utmost to fulfill our resulting responsibility to treat each person with fairness, compassion, and decency.\n#### Updates\n## Section 5 - Overall Summary\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2024 GGC Performance Goals - Information Security","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/2024 GGC Performance Goals - Information Security.md","lastModified":"2024-09-16T22:08:40.621Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2024 GGC Performance Goals - Information Security\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2024 Performance Evaluation Goals - Systems Administrator","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Performance Management/_Forms & Templates/2024/2024 Performance Evaluation Goals - Systems Administrator.md","lastModified":"2024-09-16T22:05:50.714Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2024 Performance Evaluation Goals - Systems Administrator\n## Goal 1: Mastery of System Technologies and Continuous Learning\nObjective: Demonstrate a commitment to staying abreast of the latest advancements in system technologies. Acquire comprehensive knowledge of relevant software, hardware, and security protocols. Aim to become an expert in the field, fostering a deep understanding of system architecture and its evolving landscape.\n## Goal 2: Streamlined System Analysis and Troubleshooting\nObjective: Enhance the ability to analyze complex system issues efficiently. Develop skills to troubleshoot and diagnose problems swiftly, minimizing downtime. Implement proactive measures to identify potential issues before they escalate, ensuring the seamless operation of critical systems.\n## Goal 3: Collaborative Knowledge Sharing and Documentation\nObjective: Foster a collaborative knowledge-sharing environment within the IT team. Actively engage in sharing insights, best practices, and solutions to common issues. Prioritize the creation and maintenance of comprehensive documentation to facilitate efficient troubleshooting and empower team members with valuable insights.\n## Goal 4: Innovative Solutions for System Optimization\nObjective: Cultivate a mindset of innovation in addressing system challenges. Actively seek opportunities to propose and implement innovative solutions that enhance system performance, security, and scalability. Explore new technologies and methodologies to optimize systems and contribute to the organization's technological advancement.\n## Goal 5: Efficient Time and Project Management\nObjective: Enhance efficiency through proficient time and project management. Prioritize system maintenance, upgrades, and projects effectively, ensuring minimal disruptions to daily operations. Implement strategies to manage competing priorities and deliver high-quality system administration within established timelines.\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2024 Performance Evaluation Goals - Security Analyst","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Performance Management/_Forms & Templates/2024/2024 Performance Evaluation Goals - Security Analyst.md","lastModified":"2024-09-16T22:05:13.941Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2024 Performance Evaluation Goals - Security Analyst\n## Goal 1: Fundamental Understanding and Continuous Learning\nObjective: Demonstrate a commitment to building a strong foundation in information security. Stay updated on the latest threats, vulnerabilities, and security technologies. Aim to become proficient in key security concepts, methodologies, and industry best practices.\n## Goal 2: Thorough Security Incident Analysis and Response\nObjective: Enhance the ability to analyze and respond to security incidents effectively. Develop skills in identifying, analyzing, and mitigating security threats. Strive to reduce incident response times, ensuring a swift and well-coordinated resolution to maintain the security posture of the organization.\n## Goal 3: Collaborative Knowledge Sharing and Documentation in Security Practices\nObjective: Foster a collaborative environment within the security team. Actively engage in knowledge sharing, contributing insights, and participating in discussions on emerging threats. Prioritize the creation and upkeep of documentation to support incident response procedures and enhance team-wide understanding of security protocols.\n## Goal 4: Innovative Approaches to Enhance Security Measures\nObjective: Cultivate a mindset of innovation in addressing security challenges. Actively seek opportunities to propose and implement innovative solutions that strengthen the organization's security posture. Explore emerging technologies and methodologies to proactively address evolving threats and vulnerabilities.\n## Goal 5: Efficient Time and Project Management\nObjective: Improve efficiency through effective time and project management. Prioritize security tasks and projects, ensuring timely completion of assignments. Implement strategies to manage competing priorities, contributing to the overall effectiveness of security operations and the protection of sensitive information.\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Recommendation Letters","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Performance Management/Recommendation Letters/Recommendation Letters.md","lastModified":"2024-09-16T22:01:01.286Z","tags":[],"content":"# Recommendation L