 Information Policy & Management.md","lastModified":"2024-09-16T19:53:23.938Z","tags":[],"content":"---\n{}\n---\n\n# 63.09 - OMSCY - PUBP 6501 - Information Policy & Management\n\n[[63.09 - PUBP 6501 - Information Policy & Management.canvas]]\n\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"63.07 - OMSCY - CS 6250 - Computer Networks","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/OMSCY/63.07 - OMSCY - CS 6250 - Computer Networks/63.07 - OMSCY - CS 6250 - Computer Networks.md","lastModified":"2024-09-16T19:53:23.926Z","tags":["#heading"],"content":"---\n{}\n---\n\nTitle:: '63.07 - CS 6250 - Computer Networks'\nSchool:: [[Georgia Institute of Technology (GaTech)]]\nCourseNumber:: 'CS 6250'\nCourseTitle:: 'Computer Networks'\nArea:: ''\nProgram:: [[OMSCY -]]\nSemester:: [[2023-01 - 2023 Spring Semester]]\nProfessor:: [[Maria Conte]]\nStatus:: \nPriority:: \nLesson:: [[Lesson 1 - Introduction, Internet History, and Architecture]]\nLesson:: [[Lesson 2 - Transport and Application Layers]]\nLesson:: [[60 - Education/63 - GaTech OMS Cybersecurity/63.07 - CS 6250 - Computer Networks/Lessons/Lesson 3 - Intradomain Routing/Lesson 3 - Intradomain Routing]]\nLesson:: [[60 - Education/63 - GaTech OMS Cybersecurity/63.07 - CS 6250 - Computer Networks/Lessons/Lesson 4 - AS Relationships and Interdomain Routing/Lesson 4 - AS Relationships and Interdomain Routing]]\nLesson:: [[Lesson 5 - Router Design and Algorithms - Part 1]]\nLesson:: [[Lesson 6 - Router Design and Algorithms - Part 2]]\nLesson:: [[Lesson 7 - SDN Part 1]]\nLesson:: [[Lesson 8 - SDN Part 2]]\nLesson:: [[Lesson 9 - Internet Security]]\nLesson:: [[Lesson 10 - Internet Surveillance and Censorship]]\nLesson:: [[Lesson 11 - Applications Part 1 - Video]]\nLesson:: [[Lesson 12 - Applications Part 2 - CDNs]]\nLesson:: [[Lesson 13 - Future of the Internet (Optional)]]\nProject:: [[Project 1 - Optional warmup - Simulating Networks]]\nProject:: [[Project 2 - Spanning Tree Protocol for Network Switches]]\nProject:: [[Project 3 - Distance Vector Routing]]\nProject:: [[Project 4 - SDN Firewall]]\nProject:: [[Project 5 - BGG Hijacking]]\nProject:: [[Project 6 - BGP Measurements]]\nProject:: [[Project 7 - Internet-Wide Events Extra Credit]]\n\n# 63.07 - OMSCY - CS 6250 - Computer Networks\n## Links\n- [Canvas LMS](https://gatech.instructure.com/courses/296784)\n- [EdStem](https://edstem.org/us/courses/30804/discussion/)\n- [An Introduction to Computer Networks](http://intronetworks.cs.luc.edu/current/html/)\n- [Basic Network Concepts - Student Created Collab - Google Doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nFqMadJnXguMvaIONHAsz-hS4VR1LEvjpefBC9tX-FI/edit#heading=h.bdwzipra5gj7)\n- [CS 8803 - Cyber-Physical Systems Security (intro course)](https://www.udacity.com/course/cyber-physical-systems-security--ud279)\n\n## People\nProfessor:: [[Maria Conte]]\n\n## Communication\n[Canvas Announcements](https://gatech.instructure.com/courses/296784/announcements)\n[Edstem Discussion](https://edstem.org/us/courses/30804/discussion/)\n\n## Structure\n### Syllabus\n![[CS6250 Computer Networks Syllabus Spring 2023.pdf]]\n\n#### Syllabus Notes\n1. There is no required textbook for this class\n2. Each Lesson has a quiz.\n3. There are X Assignments\n\t1. \n4. There are 2 closed book exams. The exams will be based on the lectures and readings provided, rather than material outside of these.\n\t1. [[Exam 1]] is due 2023-03-05\n\t2. [[Exam 2]] is due 2023-04-30\n5. All quizzes, exams, and projects are due at 23:59:59 [[Anywhere on Earth Time Zone (AOE)]], unless otherwise noted.\n\n### Course Learning Outcomes\nBy the end of the course, you will be able to:\n- Understand, from an evolution perspective, why the Internet architecture has its current form\n- Learn how basic algorithms and protocols work, such as link-state routing, distance vector routing\n- Understand problems related to convergence, instability, configuration verification\n- Understand router design and functionalities such as switching, queueing, packet classification\n- Learn about Software Defined Networking technologies and applications\n- Apply Internet measurements and analytics to achieve multiple tasks\n- Evaluate issues related to Internet security, surveillance, and censorship\n- Understand how modern Applications work: voice and video applications\n\n## Books\n### Required\nNone\n\n### Recommended\n[[Computer Networking - A Top-Down Approach by Kurose & Ross]]\n- 7th edition, ISBN-10: 9780133594140 ISBN- 13: 978-0133594140\n- (you might use the 6th but it doesn’t cover SDN as well)\n\n## Content\n### Study Questions\n![[CS6250 Study Questions.pdf]]\n\n### Lessons\n- [[Lesson 1 - Introduction, Internet History, and Architecture]] ✅ 2023-01-21\n- [[Lesson 2 - Transport and Application Layers]]\n- [[60 - Education/63 - GaTech OMS Cybersecurity/63.07 - CS 6250 - Computer Networks/Lessons/Lesson 3 - Intradomain Routing/Lesson 3 - Intradomain Routing]]\n- [[60 - Education/63 - GaTech OMS Cybersecurity/63.07 - CS 6250 - Computer Networks/Lessons/Lesson 4 - AS Relationships and Interdomain Routing/Lesson 4 - AS Relationships and Interdomain Routing]]\n- [[Lesson 5 - Router Design and Algorithms - Part 1]]\n- [[Lesson 6 - Router Design and Algorithms - Part 2]]\n- [[Lesson 7 - SDN Part 1]]\n- [[Lesson 8 - SDN Part 2]]\n- [[Lesson 9 - Internet Security]]\n- [[Lesson 10 - Internet Surveillance and Censorship]]\n- [[Lesson 11 - Applications Part 1 - Video]]\n- [[Lesson 12 - Applications Part 2 - CDNs]]\n- [[Lesson 13 - Future of the Internet (Optional)]]\n\n### Assignments\n- [Step 8: Syllabus Quiz](https://gatech.instructure.com/courses/296784/assignments/1225312/submissions/43935) ✅ 2023-01-19\n- [Lesson 1 Weekly Quiz: Introduction, History, and Internet Architecture](https://gatech.instructure.com/courses/296784/assignments/1225342/submissions/43935) ✅ 2023-01-21\n- [Lesson 2 Weekly Quiz: Transport and Applications Layers](https://gatech.instructure.com/courses/296784/assignments/1225344/submissions/43935)\n- 