,"lastModified":"2024-09-14T11:30:48.899Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2020 Trek Fuel EX 7\n## Purchased\n- [[2024-07-22 - Monday]]\n## Registration\n\n## Initial Specs\n[2020 Trek Fuel EX 7 Bike - Reviews, Comparisons, Specs - Bikes - Vital MTB](https://www.vitalmtb.com/product/guide/Bikes,3/Trek/Fuel-EX-7,27145)\n\nRear Shock\n\nFOX Performance Float EVOL, RE:aktiv with Thru Shaft 3-position damper, tuned by Trek Suspension Lab\n\nRear Travel\n\n130mm\n\nFork\n\nRockShox 35 Gold, DebonAir spring, Motion Control damper, tapered steerer, 44mm offset, Boost110, 15mm Maxle Stealth\n\nFork Travel\n\n140mm\n## Notes\n- [[2024-08 - August|2024-08]] & [[2024-09 - September|2024-09]]\n\t- Installed new front end to match [[Rider Area Distance (RAD)]]:\n\t\t- Cost: ~$235\n\t\t- Parts:\n\t\t\t- [[SQLab 3OX 780mm 16° Handlebar]] - $145\n\t\t\t- ~~[[SQLab 80X 35mm Stem]]~~ lost in shipping\n\t\t\t- [[Spank Spoon 33mm Stem]] - $60\n\t\t\t- [[Trek Knock Block Locking Spacer]] (to allow for non-[[Trek]]/[[Bontrager]] stem]] -$20\n\t\t\t- Spacers - $10\n\t\t- Issues:\n\t\t\t- Proprietary [[Trek Knock Block]]\n\t\t\t- Stem lost in shipping\n\t\t\t- Stripped [[dropper post lever]] by over tightening ","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Bike Fit","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Bike Fit.md","lastModified":"2024-09-14T10:27:49.872Z","tags":[],"content":"# Bike Fit\nfor [[2020 Trek Fuel EX 7]]\nand [[DJ Frankenbike]]\n\n5’11” = 180.34 cm\n\n## [[Rider Area Distance (RAD)]]\n#### by formula\nRAD- = 180.34 * 4.45 = 802.51mm\nRAD = 180.34 * 4.5 = 811.53mm\nRAD+ = 180.34 * 4.55 = 820.55mm\n\n#### by measurement (using formula ratio)\n“knuckle height” = 31”\nRAD- = 778.66mm\nRAD = 31” =  787.4mm\nRAD+ = 796.15mm\n\n## Bar Width\n180.34 * 4.40 = 793.50mm (maximum)\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Rider Area Distance (RAD)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Ideas/Rider Area Distance (RAD).md","lastModified":"2024-09-14T10:11:10.127Z","tags":["#mt