yees]]\n[[83.01.08 - Staff Augmentation]]\n## Positions\n[[Management - Hire Director of IT Service Management & Support]]\n[[Management - Hire IT Endpoint Administrator - 238805]]\n[[Management - Hire Network Administrator III]]\n[[Management - Hire Systems Administrator III - 10004959 (Stacy's Backfill)]]\n[[Management - Hire Information Security Professional III]]\n[[Management - Hire Systems Administrator II Job Posting]]\n[[Management - Hire Director of Networking & Telecommunications]]\n[[80 - GGC/83 - Management/83.01 - Hiring/83.01.10 - Hire Systems Administrator III - 10004959 (Jordan's Backfill)/Project Template]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Process Management","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Process Management/Process Management.md","lastModified":"2024-09-07T10:29:22.508Z","tags":[],"content":"# Process Management\n \n\n \n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Project Management","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Project Management/Project Management.md","lastModified":"2024-09-07T10:29:06.111Z","tags":[],"content":"# Project Management\n... from [[Kevin McCuen]]\n\n## **Status Types & Definitions:**\n-   **Not Started** - No attention is being given to the specific task\n-   **Planning** - There are conversations and/or information gathering activities starting to happen\n-   **Agenda Item** – Indicates that particular task needs to be discussed specifically at the next meeting\n-   I**n Progress** – There is active work being done on a task or action item\n-   **Waiting For** – This is used when you’ve come to a point where no further progress can be made because you’re waiting for someone or something else to complete.\n\t-   Please indicate in the chat feed specifics when selecting this option.\n-   **Cancelled** – The task is no longer needed or relevant to the project.\n-   **Complete** – All work associated with the task is done, documentation is complete, and archived\n-   **Closed** – (Reserved for the PM) When all tasks, action items, decisions, risks, and issues have been completed.\n\t-   This will trigger a Project Close-out and Lessons Learned meeting.\n\n## **Project Documentation**\n- ###  **Decisions Log**\n\t-   This is for items that are questions or thoughts about the project that end with a (?) and should be discussed as the project progresses.\n\t-   These can be identified and documented at any time throughout the project\n\n- ###  **Issues Log**\n\t-   This is for items that need to be considered when planning, working, and communicating the project outside of the project team.\n\t-   These items are going to happen no matter what you do, they just have to be managed.\n\n- ###  **Risks**\n\t-   This is for items that can negatively or positively impact the deliverable (outcome) of the project itself.\n\t-   If it has the potential to negatively impact the project we want to do one of the following:\n\t\t-   Avoid (take steps to keep from affecting the project)\n\t\t-   Mitigate (take steps to lessen the impact of the risk)\n\t\t-   Transfer (take steps to move the risk off the project team)\n\t\t\t-   Ex: USG ITS manages Banner to they assume the risk versus GGC managing their own Banner instance\n\t\t-   Accept (take steps to incorporate the risk within the project)\n\t-   If it has the potential to positively impact the project we want to do one of the following:\n\t\t-   Exploit (make sure this happens)\n\t\t-   Share (help others benefit)\n\t\t-   Enhance (take steps to amplify the result)\n\t\t-   Accept (accept it as it is)\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Purchasing","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Purchasing/Purchasing.md","lastModified":"2024-09-07T10:28:32.157Z","tags":[],"content":"# Purchasing\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Time Management","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Time Management/Time Management.md","lastModified":"2024-09-07T10:27:50.222Z","t