3aryEhiH&at=9\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"GRC - 2019 & 2020 USG GLBA Audits","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/GRC/Audits/GRC - 2019 & 2020 USG GLBA Audits/GRC - 2019 & 2020 USG GLBA Audits.md","lastModified":"2024-09-07T10:21:58.875Z","tags":[],"content":"# GRC - 2019 & 2020 USG GLBA Audits\n \n\n \n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Kaizen - 2023 MOR Coaching Engagement","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Projects/Kaizen - 2023 MOR Coaching Engagement/Kaizen - 2023 MOR Coaching Engagement.md","lastModified":"2024-09-07T10:17:36.425Z","tags":["#2","#3"],"content":"---\nStatus: In Progress\nClosed: false\nArea: Kaizen\nPriority: B\n---\n\n# Kaizen - 2023 MOR Coaching Engagement\nwith [[Sean MacDonald]]\n\n\"Vision without action is a daydream, Action without vision is a nightmare.\"\n\n## [[2023-06-06 - Tuesday]] - Objectives/goals for you in this coaching engagement\n\n1. Taking care of yourself. Vacation, the gym, playing Zelda, etc. are all part of your self-care focus. Be intentional about making the habits that matter here stick.\n2. Declare your desired future. My analogy is you are aimlessly walking through the mud. Declare where you are headed, see the mud getting less deep over time. Pick a destination, and yes, set a date, we talked through the pros and cons.\n3. Draft the plan. Depending on which destination you choose, map the plan that will get you there.\n4. From #2 and #3, start to bring in the reflection on identity and habit. What actions and habits will support this desired direction you are headed. Including the practices that will serve you as you try to ease slowly away from some of things on the other side of this declared path.\n\n## [[2023-08-22 - Tuesday]] Coaching Notes\n### Identity\n- You get to decide.\n- What are you okay with?\n- How do you want to live, work?\n- Are you the kind of guy that is okay with an \"uncomfortable nitch\"?\n- Are you the kind of guy that can\n\t- step out of his comfort zone,\n\t- change,\n\t- reach for something that leverages what you bring,\n\t- gives you energy, and\n\t- allows you to do your best work? \n### Options\n\nSounded like of the four options on the table in our last call, some were becoming less and less likely. These were:\n1. do what you are doing and get what you've been getting\n2. do what you are trying to do in a different way\n3. work the plan you believe will allow for success, or\n4. leave\n\n### Timeline\n\n- We are hopeful for 3 above. And we are afraid that, in a blink of an eye, it could be a year from now and you are still at 1.\n\nThus, we discussed a timeline of year end, but with milestones along the way. Again, you get to decide.\n\n### Networking\n\n- We talked about the multiple benefits to networking right now.\n\n- Leading into the Sept conference, leveraging the conference, and post-conference are all great times/reasons to lean into this.\n\n### Others\n\n- We also talked about reflecting on and assessing how you might evolve the relationship with your manager. Who we work for matters.\n\n- We talked about team, and team development, pulling back up the 9-box model to help you think about meeting each team member where they are.\n\n- Strategic thinking, looking further out, setting up the org for success. Doing more of that and less time putting out fires and focusing on the immedaite.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"aimlessly walking through the mud","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Ideas/aimlessly walking through the mud.md","lastModified":"2024-09-07T10:17:36.417Z","tags":[],"content":"# aimlessly walking through the mud\n\n[[Sean McDonald]]’s analogy for getting unstuck shared during our [[Kaizen - 2023 MOR Coaching Engagement]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Management - Hire IT Endpoint Administrator - 238805","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Projects/Management - Hire IT Endpoint Administrator - 238805/Management - Hire IT Endpoint Administrator - 238805.