,{"title":"2024-07-13 - Saturday","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Journal/2024/2024-07 - July/2024-07-13 - Saturday.md","lastModified":"2024-07-24T16:44:02.579Z","tags":["#Autoplay","#Good","#insight"],"content":"---\nperiodicNotes: daily\naliases:\n  - 2024-07-13\ndate: 2024-07-13\nprevious: \"[[2024-07-12 - Friday]]\"\nday: \"[[2024-07-13 - Saturday]]\"\nnext: \"[[2024-07-14 - Sunday]]\"\nweek: \"[[2024-W28]]\"\ntags: \nhoursSlept: 7\nhoursExercised: 2\nhoursDeepWork: 0\nhoursMeetings: 0\nhoursScreenTime: 6.25\nsystolic: 119\ndiastolic: 78\nreflection: false\nmigration: false\nplanning: false\ntriage: false\ntasksCoffee: false\ntasksMorning: false\ntasksAfternoon: false\ntasksEvening: false\nshutdown: false\nwindDown: false\ndaily: false\ntoday: false\nmetrics: true\nhoursCoffeeTime: 2.5\n---\n# 2024-07-13 - Saturday\n[[2024-07-12 - Friday|Previous Day]] | [[2024-W28|This Week]] | [[2024-07-14 - Sunday|Next Day]]\n```meta-bind-embed\n[[Daily Header]]\n```\n## Journal\n### What are your favorite ways to relax and de-stress?\n\nI really enjoy the outdoors. The more time that I spend in the woods, the better I feel.\n\nI also enjoy projects around the house, but only (mostly?) when I don’t have to feel “productive” to get them done.\n\nI do better with IRL and “for people” projects than I do with on-screen intangible technology things. #insight\n\n### How can you find and make more time for these activities?\n\nI need to hike more. Much more. I don’t need to think of it as exercise. The importance is just getting out there, so hiking is not the important part. Being and moving (or just sitting) under the trees is the important part.\n\nMaybe I could make a plan to hike at Little Mulberry before scouts and/or on Saturdays. Sundays are no good because you do yardwork and housework on Sundays. Sundays in the off-season of grass mowing would be okay because you won’t be as tired.\n\nI need to figure out how to make home projects more fun and include the family. Reframing them with the “why” would be good. Example: I don’t care about [[Maintenance - Fix Traeger Ignite Button]], I care about cooking meat. #insight \n\nErin’s planting project does sound like fun. Serve her by helping. What does she need?\n\n### How do you know when you need to prioritize self-care.\n\nWhen I don’t take care of myself, I don’t sleep and I get cranky with my friends, family, and co-workers.\n\n### What hobbies or interests stimulate your mind and bring you joy?\n\nAs I wrote earlier, I need to get out and enjoy nature as well as reframe my projects to make them about serving people, finding the fun, and focusing on the “why”.\n\n### Are you happy with your sleep habits? Do you prioritize your sleep every night?\n\nNo. I need to de-stress and get off my screen so that I can adjust to falling asleep naturally.\n\n### What physical activities make you feel energized and happy?\n\n [[Hiking|Hiking]].\n \n [[Pickleball]] with Erin may be fun. She knows the game. Let her lead.\n\n### How does your diet affect your mood and energy levels?\n\nI eat and feel like crap. Switching to a [[Mediterranean Diet]] may help.\n\n## Plan\n1. Yardwork\n2. Pickup Sophia\n3. [[Family - Sluder - Help Move Shed]]\n\n## Bullets\n- 05:30 started using the [[stoic.]] app to do morning reflection while [[Endel#Autoplay]] is playing \n- Helping to plan [[Cousin Camp]]\n- [-] Add an automation to the [[Apple Home#Good Morning Scene]] to play [[Endel]] on the Kitchen [[HomePod]]  [created:: 2024-07-13]  [cancelled:: 2024-07-24]  [completion:: 2024-07-19]\n- Someone tried to assassinate [[Donald J. Trump]]\n\n```meta-bind-embed\n[[Daily Routine]]\n```\n\n> [!example]- Today's Work `INPUT[toggle:today]`\n> ```meta-bind-embed\n> [[Today's Work]]\n> ```\n\n> [!example]+ Accomplishments\n> > [!done]+ Done\n> > ```tasks\n> > done on 2024-07-13\n> > heading does not include Daily\n> > group by filename\n> > ```\n> \n> > [!missing]+ Cancelled\n> > ```tasks\n> > cancelled on 20