"bookmarked":false},{"title":"Help Terry to Rehabilitate from his Stroke","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Projects/Help Terry to Rehabilitate from his Stroke.md","lastModified":"2024-07-10T11:28:10.511Z","tags":[],"content":"---\n{}\n---\n# Help Terry to Rehabilitate from his Stroke\n\n## Care:\n- [[2023-10-19 - Terry's Visit to GHCS to Care for his Stroke]]\n- [[2023-10-26 - Terry's Visit to St. Mary's Hospital Rehab]]\n- [[NEGA Home Healthcare]]\n\nNotes:\n- [[2023-11-15 - Wednesday]] - I spoke with [[Sandy Schneider]] and [[Z Hoxie]] about taking [[FMLA]]\n\t- Z basically said use your leave and work it out with [[Christine Miller Divine]]\n\t\t- Only let him know if larger continuous blocks of time are needed.e\n\n## Resources:\n- [[VA Healthcare]] - [RESCUE Stroke Caregiving](https://www.stroke.cindrr.research.va.gov/en/resources/index.asp)\n- Second Stroke Prevention Flyer: [[image.jpg]]\n- [[VA Caregiver Program]]\n- \n\n[[Terry Sluder]] | [[Justin Leggett]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"81.01 - GGC Charles","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/80 - GGC/81 - GGC Teams/81.01 - GGC Charles/81.01 - GGC Charles.md","lastModified":"2024-07-10T11:03:39.683Z","tags":[],"content":"# 81.01 - GGC Charles\n[[GGC Information Systems]]\n \n\n \n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Stacy Wilbon","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Stacy Wilbon.md","lastModified":"2024-07-10T11:03:39.682Z","tags":[],"content":"# Stacy Wilbon\n[[81.07 - GGC Stacy]]\n[[GGC Information Systems]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Mohammed Issah","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Mohammed Issah.md","lastModified":"2024-07-10T11:03:39.679Z","tags":[],"content":"# Mohammed Issah\n[[81.08 - GGC Mohammed]]\n\n[[GGC Information Systems]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Jordan Smith","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Jordan Smith.md","lastModified":"2024-07-10T11:03:39.677Z","tags":[],"content":"# Jordan Smith\n[[81.09 - GGC Jordan]]\n[[GGC Information Systems]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Jessica Walker","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Jessica Walker.md","lastModified":"2024-07-10T11:03:39.674Z","tags":[],"content":"# Jessica Walker\n[[81.04 - GGC Jessica]]\n\n[[GGC Information Systems]]\n\nJessica’s behavior and accomplishments:  \n  \n\\- She has adapted well to the recent changes in leadership in the IT department. She has quickly embraced the concepts and practices of ITSM that we have introduced. For example, she is a champion of the Change Management process on our team.  \n  \n\\- She works proactively to find opportunities for continual improvement on the team. She has helped to develop new operational procedures. She was the first to embrace the code versioning and password management tools that we have recently implemented.  \n  \n\\- Until very recently, she served every day as the de facto triage person on our Service Incident and Request queue. She helped to team to establish a triage rotation so that the responsibility can be shared among the other team members.  \n  \n\\- She is willing and able to put in the effort required to come up to speed on technologies that are new to the team. She is my go-to sounding board for my own research and ideas.  \n  \n\\- She’s a self-starter and is able to manage her projects and tasks effectively. She seeks clarification and helps to prioritize her work when necessary.\n\n## Obituary\n\nJessica, the only daughter of Travis and Julie Walker, was born on August 28, 1993, in Atlanta, Georgia. She grew up in Marietta, and most recently resided in her own home in Lawrenceville.\n\nJessica idolized her older brother Terry at a young age and loved going to his baseball games.  She was so excited when she was finally old enough to play softball herself, and played until middle school. She then shifted her interest and focus to golf, and she competed at a high level throughout high school.\n\nJessica began high school in East Cobb County and attended Pope High School, and finished at Lambert High School in Suwanee where she was part of the inaugural graduating class. She went on to graduate from Georgia Gwinnett College where she found her professional passion in IT and CyberSecurity. She began her career as a student assistant in the college’s IT department, and was hired on full time as soon as she graduated.\n\nJessica is survived by her parents Travis and Julie; her brother Terry Walker, sister-in-law Amanda Walker, and her niece and nephew Beau and Jemma; and her grandparents Anne Rushworth and Peter Rushworth. She would be mad at us if we didn’t also include her dogs Cagney and Magnum and her cat Lucy here; she loved her animals so much and they were a daily lifeline and support system for her.\n\nJessica had a huge heart, loved deeply, and cared so much for all she met. Below are the words of her best friend Abby that are the best we can imagine to describe who she was.\n\n“A more loyal and hard-loving friend could not be found. Over the past few years, I witnessed Jessica take mental health head-on. She was determined to forge a path of healing. She was learning how to stand up for herself, and I was simply taken with her hard-won confidence. Jessica had a keenly developed sense of what was right, and a passion for the truth. She was principled in ways I could only dream of achieving. Julie and Travis - you raised a smart, righteous woman, with a heart of gold. I know she made you so proud with her loving and generous nature.”\n\nTo celebrate Jessica's remarkable life, funeral services will be held on Wednesday, October 11, 2023, at 12:00 pm in the Peachtree Corners Chapel of Crowell Brothers Funeral Homes & Crematory. Prior to the service, visitation will be held starting at 11:00am, all are welcomed.\n\nIn honoring Jessica's wishes, we kindly request attendees to dress comfortably, coming as they are, to celebrate her life and remember her vibrant spirit. Her family invites everyone to share their cherished memories and stories as they gather to pay their final respects and express their condolences.\n\n## GGC Announcement\n\nSad News: Passing of GGC Staff Jessica Walker\n\nDear GGC Community,\n\nIt is with great sadness that I share the sudden passing of a member of our Georgia Gwinnett College (GGC) family, Jessica Walker, who was a systems administrator II in Information Technology (IT). Jessica passed away Wednesday, Oct. 4.\n\nA resident of Lawrenceville, Georgia, Jessica dedicated her educational and professional career to GGC. She was known to have a passion for IT and cybersecurity. Her GGC colleagues remember her best for demonstrating initiative to learn new technical skills, helping to plan internal IT events, and baking and sharing phenomenal sugar cookies.\n\nA graduate of GGC, Jessica received her bachelor’s degree in information technology with a concentration in systems and security in 2019. She also appeared on GGC’s President’s List four times. Over the last six years, Jessica served in Information Technology at the college in roles of increasing responsibility, including as a networking student assistant, systems administrator I and systems administrator II. She began working towards a master’s degree in information systems with a concentration in cybersecurity in 2020 at the Georgia Institute of Technology. \n\nVisitation will be held 11 a.m.-12 p.m. Wednesday, Oct. 11, in the Peachtree Corners Chapel of Crowell Brothers Funeral Home & Crematory located at 5051 Peachtree Industrial Blvd., Peachtree Corners, GA 30092. The funeral service will begin the same day at 12 p.m. in the same location. You may [review Jessica’s full obituary](https://www.crowellbrothers.com/obituaries/Jessica-Camille-Walker?obId=29417483) for more details. \n\nFeelings of sadness and loss are a normal response to such situations. Support resources are available for faculty and staff through the Employee Assistance Program at 1.844.243.4440.\n\nThis is a tough time for the GGC family, and I encourage you to support each other while sending thoughts of peace and comfort to Jessica’s family and friends.\n\nSincerely,\n\n|                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------- |\n| **Dr. Jann L. Joseph**<br><br>**President** |\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"GGC Information Security","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Groups/GGC Information Security.md","lastModified":"2024-07-10T11:02:34.592Z","tags":[],"content":"# GGC Information Security\n[[Xiang (Daniel) Chung]]\nxchung\n2116611\n900220816\n\n[[Charles H. Leggett]]\ncleggett1\n2105027\n900214163","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Kara Latopolski","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Kara Latopolski.md","lastModified":"2024-07-10T10:50:56.535Z","tags":[],"content":"---\naliases:\n  - Dr. Kara Latopolski\n---\n# Kara Latopolski\nis the [[Georgia Gwinnett College (GGC)|GGC]] [[Dean of Students]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Amit Singh","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Amit Singh.md","lastModified":"2024-07-10T10:40:44.502Z","tags":[],"content":"---\naliases:\n  - Amit\n---\n# Amit Singh\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2024 USG ISO & CIO Workshop","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Conferences/2024 USG ISO & CIO Workshop/2024 USG ISO & CIO Workshop.md","lastModified":"2024-07-09T19:28:37.998Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2024 USG ISO & CIO Workshop\nTable of Contents\n```table-of-contents\ntitle: \nstyle: nestedList # TOC style (nestedList|nestedOrderedList|inlineFirstLevel)\nminLevel: 2 # Include headings from the specified level\nmaxLevel: 0 # Include headings up to the specified level\nincludeLinks: true # Make headings clickable\ndebugInConsole: false # Print debug info in Obsidian console\n```\n## Attendees\n- [[Georgia Gwinnett College (GGC)]]\n\t- [[Christine Miller Divine]]\n