that you must do.\n\n## [[B]]\na task that you should do, but has only mild consequences if you don't.\n\n## [[C]]\na nice to do, but has no consequences\n\n## [[D]]\na task that you can delegate\n\n## [[E]]\na task that you can eliminate w/o making any real difference\n\n## Credit\nfrom the book [[Lists/_OLD/10 - Personal/12 - Kaizen/Eat that Frog!/Eat that Frog!]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"7 Steps to Eat that Frog","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/10 - Personal/12 - Kaizen/Eat that Frog!/7 Steps to Eat that Frog.md","lastModified":"2024-06-12T19:28:30.399Z","tags":[],"content":"# 7 Steps to Eat that Frog\n1. Decide exactly what you want.\n2. Write it down. Think on paper.\n3. Set a deadline.\n4. Make a list of the steps needed to achieve this goal.\n5. Organize the list of steps into a plan.\n6. Take action on the plan immediately.\n7. Resolve to do something every day that moves you toward this goal.\n\nfrom the book [[Lists/_OLD/10 - Personal/12 - Kaizen/Eat that Frog!/Eat that Frog!]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"7 Key Result Areas in Management","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/10 - Personal/12 - Kaizen/Eat that Frog!/7 Key Result Areas in Management.md","lastModified":"2024-06-12T19:28:30.393Z","tags":[],"content":"# 7 Key Result Areas in Management\n1. Planning\n2. Organizing\n3. Staffing\n4. Delegating\n5. Supervising\n6. Measuring\n7. Reporting\n\nfrom the book [[Lists/_OLD/10 - Personal/12 - Kaizen/Eat that Frog!/Eat that Frog!]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"3 Questions for Max Productivity","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/10 - Personal/12 - Kaizen/Eat that Frog!/3 Questions for Max Productivity.md","lastModified":"2024-06-12T19:28:30.381Z","tags":[],"content":"# 3 Questions for Max Productivity\n1. What are my highest value activities?\n2. What can I, and only I, do that if done well, will make a real difference.\n3. What is the most useful use of my time right now?\n