on LinkedIn Learning/90.62 - R Course on LinkedIn Learning.md","lastModified":"2024-05-30T02:03:50.615Z","tags":[],"content":"---\nStatus: No status\nClosed: true\nPriority: No status\n---\n\nProjectName:: [[90.62 - R Course on LinkedIn Learning]]\nProjectManager:: [[Charles H. Leggett]]\nArea:: \nProgram:: \nStatus:: [[NOT STARTED]]\nPriority:: [[C]]\nStartDate:: \nDueDate::\nCompletionDate:: \n\n# 90.62 - R Course on LinkedIn Learning\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"90.30 - VMWare Contract Renegotiation","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Projects/90.30 - VMWare Contract Renegotiation/90.30 - VMWare Contract Renegotiation.md","lastModified":"2024-05-30T02:03:50.589Z","tags":[],"content":"---\nStatus: No status\nClosed: true\nPriority: No status\n---\n\nProjectName:: [[90.30 - VMWare Contract Renegotiation]]\nProjectManager:: [[Charles H. Leggett]]\nArea:: [[GGC Information Systems]]\nProgram:: [[GGC Infrastructure]] \nStatus:: [[WAITING FOR]]\nPriority:: [[C]]\n\n# 90.30 - VMWare Contract Renegotiation\n## Links\n[ClickUp]()\n[SharePoint]()\n## Reference\n\n## Project Files\n\n## Project Notes\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2023-10-13 - Friday","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Journal/2023/2023-10-13 - Friday.md","lastModified":"2024-05-30T01:36:53.443Z","tags":[],"content":"---\ndate: 2023-10-13\ntags:\n---\n# 2023-10-13 - Friday\n[[2023-10 - October]]\n\n## Notes\n- I have been using [[Foodvisor]] for 72 days now to lose weight to meet the [[GOAL - BSA Part C Weight Requirement]] among other goals & benefits.\n\t- I have lost 22.3 lbs so far.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Problems 565 through 570 - Email Autoreplies to Helpdesk","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Problems 565 through 570 - Email Autoreplies to Helpdesk.md","lastModified":"2024-05-30T01:36:39.191Z","tags":[],"content":"# Problems 565 through 570 - Email Autoreplies to Helpdesk\n\nStarted on [[2023-10-14 - Saturday]]\n\nSituation\n- The helpdesk received hundreds of messages\n\nAnalysis\n- All of the messages were from legit senders\n- The content and links for each was legitimate\n- They were all autoreplies from a request for help of some kind to a 3rd party\n\nThe theory is that an actor used the helpdesk@ggc.edu email address to make multiple requests to these 3rd parties\n- No mail was sent *from* helpdesk@ggc.edu (i.e. nothing to indicate compromise)\n\nDaniel blocked the autoreplying addresses at the helpdesk mailbox.\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"The Math behind GTD Just Doesn't Make Sense","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Ideas/The Math behind GTD Just Doesn't Make Sense.md","lastModified":"2024-05-30T01:33:32.685Z","tags":[],"content":"# The Math behind GTD Just Doesn't Make Sense\n\n[The Math behind GTD Just Doesn't Make Sense : r/gtd](https://reddit.com/r/gtd/s/hxWdUBCW9E)\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"GTD Weekly Review Process","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Getting Things Done (GTD)/GTD Weekly Review Process/GTD Weekly Review Process.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T20:50:48.604Z","tags":[],"content":"# GTD Weekly Review Process\n\n## [GTD Weekly Review Checklist](https://gettingthingsdone.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/Weekly_Review_Checklist.pdf)\n- GET CLEAR\n\t- Collect Loose Papers and Materials\n\t\t-Gather all accumulated business cards, receipts, and miscellaneous paper-based materials into your in-tray.\n\t- ~~Get “IN” to Zero~~\n\t\t-~~Process completely all outstanding paper materials, journal and meeting notes, voicemails, dictation, and emails.~~\n\t- Empty Your Head\n\t\t-Put in writing and process any uncaptured new projects, action items, waiting for’s, someday maybe’s, etc.\n-   GET CURRENT\n\t-  Review Action Lists\n\t\t-Mark off completed actions. Review for reminders of further action steps to record.\n\t- Review Previous Calendar Data\n\t\t-Review past calendar in detail for remaining action items, reference data, etc., and transfer into the active system.\n\t- Review Upcoming Calendar\n\t\t-Review upcoming calendar events–long and short term. Capture actions triggered.\n\t- Review Waiting For List\n\t\t-Record appropriate actions for any needed follow-up. Check off received ones.\n\t- Review Project (and Larger Outcome) Lists\n\t\t-Evaluate status of projects, goals, and outcomes, one by one, ensuring at least one current action item on each.\n\t\t-Browse through project plans, support material, and any other work-in-progress material to trigger new actions, completions, waiting for’s, etc.\n\t-Review Any Relevant Checklists\n\t\t-Use as a trigger for any new actions.\n- GET CREATIVE\n\t- Review Someday Maybe List\n\t\t-Review for any projects which may now have become active, and transfer to “Projects.” Delete items no longer of interest.\n\t- Be Creative and Courageous\n\t\t-Any new, wonderful, hare-brained, creative, thought-provoking, risk-taking ideas to add into your system???\n\n## Other Notes and Resources\n\n### Podcast Episodes:\n- [GTD Weekly Review tips from David Allen, with free checklist](https://gettingthingsdone.com/2018/08/episode-43-the-power-of-the-gtd-weekly-review/)\n\n\n## Need Calendar Review:\nChecking the past week, the next two weeks in my calendar and my tickler file. This includes converting stuff in the calendar into actions. Blocking in some time to do deep dive knowledge work undisturbed, and figuring out appropriate actions to prepare for scheduled meetings. Reclaim control over my time and Consider appointments that I want to defer to later or cancel.\n\n## Need \"Action List Cleanup\" if I scan my Action list and my eyes skip about avoiding many items, that has been on the list for ages\n\nAction List Cleanup: Go through your action lists and check the content ...\n- Is the action doable?\n- Is it physical and concrete?\n- Is it the NEXT action?\n- Is it possible to do in 25 minutes or less?\n- Do you still feel commited doing it?\n\n## Need \"Project Refocus\" if I'm busy but I'm not making real progress. Days go by emptying mail and milestone tasks stay uncompleted.\n\nProject Refocus: Prioritize your project list to ensure that you are doing the right actions …\n- Elevate the projects that are really important.\n- Move projects that are unimportant or undoable at this time to Someday/Maybe/Scheduled\n- Does each project have a clear outcome?\n- Is there a clear next action for each project?\n\n## Need \"Braindump\" if My head is full of stuff. I have the same idea several times but forget to write them down.\n\nBraindump: This is a thorough 10 minutes brainstorm aimed at emptying stuff from my head on to paper. This is done by mindmapping. I mindmap and brainstorm in the areas: LOVE, WORK, PLAY and GROWTH. After an initial free brainstorming phase, I use my project list as a checklist to trigger new ideas.\n\n## Need \"Someday/Maybe Review\" if I miss projects I feel excited about. I'm stuck in a routine. I need something fresh.\n\nSomeday/Maybe Review: This is looking through my saved creative ideas about things to do, to find something new and exciting to engage in. I find it really wonderful to find an old idea that I suddenly have the energy to commit to.\n\n## Need \"Personal Mission Statement Review\" if I lack motivation. I feel I'm getting nowhere. My work/life balance is out of control.\n\nPersonal Mission Statement Review: This is the big picture. How am I doing from the perspective of my life goals, my 5 year plan, and my 2 year goals. When these issues are reviewed projects are then reprioritized, and new relevant project are added.\n\nAdapted from [http://poder.dk/2007/09/13/lean-gtd-5-triggers-and-reactions-pull-in-my-gtd-system/](http://poder.dk/2007/09/13/lean-gtd-5-triggers-and-reactions-pull-in-my-gtd-system/)","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Joiner Document Format (JDF)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/OMSCY/GaTech OMS Cybersecurity (OMSCY) Program/Joiner Document Format (JDF)/Joiner Document Format (JDF).md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T17:47:36.001Z","tags":[],"content":"---\n{}\n---\n\n# Joiner Document Format (JDF)\n[Folder - Google Drive](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1xDYIomn9e9FxbIeFcsclSbXHTtHROD1j)\n\n![[JDF2.2-Starter.docx]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"OMS Cybersecurity Student Services Team","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/OMSCY/GaTech OMS Cybersecurity (OMSCY) Program/OMS Cybersecurity Student Services Team.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T17:47:36.000Z","tags":[],"content":"---\n{}\n---\n\n# OMS Cybersecurity Student Services Team\n- [[Jennifer]]\n- [[Allison]]\n- [[Shea]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"OMS Cybersecurity","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/OMSCY/GaTech OMS Cybersecurity (OMSCY) Program/OMS Cybersecurity.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T17:47:36.000Z","tags":[],"content":"---\n{}\n---\n\n# OMS Cybersecurity\n[[OMS Cybersecurity Student Services Team]]\n[[2020 - Fall]]\n[[2021 - Spring]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"OMSCY Course List and Descriptions","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/OMSCY/GaTech OMS Cybersecurity (OMSCY) Program/OMSCY Course List and Descriptions.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T17:47:36.000Z","tags":[],"content":"---\n{}\n---\n\n# OMSCY Course List and Descriptions\n![[oms-cybersecurity-course-list.pdf]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Spring 2024 Course Offerings","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/OMSCY/GaTech OMS Cybersecurity (OMSCY) Program/Spring 2024 Course Offerings.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T17:47:36.000Z","tags":[],"content":"---\n{}\n---\n\n# Spring 2024 Course Offerings\n\n![[oms-cybersecurity-course-schedule.pdf]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"pubp6725-fall2020-group45","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/OMSCY/63.01 - OMSCY - PUBP 6725 - Information Security Policies & Strategies/Files/pubp6725-fall2020-group45.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T17:47:3