 to deploy resources for information security\n6. How to know if information security measures are successful.\n\n### Information Security Begins With Top Management\n1. Star performers.\n2. Associated with brand value\n3. Failure severely impacts the organization\n4. Delays for the process are unacceptable\n5. Major investments made to perfecting it\n6. Major technical investments to make it efficient\n\nResults in classification:\n1. Critical\n2. Important\n3. Routine\n\n### Three pillars of security and security issues are different for different processes.\n1. Confidentiality = Restricted access\n2. Integrity = Completeness and accuracy\n3. Availability = Accessible when needed\n\n## Transcript\n\n[00:00:00]  \nIn this module we are focusing on the strategic dimensions on  \ninformation security and in this lesson we will address the implementation  \nof the secure information security process after this lecture you will be  \nable to determine the components of the implementation of an  \norganizational information security policy you will be able to select the  \nsteps to follow in the implementation of information security for guys  \national processes and you will be able to use models to assess the  \ninformation security status with respect to the organizational structure  \ninformation security policy implementation must address concerns of top  \nmanagement since we have established the top management has to be fairly  \ninvolved and is basic to the credibility and the success of any  \ninformation security policy top management concerns often are the value  \ninformation has for the business it also would be how information security  \ncontributes to business objectives since reduction of business value will  \nnot be something top manager will be happy about they will also be  \nconcerned about how information can be made more secure they will be  \nconcerned about the responsibility for security information that is what  \npart of the United Nations i