p","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Trails/Appalachian Trail (AT)/Appalachian Trail Heat Map.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:39:45.333Z","tags":[],"content":"# Appalachian Trail Heat Map\n\n[Where Are The Hikers? Appalachian Trail Heat Map](https://www.wherearethehikers.com/heatmap/)","bookmarked":false},{"title":"AT Shuttles  around the GA-NC Line","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Trails/Appalachian Trail (AT)/AT Shuttles  around the GA-NC Line.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:37:26.033Z","tags":[],"content":"# AT Shuttles  around the GA-NC Line\n\nRon - 706.781.7641\nSam - 706.994.6633\nGena - 423.653.7417\nPirate - 706.994.0178","bookmarked":false},{"title":"FS67","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Forest Service Roads/FS67.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:35:05.634Z","tags":[],"content":"# FS67\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Albert Mountain & Bigspring Gap","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Gaps/Albert Mountain & Bigspring Gap.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:35:01.353Z","tags":[],"content":"# Albert Mountain & Bigspring Gap\n[[Albert Mountain]]/[[Bigspring Gap]] -- follow [[FS67]] for 11 miles to it's\tend at a parking lot. At the far end of the lot, an old\tgated road leads about 1/3 mile to the [[Appalachian Trail (AT)]] between [[Albert Mountain]]. and [[Bigspring Gap]]. Turn right uphill for Albert, left for [[Bigspring Gap]] and shelter.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Albert Mountain","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Mountains/Albert Mountain.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:34:05.779Z","tags":[],"content":"# Albert Mountain\n\n![[Albert Mountain & Bigspring Gap]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Bigspring Gap","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Gaps/Bigspring Gap.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:33:47.266Z","tags":[],"content":"# Bigspring Gap\n\n![[Albert Mountain & Bigspring Gap]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Lower Ridge Trail","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Trails/Lower Ridge Trail.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:32:25.965Z","tags":[],"content":"# Lower Ridge Trail\n[[Lower Ridge Trail]] to [[Standing Indian Mountain]] --This strenuous trail\twill take you to the top of Standing Indian Mtn. in a little under 5\tmiles. It is a rough trail and not always well-maintained. It starts\tlike the [[Kimsey Creek Trail]], turns Left at the bridge over the river,\tand skirts the campground.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Long Branch Trail","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Trails/Long Branch Trail.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:32:25.946Z","tags":[],"content":"# Long Branch Trail\n[[Long Branch Trail]] -- follow [[FS67]] for 1.6 miles to the \"back-\tcountry Information Area\", a parking lot with displays\tat the end of the pavement. The [[Long Branch Trail]] starts\tjust across the road from the parking area, and leads\t2.0 miles to the [[Appalachian Trail (AT)]] at [[Glassmine Gap]], which is about\tmid-way between [[Bigspring Gap]] and [[Rock Gap]].","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Kimsey Creek Trail","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Trails/Kimsey Creek Trail.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:32:25.915Z","tags":[],"content":"# Kimsey Creek Trail\n[[Kimsey Creek Trail]] to [[Deep Gap]] -- From the Backcountry Parking Area,\ttake the blue-blazed trail that leaves beside the bulletin board. Follow this trail into the Standing Indian Campground, and watch for signs just after crossing the bridge across the [[Nantahala River]], and again at a trail junction a short way into the woods. The trail skirts\tthe campground area, then follows [[Kimsey Creek]] upstream to [[Deep Gap]]\tand the [[Appalachian Trail (AT)]].","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Timber Ridge Trail","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Trails/Timber Ridge Trail.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:32:25.821Z","tags":[],"content":"# Timber Ridge Trail\n[[Timber Ridge Trail]] -- continue on FS67 for 6.4 miles past [[Rock Gap]]. There is a small parking area at the trailhead. It is\t2.3 miles up the [[Timber Ridge Trail]] to the [[Appalachian Trail (AT)]]. This trail\tmeets the AT 0.4 miles South of [[Carter Gap]].","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Beech Gap Trail","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Trails/Beech Gap Trail.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:32:20.756Z","tags":[],"content":"# Beech Gap Trail\n[[Beech Gap Trail]] -- continue on FS67 for 6 miles past [[Rock Gap]].\tThe road turns to dirt, but is a good road. There is a small\tparking area at the Trailhead. It is 2.7 miles on the Beech\tGap Trail to the AT at [[Beech Gap]].","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Nantahala River","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Rivers/Nantahala River.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:31:02.780Z","tags":[],"content":"# Nantahala River\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"NHC Trailheads Info","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Trails/NHC Trailheads Info.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:30:57.895Z","tags":[],"content":"# NHC Trailheads Info\n\n## How safe is the parking at our Trailheads?\n- Vandalism to cars parked at trailheads is a problem all up and down the AT. Our\tsection has had little vandalism compared to some areas, but there IS some.\n- Cars left at trailheads in the backcountry, such as Deep Gap, Rock Gap, Backcountry\tinformation area, Burningtown Gap, and Tellico Gap, have occasionally been\tbroken into when items of value were visible inside the cars.\n- Hikers can usually make arrangements for leaving cars at Nantahala Outdoor Center.\n\n## Trail-Heads for N.H.C. Section of the AT\n- The first 8 Trailheads are places where the Trail meets a public road, and cars can be parked.\n- The second section lists trailheads for side-trails which can be used to access the AT (and for loop hikes).\n\n## Trailheads listed from SOUTH to NORTH on AT.\n> BLY GAP - please be aware that there is NO ROAD ACCESS to Bly Gap!\tThe nearest access in North Carolina is at Deep Gap, and in Georgia\tat Dick's Creek Gap on US76. There is a sometimes-open road to\tBlue Ridge Gap in Georgia, 3.2 miles South of Bly Gap.\n\n1. ![[Deep Gap]]\n   \n2. ![[Mooney Gap]]\n   \n3. ![[Rock Gap]]\n   \n4. ![[Winding Stair Gap]]\n   \n5. ![[Wayah Gap]]\n   \n6. ![[Wayah Bald]]\n   \n7. ![[Burningtown Gap]]\n   \n8. ![[Tellico Gap]]\n   \n9. ![[Wesser]]\n\n## Standing Indian Area access trails -- (South to North)\n\n> For all these trails, follow directions given for 2)RockGap\tabove, then CONTINUE on FS67 (when open) to these trailheads.\n\n> Trails 1, 2, and 8 leave from the \"Backcountry Information\tArea\", which is a parking area at the end of the paved part of FS67.\tFollow FS67 past Rock Gap Parking area for 1.6 miles, bearing left at the\tY at the entrance to Standing Indian Campground.\n\n1. ![[Kimsey Creek Trail]]\n2. ![[Lower Ridge Trail]]\n3. ![[Beech Gap Trail]]\n4. ![[Timber Ridge Trail]]\n5. ![[Betty Creek Trail]]\n6. ![[Mooney Gap]]\n7. ![[Albert Mountain & Bigspring Gap]]\n8. ![[Long Branch Trail]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Betty Creek Gap","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Gaps/Betty Creek Gap.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:28:11.438Z","tags":[],"content":"# Betty Creek Gap\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Betty Creek Trail","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Trails/Betty Creek Trail.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:27:40.689Z","tags":[],"content":"# Betty Creek Trail\n[[Betty Creek Trail]] -- continue on [[FS67]] for 8.3 miles past [[Rock Gap]]. There is a clearing/camping area at this trailhead.\tThe beginning of the Betty Creek trail is poorly marked --\tit starts at an opening in the East side of the clearing,\tand almost immediately crosses a small creek. Past the\tcreek follow the blue blazes for about a half mile to the [[Appalachian Trail (AT)]] at [[Betty Creek Gap]].","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Nantahala Outdoor Center (NOC)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Companies/Nantahala Outdoor Center (NOC).md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:14:20.737Z","tags":[],"content":"# Nantahala Outdoor Center (NOC)\n\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Trails","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Trails/Trails.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T05:03:50.493Z","tags":[],"content":"# Trails\n\n## Long\n- [[Appalachian Trail (AT)]]\n- [[John Muir Trail]]\n- [[PCT]]\n- [[CDT]]\n## Medium\n- [[Bartram Trail]]\n- [[Byron Reese Trail]]\n## Short\n- [[Jack’s River Falls]]\n\n[[41 - Outdoors]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Alfred Barker","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Alfred Barker.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T04:42:15.653Z","tags":[],"content":"# Alfred Barker\n\nAnnounced his retirement at the [[2024 USG ISO & CIO Workshop]] on [[2024-05-21 - Tuesday]] effective [[2024-06-30 - Sunday]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"University of North Georgia (UNG)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Higher Education Institutions/University of North Georgia (UNG).md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T04:38:42.367Z","tags":[],"content":"# University of North Georgia (UNG)\n## People\n[[Rob Cherveny]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Rob Cherveny","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Rob Cherveny.md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T04:38:18.972Z","tags":[],"content":"# Rob Cherveny\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Kennesaw State University (KSU)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Higher Education Institutions/Kennesaw State University (KSU).md","lastModified":"2024-05-29T04:36:40.639Z","tags":[],"content":"# Kennesaw State University (KSU)\n\n## People\n[[Stephen Gay]]\n[[Thomas Butterworth]]\n## Resources\n[[KSU_RiskRegister_Template.xlsx]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Thomas Butterworth","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Thomas Butterwo