 Perf Mgmt Form_Provisional.pdf]]\n\n[[2021 GGC Perf Mgmt Form_Supervisor.pdf]]\n\n[[2021 GGC Perf Mgmt_Staff.pdf]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Compensation & Benefits","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Compensation & Benefits/Compensation & Benefits.md","lastModified":"2023-11-30T17:54:34.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Compensation & Benefits","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Scheduling & Flexibility","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Scheduling & Flexibility/Scheduling & Flexibility.md","lastModified":"2023-11-30T17:53:06.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Scheduling & Flexibility\n\n![[2023-05 - IS&S - Teleworking Agreements.pdf]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Annual Reporting Requirements","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/University System of Georgia (USG)/USG Cybersecurity/Annual Reporting Requirements.md","lastModified":"2023-11-30T17:42:27.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Annual Reporting Requirements\nSee also: [[Incident Reporting Requirements]]\n\nPer Section 5.10 of the USG [[IT_Handbook_V2.9.3.pdf]], we are required to report the following:\n\n## Cybersecurity Officer Contact Information Update\n    \nAs noted in Section 5.2.2 of the USG IT Handbook, the name and appropriate designee contact information must be sent to USG Cybersecurity within 10 business days of any designee change.\n\n##  Cybersecurity Incident Response Plan Submission\n\nAs noted in Section 5.3.1 of the USG IT Handbook, a cybersecurity incident response plan must be formally documented and electronically sent and filed with USG Cybersecurity.\n\n## Remediation and Mitigation Tracker\n\nThe Remediation and Mitigation Tracker tool provides a mechanism to track the managing department and point of contact (POC) information; summarizes the issues from the final audit/assessment; identifies the specific requirements to address an issue; records a scheduled completion date; and tracks the status of the remediation effort.\n\n## Cybersecurity Program Review (CPR) Submission\n\nThe Governor’s Executive Order of March 19, 2008, requires development of a composite report on the status of cybersecurity for all state agencies. The USG has chosen to align itself with this order by producing its own USG CPR. Reference Figure 3 Required Reporting Diagram. USG Cybersecurity will complete the following CPR processes on an annual basis:\n\n## Reporting Schedule\n\n![[USG IT Handbook - Section 5.10 - Required Reporting - Timeline.png]]\n\n-   January: USG Cybersecurity shall merge the spring and fall analysis into the annual cybersecurity risk and maturity report and make available to respective USG CIOs, CISOs and USO senior staff.\n\n-   February: USG Cybersecurity requests USG organizations to update winter Remediation and Mitigation Trackers (trackers). USG organizations are permitted 31 days to complete the trackers.\n    \n-   March: USG Cybersecurity collects, compiles and analyzes the updated winter trackers.\n\n-   April: USG Cybersecurity shall review previous CPR reports to determine if changes are required and identify areas of focus for the upcoming review period. USG Information Technology Services (ITS) senior staff and the Internal Audit and Compliance department will review proposed changes. USG Cybersecurity shall inform USG organization of any revisions to the report, changes to the CPR reporting process and the areas of focus for the upcoming review period.\n\n-   May: USG Cybersecurity releases the Spring CPR Survey to USG organizations. USG organizations have 30 days to complete the survey.\n    \n-   June: USG Cybersecurity collects, compiles and analyzes Spring CPR Survey results.\n    \n-   August: USG Cybersecurity requests USG organizations to update summer trackers. USG organizations are permitted 31 days to complete the trackers.\n    \n-   September: USG Cybersecurity collects, compiles and analyzes the updated summer trackers.\n    \n-   October: The winter and summer analysis of the trackers are merged into the annual report(s) respective to what is being tracked (i.e., Audit, MFA FSA....), which shall be made available to respective USG CIOs, CISOs and USO senior staff.\n\n-   November: USG Cybersecurity releases the Fall CPR Survey to USG organizations. USG organizations have 30 days to complete the survey.\n    \n-   December: USG Cybersecurity collects, compiles and analyzes Fall CPR Survey results.\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Incident Reporting Requirements","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/University System of Georgia (USG)/USG Cybersecurity/Incident Reporting Requirements.md","lastModified":"2023-11-30T17:42:18.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Incident Reporting Requirements\nAs noted in Section 5.3.2 of the USG IT Handbook, a timely response is critical. USG organizations must report all cybersecurity incidents or events of interest affecting information or information systems, products, or services for any of the cybersecurity objectives of confidentiality, integrity, or availability to USG Cybersecurity through the ITS Helpdesk (helpdesk@usg.edu) at 706-583-2001, or 1-888-875-3697 (toll free within Georgia). For all incidents affecting mission-critical systems and categorized as “High” shall be reported to USG Cybersecurity within one hour of identification.\n\n#  Cybersecurity Incident Follow-up Reporting Requirement\nAs noted in Section 5.3.3 of the USG IT Handbook, an incident follow-up report must be submitted to USG Cybersecurity.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Beyond the Bullet Journal How to Hack Your BuJo","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Articles/Beyond the Bullet Journal How to Hack Your BuJo.md","lastModified":"2023-11-30T16:06:20.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Beyond the Bullet Journal: How to Hack Your BuJo\n\n[Beyond the Bullet Journal: How to Hack Your BuJo](https://www.attorneyatwork.com/beyond-bullet-journal-bujo/)\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Information System Definition","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Data/Information System Definition.md","lastModified":"2023-11-30T14:44:41.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Information System Definition\n\nNOTE: many of the terms that I use here are defined in existing sources (e.g.  our Data Governance documentation, USG BPM, IT Handbook, HECVAT, NIST CSF, etc.) and should be used as written to avoid confusion.\n\n- System Name\n- System Description\n\t- Blurb of the reason that we run this service.\n\t- Link to system in Service Catalog\n- List of Customers (students, faculty, staff, individual departments, etc.)\n- System Owner\n\t- Person (often outside of IT)\n\t- Division\n\t- Department\n- IT or EMTech Owner (Same-as or partner-of System Owner)\n\t- Person\n\t- Division\n\t- Department\n- Vendor\n\t- Company’s name\n\t- Company contact’s name, title, email, and phone number\n- Support Hours (from our after-hours support topic)\n\t- Business Hours (8am-5pm M-F)\n\t- 24x7x365\n- Business Critical\n\t- True\n\t- False\n- Contains PII\n\t- True\n\t- False\n- Hosting Model\n\t- On-prem\n\t- USG Hosted\n\t- Cloud Vendor (SaaS)\n- Status\n\t- Under Development\n\t- Major Modification\n\t- Operational\n- Systems Security Plan (SSP) Approval date\n- MM/DD/YYYY\n- Approving Official\n\t- Person\n- System Security Officer\n\t- GGC ISO\n- Data Owner\n\t- President\n- Data Trustee\n\t- See list in Data Governance document\n- Data Steward\n\t- See role definition in Data Governance document\n- Data Manager\n\t- See role definition in Data Governance document\n- Other Designated Contacts\n\t- Any other responsible Subject Matter Experts (SMEs)\n- Regulatory Requirements (multi select)\n\t- USG BPM\n\t- USG IT Handbook\n\t- FERPA\n\t- HIPAA\n\t- PCI-DSS\n\t- GLBA\n\t- Others?\n- Interconnected (or sub) System(s)\n\t- List of all integrated and/or dependent systems\n- Backup Strategy\n\t- GGC\n\t- Vendor\n\t- Shared Services\n- Link to SharePoint share or Confluence page with supporting documents\n\t- Systems Security Plan (SSP)\n\t- Data Retention Schedule\n\t- IT Operations Runbooks\n\t- Support Documentation\n\t- Business Continuity Plan\n\t- Disaster Recovery Plan\n\t- HECVAT\n\t- VPAT\n\t- SLA\n\t- OLA(s)\n\t- KPI(s)\n\t- etc.\n\n## Reference\n### Initial Email:\n> **From:** Charles Leggett <cleggett1@ggc.edu>  \n> \n> **Subject:** **Re: BLT Systems List Discussion**  \n> \n> **Date:** October 21, 2023 at 08:05:37 EDT  \n> \n> **To:** Kevin McCuen <kmccuen@ggc.edu>  \n> \n> **Cc:** Christine Miller Divine <cmillerdivine@ggc.edu>, Jeremy Tuttle <jtuttle3@ggc.edu>, Amit Singh <asingh10@ggc.edu>, Jacky Sylvain <jsylvain@ggc.edu>, Tracy Burge <tadkins5@ggc.edu>, Eugene Horn <ehorn1@ggc.edu>, Kathryn Wise <kwise@ggc.edu>  \n> \n> Hey Kevin, et al.\n> \n> Building on what you sent, here’s my proposed list of fields:\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"status.ggc.edu","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/ITSM/status.ggc.edu.md","lastModified":"2023-11-30T14:38:48.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# status.ggc.edu\n\n[GGC Status](https://status.ggc.edu)\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"GGC IT Services","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/ITSM/GGC IT Services/GGC IT Services.md","lastModified":"2023-11-30T14:34:11.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# GGC IT Services\n\n- Website (www.ggc.edu)\n- Single Sign-on (SSO)\n-  Teaching & Learning\n\t- MyCourses\n\t- Kaltura\n\t- Grizzly Den (Banner)\n\t- DegreeWorks\n\t- GradesFirst / EAB Navigate\n\t- LinkedIn Learning\n\t- Grizzly Learning Path (Percipio)\n\t- Turnitin\n\t- SL&L/Via (Portfolio)\n\t- CRM Recruit\n\t- Classroom Technology\n\t- Class Climate\n\t- domains.ggc.edu  ?\n-  Network\n\t- Wired Network\n\t- Wireless Network (GGC Wifi, GGC Guest, & eduroam)\n\t- VPN\n\t- PeachNet Internet Access\n-  Communication & Collaboration Tools\n\t- Claw Mail\n\t- Microsoft Teams\n\t- Microsoft Office 365\n\t- Microsoft OneDrive / SharePoint\n\t- LISTSERV\n\t- Zoom\n-  Telephone Systems\n\t- Office & Desk Phones\n\t- Softphones\n-  Productivity Tools\n\t- Device Management\n\t- Printing & Scanning\n\t- File Sharing\n\t- ClickUp\n- GeorgiaFIRST PeopleSoft Financials\n- OneUSG Connect (oneusgconnect.usg.edu)\n- Help Desk Portal\n- WordPress","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Interstitial Journaling (IJ)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/10 - Personal/12 - Kaizen/Interstitial Journaling (IJ).md","lastModified":"2023-11-30T13:24:19.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Interstitial Journaling (IJ)\n\nThought Leaders:\n- [[Tony Stubblebine]]\n- [[Anne-Laurie Le Cunff]]\n\nRelated:\n- [[The Hawthorne Effect]]\n\n## Articles:\n[Interstitial journaling: combining notes, to-do & time tracking](https://nesslabs.com/interstitial-journaling) - [[Ness Labs - Mindful Productivity School for Knowledge Workers]] - [[Anne-Laurie Le Cunff]]\n\n\n[Interstitial Journaling: Capturing the Ebb and Flow of Thoughts](https://www.curiouslychase.com/posts/interstitial-notes/) - [[Curiously Chase]]\n- Compares to [[BuJo]]\n- Ideas on how to implement in [[Obsidian]] including:\n\t- [Get all links to the current file with Obsidian and Dataview](https://www.curiouslychase.com/posts/get-all-links-to-the-current-file-with-obsidian-and-dataview/)\n\n[Replace Your To-Do List With Interstitial Journaling To Increase Productivity](https://betterhumans.pub/replace-your-to-do-list-with-interstitial-journaling-to-increase-productivity-4e43109d15ef) - [[Tony Stubblebine]] - [[Better Humans]]\n\n[How to do Interstitial Journaling With (or Without) Notion and Become More Intentional About Your Day - Goodhart](https://goodhartphotographyva.com/interstitial-journaling-with-notion/)\n\n[How 'interstitial journaling' can help you focus your day and work smarter](https://www.nbcnews.com/better/lifestyle/how-interstitial-journaling-can-help-you-focus-your-day-work-ncna1036166) - [[NBC News]]\n\n[Improve Your Focus and Concentrate Better With This Bullet Journaling](https://bulletjournal.com/blogs/bulletjournalist/how-to-improve-focus-using-a-bullet-journal) - [[BuJo]]\n\n[Interstitial Journaling | by Joey Harris | Medium](https://personalshakespeare.medium.com/interstitial-journaling-54c6b7856c40)\n\n## Videos:\n[How I Use Interstitial Journaling to Increase Productivity](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=64b0Pm1E-5M) - [[Dan Silvestre]]\n\n[Interstitial Journaling: Track Your Day to Clear Your Mind and Be More Productive](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fDzoQ5rCAV8) - [[Shu Omi]]\n\n[Interstitial Journaling - a simple productivity workflow - YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KpLfZi8YXvg) - [[Growth Quest]]\n\n[Stay motivated all day - Interstitial Journaling in your agency - YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TwGhTvCkQ8M) - [[Trailblazer FM with Lee Matthew Jackson]]\n\n[A NEW approach to TASK MANAGEMENT | Interstitial journaling in Tana - YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ipZbJZ9Vz7g) - [[Tomi Nuottamo]]\n\n[Interstitial Journaling for Productivity and Mindfulness - YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tCnQSN0bBPU&t=5s) - [[ankteckningar]]\n\n[Interstitial Journaling on Logseq - YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wdFWkyVcYVU) - [[Elymar Apao]]\n\n[What's Destroying Your Attention And How To Fix it - YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JzYJGRaCaOg&t=1s) - [[Ryder Carroll]] - [[BuJo]]\n\n\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"VitalSmarts GTD Course","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Training/62.02 - VitalSmarts GTD Course/VitalSmarts GTD Course.md","lastModified":"2023-11-30T13:20:39.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# VitalSmarts GTD Course\n\n![[Getting Things Done Live Online Toolkit.pdf]]\n\n[[Resources/Unstructured/GTD]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"YNAB","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Family/Leggett/Finances/YNAB/YNAB.md","lastModified":"2023-11-29T20:29:48.538Z","tags":[],"content":"# YNAB\n \n\n \n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Gazelle","path":"/Users/clegg