e::\nCompletionDate:: \n\n# 90.60 - Comprehensive Policy Review\n## Reference\n[[86.12 - GGC Administrative Policy Manual (APM)]]\n[[86.11.01 - USG IT Handbook (ITHB)]]\n[[86.11.02 - USG Business Procedures Manual (BPM)]]\n\n## Tracking\n[IT Policies Tracking Sheet](https://ggcedu-my.sharepoint.com/:x:/g/personal/kmccuen_ggc_edu/EU7sATvRoFdHlnof_0JQvIsBvQdyryv3Hzs8NEAOLV2l2g?e=iXczkK&wdOrigin=TEAMS-ELECTRON.p2p.bim&wdExp=TEAMS-CONTROL&wdhostclicktime=1671735882789&web=1)\n[[GGC Information Security Policies]]\n\n## Policy Review Request\n[Policy Review Form](https://forms.office.com/r/MvzE2AsT8e)\n\n## Guidelines\n[Policy Requirements Policy](https://catalog.ggc.edu/content.php?catoid=42&navoid=5863#-11-policy-on-policies)\n[[Guidelines for Comprehensive Review Packet.pdf]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"90.61 - ClickUp Implementation","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Projects/90.61 - ClickUp Implementation/90.61 - ClickUp Implementation.md","lastModified":"2023-11-20T17:04:44.000Z","tags":[],"content":"---\nStatus: No status\nClosed: true\nPriority: No status\n---\n\n# 90.61 - ClickUp Implementation\n\n![[2021.02.18 - Work and Project Management Tool Comparison.png]]\n\n[PM Tool Requirements.v1](https://ggcedu-my.sharepoint.com/:x:/r/personal/ngraterol_ggc_edu/_layouts/15/Doc.aspx?sourcedoc=%7BB14FBA98-B34C-4E55-BA53-B0ED4AB12C85%7D&file=PM%20Tool%20Requirements.v1.xlsx&action=default&mobileredirect=true)","bookmarked":false},{"title":"90.63 - Risk Management Council Establishment","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Projects/90.63 - Risk Management Council Establishment/90.63 - Risk Management Council Establishment.md","lastModified":"2023-11-20T17:04:44.000Z","tags":[],"content":"---\nStatus: No status\nClosed: true\nPriority: No status\n---\n\n# 90.63 - Risk Management Council Establishment\n**From:** Russell Mathis <rmathis@ggc.edu>  \n**Subject:** **Enterprise Risk Management Council**  \n**Date:** February 1, 2021 at 10:47:37 EST  \n**To:** \"Ruth W. Berger\" <rberger@ggc.edu>, Jo Galle <jgalle@ggc.edu>, Janice Balte <jbalte@ggc.edu>, Tomas Jimenez <tjimenez@ggc.edu>, Sloan Jones <sjones45@ggc.edu>, Katherine Kyle <kkyle@ggc.edu>, Laura Ledford <lledford@ggc.edu>, \"Terrance W. Schneider\" <tschneid@ggc.edu>, \"Charles H. Leggett\" <cleggett1@ggc.edu>, Laura Brown <lbrown2@ggc.edu>  \n\nTeam,\n\nWe will be reinvigorating GGC’s Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) initiative in 2021.  Although it has been a while, each of you were previously identified as appointees to the ERM Committee and as such will be instrumental in driving risk awareness, identifying areas of opportunity, and developing solutions to ensure the success of ERM at GGC. \n\nThe adoption of an institution-wide approach to risk management is a requirement of USG BOR Policy 7.11 - _Risk Management_, and is further delineated in GGC’s Risk Management policy – APM 7.15.  The USG policy depicts Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) as “a process-driven tool that enables management to visualize, assess, and manage major risks that may adversely impact the attainment of key organization objectives.”  The policy further states that “an institution-wide approach to risk management shall be adopted by all USG institutions, and that all risk management efforts shall be focused on supporting the institution’s objectives.” \n\nIn addition to the above referenced policies, I am attaching a _GGC ERM Manual_ for your review prior to our first meeting.  This document provides a summary of what ERM encompasses as well as the basic framework that was initially adopted by the USG for implementing ERM at the System office. \n\nI will be setting up a ‘Risk Management Council’ in Microsoft Teams soon, for which you will be receiving an invitation/notice.  You will be hearing from me soon to set up our first meeting (via the Microsoft Teams App).  Thanks in advance for your participation.  Hopefully we can leverage this USG requirement into a tool that will provide long-lasting benefit to GGC.\n\nIf you have any questions or concerns please contact me.\n\nBest regards,\nRuss\n\n**Russell B. Mathis, CPA, CIA**\n**Internal Audit Director**\n\n![[2021.02.19 - GGC ERM Manual 2021.pdf]]\n![[2021.02.19 - APM 7-15.pdf]]\n![[2021.02.19 - BOR Policy 7-11 Risk Management.pdf]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"90.64 - SharePoint Migration","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Projects/90.64 - SharePoint Migration/90.64 - SharePoint Migration.md","lastModified":"2023-11-20T17:04:44.000Z","tags":[],"content":"---\nStatus: No status\nClosed: true\nPriority: No status\n---\n\n# 90.64 - SharePoint Migration\n \n\n \n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"90.65 - Softphone Implementation","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Projects/90.65 - Softphone Implementation/90.65 - Softphone Implementation.md","lastModified":"2023-11-20T17:04:44.000Z","tags":[],"content":"---\nStatus: No status\nClosed: true\nPriority: No status\n---\n\n# 90.65 - Softphone Implementation\n\n## Eligibility\n1. The Provost made the decision that all Faculty will have one.\n2. Staff will get phones in this order (determined by roll)\n\t1. Desk Phone\n\t2. Softphone\n\t3. Cell phone\n\n## Evolve IP\n\n### Provisioning\nBen Silver <bsilver@evolveip.net>\n\n### Messages App\n\nSMS/MMS Service backend:\nhttps://www.zipwhip.com\n\nMessages Teams App Feature Guide:\nhttps://support.evolveip.net/display/EIQ/SMS+-+Evolve+Messaging+-+Feature+Guide\n\nApp Testing and Troubleshooting\n[[2021-07-20 - Evolve IP Messages App v1.0.3 \"Testing Party\"]]\n\n\n---\n\n\n## Microsoft Calling\nPTN Escalation:\nRobert Conn\nrocon@microsoft.com\n+14255383976\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"90.66 - Tennis Court Cameras","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Projects/90.66 - Tennis Court Cameras/90.66 - Tennis Court Cameras.md","lastModified":"2023-11-20T17:04:44.000Z","tags":[],"content":"---\nStatus: No status\nClosed: true\nPriority: No status\n---\n\n# 90.66