 Configuration\n\n## Eric's Notes\n\n*********************************************************Netmotion User Credentials***********************************************\nnetmotion user credentials\nusername:ggcpd\npasswd: 1!password!1\nDomain ggcpd\n\nContact X2 support diversecomputing retrieve Shared Secrert for X2 Radius Server and give to Doug Schad to complete testing \n\tX2 support diversecomputing will get on GGC's X2 server to get Shared Secret Password for Radius\n\t\tJustin Lenczewski \t850-656-3333 ext 290\n\t\tAdam Corvin  \t\t850-656-3333 ext 274\nNew Shared Secret Passwd: EubiwRm0\nOld Shared Secret Passwd: testing123\n\n******************************************* How to add users to eAgent *****************************************************\n\nStep 1 \n\t* Login to ADDC01 (10.42.102.10) via Remote Desktop\n\t* Got Active Directory users & groups\nStep 2 \n\t* add to user group grpPublicSafety & grpPublicSafety-X2\n\n*****************************************X2 eAgent SSH CLI access ****************************************************************************\nX2 eAgent Root Passwd: Eix1uPhitWi_3#2x3\n\nuser name: emaddox\tPasswd: JakkkE50$\n\nChange Shared Secret Passwd:\nStep 1 \n\t* SSH via Putty or Secure CRT to X2 eAgent server 10.42.234.100\n\t\t-- username: root\tPasswd: Eix1uPhitWi_3#2x3\n\n\nStep 2\n\t* cd /etc/dci/dciconf/\n\t\t-- ls ( locate appsettings.py)\n\t\t\t** appsettings.py      crontabsettings.pyc  nodesettings.py   settings.pyc  websettings.py\n\t\t\t   appsettings.pyc     __init__.py          nodesettings.pyc  urls.py       websettings.pyc\n\t\t\t   crontabsettings.py  __init__.pyc         settings.py       urls.pyc\n\nStep 3\n\t* vim appsettings.py\n\t\t-- enter text mode \"i\"\n\t\t\t** scrooll down to \"FREERAD_SECRET_1 = 'EubiwRm0'\"\n\t\t\t\t--- change passwd 'EubiwRm0'\n\t\t-- enter command mode pressing \"ESC\" on keyboard\n\t\t-- exit vim by pressing shift + Colon cursor moves to end of file then press wq enter\n\t\t-- restart eAgent:  service easwitch restart or sudo  service easwitch restart (not logged as root)\n\n**APPSETTINGS.PY file***\n # BASE\nTIME_ZONE = 'America/New_York'\nNOTIFICATION_EMAIL = 'root@localhost'\n\n# 91.12 - eAgent X2 MFA Configuration\nROOTDB_PASSWORD = 'Bvak2SN8'\nDEFAULTDB_PASSWORD = 'EYMv6h3s'\nAUDITLOGDB_PASSWORD = 'EYMv6h3s'\nFREERADIUSDB_PASSWORD = 'EYMv6h3s'\n\n# EAP RADIUS\nFREERAD_IPADDR_1 = '10.40.151.45'\nFREERAD_PORT_1   = '1812'\nFREERAD_DOMAIN_1 = 'dci'\nFREERAD_SECRET_1 = 'EubiwRm0'\n\n# PAP RADIUS\nPYRAD_IPADDR_1 = '127.0.0.1'\nPYRAD_PORT_1   = '1912'\nPYRAD_DOMAIN_1 = 'setup'\nPYRAD_SECRET_1 = 'testing123'\n\n# makeshift settings pulled in\nDCI_WWW_SECUREX2_ENFORCEWEBSECONDFACTOR = True\n\n\n\n**************************************************************Palo Alto Security & Nat Policy *******************************************************************\nSecurity Policy\nSR allow_X2_psma\n\nSource Zone: campus-outside\tSource Address: LPD_Netmotion1 (72.54.140.66), LPD_Netmotion2(72.54.140.88)\t    Type: Universal\nDestination Zone: campus-inside\t\tDestination Address: nat_gv-psma-01 (168.28.16.168)\t  Service: port UDP/1812\n\n\nNAT Policy\nAutoNAT X2-psma\nSource Zone: campus-inside\tDestination Zone: campus-outside\tDestination interface: Any\tSource Address: gv-psma-01 (10.42.234.100)\nDestination address: any\tService: any\tSource Translation: Static ip; nat_gv_psma-01 (168.28.16.168); bi-directional: yes \n\n\n******************************************************External DNS and Active Directory Info ***********************************\n\ngv-psma-01      in      A       168.28.16.168\npsma            in      CNAME   gv-psma-01.ggc.edu.\n\n\nVLAN2034  10.42.234.100\n\nHostname and IP of the X2 server: gv-psmfa-01.ggc.edu   \nHostname and IP of your DCs/Nameservers: addc01.ggc.edu: 10.42.102.10 and addc02.ggc.edu: 10.42.2.10\nInternal IP of the NetMotion VPN: 10.40.151.45 \n\n\nAdd Users Via ADDOC1 >>  add to user group grpPublicSafety \n  **  Must be in grpPublicSafety group and grpPublicSafety-X2 group to become an Admin\n\nusername: Root\nPassword: Eix1uPhitWi_3#2x3\n\nX2 Netmotion Server\n\nConnect via ssh 10.42.234.100 using root \n\nConnect via https://10.42.234.100 eAgent X2 portal using Domain Account.\n\n*************************************************************************************************************************\n\nYou will have to NAT a Static/Public External IP address to your internal X2 server.  You will have to allow port UDP/1812 for inbound and outbound traffic.  \n\nOnce this has been completed, I will need to know that Static/Public IP address to add it into NetMotion.  I will be creating to Device Groups, LPD and GGCPD.  \n\nEach device group is assigned an Authorization Profile, also called LPD amd GGCPD that allows separate settings for each group.  \n\nThis is where I will assign GGC users to your RADIUS Server to authenticate them.\n\nHow it works all works.Ö The Netmotion VPN is configured on your end to connect to 72.54.140.74 (Netmotion Public IP Address NATíd to my Netmotion Server). \n\nNetmotion receives your incoming packet and identifies what your device name is (computer name) and checks to see if there are any specific device settings that need to apply. \n\nIt then says, there is a RADIUS Server assigned to this device and attempts to connect to your X2 Public IP address.  It tells it to look at the name provided \n\nand authenticate the user, which then the X2 sends the credentials through Netmotion to your device.  You place the proper credentials \n\nassigned in the X2 software and if it passes, X2 tells NemotionÖWeíre Good and Netmotion connects to the server. We have opened up all Zuercher (CAD/MOBILE)\n\nports between Netmotion and Zuercher.  Everything in Zuercher authenticates through the IP and not Domain credentials.  So we shouldnít have an issueÖHOPEFULLY!\n\nI know our outbound IPís can be either 72.54.140.66 or 72.54.140.88, depending on o