Barker@USG.EDU>  \n> \n> **Subject:** **[USG-ISOS-L] USG Unified ERP Planning Project Kick-Off Meeting - Presentation**  \n> \n> **Date:** October 18, 2023 at 16:40:55 EDT  \n> **To:** [[USG-ISOS-L@LISTSERV.UGA.EDU]] \n> **Reply-To:** USG Info Security Officers <USG-ISOS-L@LISTSERV.UGA.EDU>  \n> \n> Sent on behalf of the [[USG Office of Strategic Implementation]]\n> \n> All, FYI – Thank you for your participation in our Unified [[Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP)]] Project kick-off meeting this morning.  We had over 500 participants attend our meeting and want to thank you all for your support!  The presentation is attached.\n\n![[USG Systemwide Kickoff - FINAL.pdf]]s","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2021-07-20 - Evolve IP Messages App v1.0.3 \"Testing Party\"","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Journal/_Calendar_/2021-07-20 - Evolve IP Messages App v1.0.3 \"Testing Party\".md","lastModified":"2023-11-20T13:46:22.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2021-07-20 - Evolve IP Messages App v1.0.3 \"Testing Party\"\n\non [[2021.07.20]]\n\n1. The Messages app within Teams has to be active to receive notifications.\n\n2. Messages are marked as read if you change focus away from the Messages app within Teams.\n\n3. Approval to send native notifications is not requested at first run. It is requested at the first attempt at native notification delivery.\n\n4. The macOS client sometimes receives messages that are marked as read immediatly without a notification.\n\n5. There is an unknown upper bound to the length of message that you can receive via SMS. Messages are truncated to 40ish words.\n\n6. Messages FROM a tester via Messages app WERE DELIVERED, but marked as \"Failed to send\" on both sides of the conversation.\n\n![[2021.07.20 - Failed to Send, but was Received 1of2.png]]\n![[2021.07.20 - Failed to Send, but was Received 2of2.png]]\n\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2021.09.21 - Asked for access to DCL due to fire panel notification","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidi