ity Professional Conference 2009 25226e34d3734137a07cfb75f8693d6e","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/30 - Social/33 - Travel & Events/2009 EDUCAUSE Security Professional Conference 2009 25226e34d3734137a07cfb75f8693d6e.md","lastModified":"2023-10-30T23:49:50.000Z","tags":["#8212"],"content":"# 2009 EDUCAUSE Security Professional Conference 2009 25226e34d3734137a07cfb75f8693d6e\n\n**Tuesday April 21st**\n\n**10:45 - Corporate and Campus Solutions: Deploying Tools for Cleaning Personal Information**\n\n- Identity Finder - Allow PII discovery and remediation ability to distributed environment. \"Power to the people!\"\n- Central Monitoring Console\n- Client Software required. Can be customized to be a \"quiet install\". Penn chose to have some _not_ report back to central monitoring system so as not to be \"big brother\".\n\n**1:00 - Management and Operations: Building a Cybersecurity Operations Center**\n\n- Purdue - Greg Hedrick\n    - Incident Response\n        - Lookup: RTIR [http://bestpractical.com/rtir/](http://bestpractical.com/rtir/) ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Network Monitoring\n        - Weather Map ✅ 2023-01-06\n        - Cacti ✅ 2023-01-06\n- Penn State - Cathy Kimble\n    - Distributed Snort Sensors\n        - Sourcefire\n        - Emerging Threat\n        - prevx.com\n        - threatexpert.com\n    - Numera Footprints (Like RTIR)\n    - Find PII - Proventsure\n- VaTech - Randy Marchany\n    - \"SOC\" name is being taken over by physical security. Now calling it a CyberSOC or CSOC.\n    - Hackers are using IPv6 for command and control now b/c usually not supported by security products\n    - Pull the data from throughout IT and analyze it. It is already being collected.\n    - Their metrics work matches the EDUCAUSE Metrics work that is being done\n    - Acunetix\n    - \"Security Operation Center Concepts & Implementation by Renauld Bidou\" ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - They have a drillable map of servers and services so they can see where concentrations of MySQL for example are physically on campus.\n\n**3:15 - Policy and Compliance: Integrating FISMA and NIST into .edu (or Play NISTy for Me)**\n\n- Speaker is at 300+ mph not enough caffeine to follow\n- 800-37, 15 & 53\n\n**Wednesday April 22nd (Earth Day!)**\n\n**8:30 - Technology - Advanced\\: Improving Security Event Correlation and Analysis Using Intelligent Agents**\n\nTowson - Lynn Ray, CISO\n\nSnare Agent\n\nEpilog Agent\n\nImperva Agent\n\nFeed back to SEM (Cisco Mars)\n\n514/UDP (syslog?) Not Secure! Need to move sensitive logs over secure channel.\n\n**9:45 - Technology - Advanced\\: REN-ISAC and CSI2&#8212;The Security Event System**\n\nwes young\n\nTammy - Argon National Labs\n\nGet away from human language processing and into machine distributable. Human out of the loop.\n\nAutomated detection and response\n\n\"Virtual Neighborhood Watch\"\n\nStandards based XML IETF\n\n[https://secure.ren-isac.net/dokuwiki/doku.php?id=start:ses](https://secure.ren-isac.net/dokuwiki/doku.php?id=start:ses)\n\n[https://code.ren-isac.net/trac/ses](https://code.ren-isac.net/trac/ses)\n\n- Lookup MLATS? Law Enforcement negotiations with other countries. ✅ 2023-01-06\n\n**11:00 - General Session\\: Practical Experiences of a Chief Security Officer**\n\n**12:00 - Postconference Seminar\\: REN-ISAC Member Meeting**\n\n- Doug Pearson\n    - Read the new Information Sharing Model ✅ 2023-01-06\n- Bill Terry - Executive Advisory Group\n- Randy Raw (MORENet) - Technical Advisory Group\n- Brian - R-I MAT\n    - ✅ 2023-01-06\n\n        Smart Network Data Services SNDS and **Junk eMail Reporting Program (JERP) (https://secure.ren-isac.net/dokuwiki/doku.php?id=start:mat)**\n\n- Ken Connelly - Membership Committee\n- Beth ?? (MORENet)\n    - Nepenthes (feed to MORENet)\n    - Anubis (feed to MORENet)\n    - SES (feed _from_ MORENet)\n- Presentation from IT-ISAC\n    - Nick Bradley\n    - Mike\n- SPAM\n    - If a user chooses to forward. Their mail is aggressively processed outbound\n    - Establish breaks or alerts at 1000/5000 messages outbound per day\n    - Push off Red Flags to the business unit. They need to define their business process.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Figure out Folder Note Templates","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Figure out Folder Note Templates.md","lastModified":"2023-10-30T23:49:41.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Figure out Folder Note Templates\n- Look at [[Bibliography]] for Folder Note example.\n\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Employee Onboarding 7d0ef4e2d8a74c8091d9e56ad5df64f5","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Procedures/Employee Onboarding 7d0ef4e2d8a74c8091d9e56ad5df64f5.md","lastModified":"2023-10-30T23:47:44.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Employee Onboarding 7d0ef4e2d8a74c8091d9e56ad5df64f5\n\n- Before First Day\n    - Create Onboarding Agenda ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Designate an onboarding buddy ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Send Welcome Letter with Onboarding Agenda ✅ 2023-01-06\n- Welcome meeting agenda\n\n    What's your name?\n\n    Diana will help you to get setup\n\n    Introduce to Onboarding Buddy\n\n    Normal schedule 8-5 M-F, 24x7x365 for Critical Security Incident Response\n\n    Our reoccurring meetings are: 1on1s, Weekly FTEs, Monthly All-hands, and Monthly Social Outing\n\n    GGC's Administrative Policy Manual is at http://catalog.ggc.edu\n\n    You will have a Benefits and Policy Orientation soon\n\n- First Week\n    - Is your computer working? Any issues with it? ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Have you setup Direct Deposit? ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Setup VPN ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Setup MS Authenticator App for MFA ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Do you have access to OneUSG Connect? ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Did you get your phone? ✅ 2023-01-06\n- Task\n    - Set calendar reminder for the end of the 6 month probationary period ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Schedule meetings with each of the people that new employee should know ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Schedule Quarterly Performance Review Meetings (at the end of every quarter in the second week of the last month) ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Setup \"??? @ GGC\" in Contacts with Anniversary Date ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - ???, are you happy here? ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - ???, how do you think that your work here helps to progress your career goals? ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - ???, what do I do that wastes your time without contributing to your effectiveness? ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - ???, your quarterly performance review is coming up. Please review your goals. ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - ???, your work anniversary is XXX. Can I buy you lunch and do a Stay Interview? (see notes) ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Account Provisioning ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Request Badge Access via clawcard@ggc.edu ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Request GGC AD Admin Account (see sub tasks) ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Invite to USG Slack ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Request Access to USG ServiceNow ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Grant access to SecureWorks ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Request Access to GGC Helpdesk ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Request Access to PaloAltos ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Grant Access to Qualys ✅ 2023-01-06\n    - Request Access to MS Team ✅ 2023-01-06","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Lightweight Decisions","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/40 - Hobbies/41 - Outdoors/41.01 - Backpacking/Lightweight Decisions.md","lastModified":"2023-10-30T22:53:41.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Lightweight Decisions \n\n- Don't bring the PackTowel. Use your bandana instead.\n- Cut the tubing off of your cookpot. It was a failed experiment.\n- Weight your titanium spoon against the lexan and corn plastic ones. Take the lightest\n- Sell (?) the SOL Emergency Bivy and use a regular Mylar blanket instead. ✅ 2023-01-06\n- Use sandwich bag for First aid and Survival\n- Put an extra Swiss Army Classic into survival","bookmarked":false},{"title":"81.17 - GGC Tracy","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/80 - GGC/81 - GGC Teams/81.17 - GGC Tracy/81.17 - GGC Tracy.md","lastModified":"2023-10-30T13:21:58