Lists/_Unstructured_/GGC IS&S SCRUM.md","lastModified":"2023-10-20T11:35:21.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# GGC IS&S SCRUM\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Christopher Rosbury","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Christopher Rosbury.md","lastModified":"2023-10-20T11:29:58.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Christopher Rosbury\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"15 ITSM ITIL Metrics for Incident & Service Management Success","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/15 ITSM ITIL Metrics for Incident & Service Management Success.md","lastModified":"2023-10-19T22:37:27.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 15 ITSM ITIL Metrics for Incident & Service Management Success\n\n[15 ITSM ITIL Metrics for Incident & Service Management Success](https://orangematter.solarwinds.com/2019/05/09/15-itsm-itil-metrics-for-tracking-incident-management-success/)\n\n## The 4 Most Interesting Ones:\n\n2. **First-Touch Resolution Rate** - First-touch resolution rate is the percentage of incidents resolved the first time, with no repeat calls.\n\n_Why it's a good ITSM KPI metric to track:_ High first-time incident resolution correlates with greater customer satisfaction and is a good sign of incident management maturity.\n\n3. **SLA Compliance Ratio** - This ratio is the number of resolutions needed to fulfill service level agreement (SLA) guidelines related to response time, workflow prioritization, cost, and other metrics.\n\n_Why it's a good ITSM KPI metric to track:_ A high SLA compliance ratio helps ensure you meet obligations without unnecessary loss of productivity or revenue opportunities.\n\n9. **Incidents by Type** - This metric represents the number of incidents categorized by the affected device or application. By identifying the most troublesome devices and software, you can partner with each vendor as needed or consider other alternatives.\n\n_Why it's a good ITSM KPI metric to track:_ Tracking incident types can allow you to allocate your agents based on their skillsets to make decisions about training. [Encouraging employees to submit service requests via the service portal](https://orangematter.solarwinds.com/2018/02/06/self-service-portal-three-ways-to-increase-employee-adoption/) can help facilitate more accurate data collection when it comes to categories and subcategories, which makes this metric even more beneficial.\n\n12. **Escalated Incidents -** Escalated incidents are the total number of incidents resolved by Level 2 or 3 team members.\n\n_Why it's a good ITSM KPI metric to track:_ An increase could suggest skills gaps for front-line team members. An uptick in escalated incidents may also indicate a need to increase the depth of your [service catalog by creating workflows](https://orangematter.solarwinds.com/2018/07/12/how-to-build-service-catalog-workflow/) for those types of complex requests.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP).md","lastModified":"2023-10-19T13:42:51.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP)\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2023-10-14 - Saturday","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Journal/2023/2023-10-14 - Saturday.md","lastModified":"2023-10-18T12:34:33.892Z","tags":[],"content":"---\ndate: 2023-10-14\nweek: \"[[2023-W41]]\"\nmonth: \"[[2023-10 - October]]\"\ntags:\n---\n# 2023-10-14 - Saturday\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Data System Criticality Questions","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Data System Criticality Questions.md","lastModified":"2023-10-17T19:23:36.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Data System Criticality Questions\n\n1. Does this system contain sensitive information? Would a breach subject the College to significant liability or reputational risk?\n   \n2. Would a failure or unavailability of this system have a major impact on campus operations?Would the Colle