]\njump:: [[2023-W40]]\n\n\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Amanda Thomas","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Amanda Thomas.md","lastModified":"2023-10-10T17:48:36.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Amanda Thomas\n\n[[H&R Block]] at [[Mall of Georgia]].\nHelped with [[2022 Sluder Taxes]].\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"H&R Block","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Companies/H&R Block.md","lastModified":"2023-10-10T17:18:21.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# H&R Block\n\n[[Amanda Thomas]] at [[Mall of Georgia]]\n\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2022 Sluder Taxes","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/2022 Sluder Taxes.md","lastModified":"2023-10-10T17:18:21.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2022 Sluder Taxes\n\nPaid [[H&R Block]] online for extension to [[2023-10-15 - Sunday]]\n\n[[2023-10-06 - Friday]] visited [[H&R Block]] and spoke to [[Amanda Thomas]]\n\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Mall of Georgia","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Mall of Georgia.md","lastModified":"2023-10-10T16:28:46.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Mall of Georgia\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Raven Cliff Falls","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Trails/Raven Cliff Falls.md","lastModified":"2023-10-10T15:38:57.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Raven Cliff Falls\n\n## USFS\n[Chattahoochee-Oconee National Forest - Raven Cliffs Trailhead](https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/conf/recarea/?recid=10515)\n\n## AllTrails\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/trail/us/georgia/raven-cliff-falls-trail?sh=cexeft\n\n## GaiaGPS\n![[Raven Cliff Falls Trail.pdf]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"NIST Guidance on Maximum Password Age","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Ideas/NIST Guidance on Maximum Password Age.md","lastModified":"2023-10-10T15:36:31.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# NIST Guidance on Maximum Password Age\n\n[[NIST Special Publication 800-63B - Digital Identity Guidelines]]\n  \nSection 5.1.1.2 paragraph 9 states:  \n  \n“Verifiers SHOULD NOT require memorized secrets to be changed arbitrarily (e.g., periodically). However, verifiers SHALL force a change if there is evidence of compromise of the authenticator.”  \n  \nUsers tend to choose weaker memorized secrets when they know that they will have to change them in the near future. When those changes do occur, they often select a secret that is similar to their old memorized secret by applying a set of common transformations such as increasing a number in the password. This practice provides a false sense of security if any of the previous secrets has been compromised since attackers can apply these same common transformations. But if there is evidence that the memorized secret has been compromised, such as by a breach of the verifier’s hashed password database or observed fraudulent activity, subscribers should be required to change their memorized secrets. However, this event-based change should occur rarely, so that they are less motivated to choose a weak secret with the knowledge that it will only be used for a limited period of time.\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"ISC^2","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Companies/ISC^2.md","lastModified":"2023-10-10T15:34:04.816Z","tags":[],"content":"# ISC^2\n\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Certifications","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/Certifications.md","lastModified":"2023-10-10T15:33:02.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Certifications\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Pescitelli","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Families/Pescitelli.md","lastModified":"2023-10-10T15:30:45.056Z","tags":[],"content":"# Pescitelli\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Mass Psychosis","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Index/Mass Psychosis.md","lastModified":"2023-10-10T14:44:22.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Mass Psychosis\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"After Skool","path":"/Users