ergent - Hoover's Online","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2023-09-07 - Pack 503 Round-up at Dacula EMS","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Journal/_Calendar_/2023-09-07 - Pack 503 Round-up at Dacula EMS.md","lastModified":"2023-09-08T15:24:32.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2023-09-07 - Pack 503 Round-up at Dacula EMS\n\n![[IMG_0425.jpeg]]\n![[IMG_0426.jpeg]]\n![[IMG_0427.jpeg]]\n![[IMG_0428.jpeg]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2023 GGC Performance Goals","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Performance Management/_Forms & Templates/2023/2023 GGC Performance Goals.md","lastModified":"2023-09-01T17:31:19.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2023 GGC Performance Goals\n- Charles\n\t- Update security incident response plan and convene CSIRT\n\t      **Description** : I believe USG is asking all campuses to update security incident response plans; this is also mentioned in our GLBA action items. The CSIRT needs to be planned, convened, and trained.\n\t- Update cybersecurity program plan\n\t      **Description** : USG is also asking campuses for updated cybersecurity program plans.\n\t- Enhance email protection\n\t      **Description** : Prevent, detect, and respond to email-based cyberattacks.\n\t- Conduct infrastructure review\n\t      **Description** : Include VmWare, storage/backup, and DNS\n\t- Continue coaching team to adopt high-level goals\n\t   .   **Description** :\n\t\t- Providing proactive, preventive, and complete solutions whenever possible\n\t\t- Planning for user experience as part of technology projects/changes\n\t\t- Considering business needs/impact as art of technology projects/changes\n\t\t- Professional communication and responsiveness\n\t\t- Help ensure we close the loop on service requests|\n\t- Continue developing trusted partnerships inside and outside\n\t       **Description** : Being perceived as a trusted partner is essentail to success in security officer role at GGC. Apply concepts from Speed of Trust.\n- Mohammed\n\t- Decommission Windows Server 2012 Domain Controllers\n\t- Upgrade Exagrid and Veeam Backup Systems\n\t- Renew all SSL Certificates for all SSO and HTTPS Services\n\t- Complete VMWare Consolidation\n- Chris\n\t- Storage Replacement\n\t- DNR Migration\n\t- O365 Security Assessment\n\t- Mimecast Warrior Certification\n- Jessica\n\t- Complete Microsoft Student Data Sync (SDS) Implementation\n\t- Upgrade and Maintain Account Onboarding Script and Process\n\t- Complete Account Cleanup of Primary Affiliation Types\n- Blake\n\t- Add Valid DNS Auth (SPF, DMARC, & DKIM) Records for Services\n\t- Complete External DNS Record Clean-up w/ Git Commit History\n\t- Clean-up Old & Unused Email Distribution Groups\n- Daniel\n\t- Write Security Operations Runbooks for 5 Most Common Alerts\n\t- Disable Unnecessary Anti-SPAM Rules\n\t- Set Outbound Email Sending Limit per Account\n\t- Fix Recommended Security Items in O365 Security Assessment\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"T5109 - Tent Selection","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_Unstructured_/T5109 - Tent Selection.md","lastModified":"2023-09-01T16:47:08.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# T5109 - Tent Selection\n\n## Tent Proposals\n[Tent Proposals - Google Sheets](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/138zxwJFcb0Nm1fqnhhar8kN9pa_hkvknYjOHnHAoz38/edit?usp=sharing)\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"88.49 - 1Password","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/ITSM/GGC IT Services/88.49 - 1Password/88.49 - 1Password.md","lastModified":"2023-09-01T13:54:14.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 88.49 - 1Password","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Backpacking Merit Badge","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Scouting/BSA/Scouts BSA/Merit Badges/Backpacking Merit Badge/Backpacking Merit Badge.md","lastModified":"2023-08-31T16:52:28.000Z","tags":[],"content":"up:: [[Merit Badges]]\ndown:: \njumps:: \n\n# Backpacking Merit Badge\n## Related Links\n[Backpacking Merit Badge | Boy Scouts of America](https://www.scouting.org/merit-badges/backpacking/)\n[[Potential 3-day and 5-day Backpacking Dates]]\n[[Backpacking Trip Plan.docx]]\n\n## Requirements\n1. Discuss the prevention of and treatment for the health concerns that could occur while backpacking, including hypothermia, heat reactions, frostbite, dehydration, insect stings, tick bites, snakebite, and blisters.\n2. Do the following:\n    1. List 10 items that are essential to be carried on any backpacking trek and explain why each item is necessary.\n    2. Describe 10 ways you can limit the weight and bulk to be carried in your pack without jeopardizing your health or safety.\n3. Do the following:\n    1. Define limits on the number of backpackers appropriate for a trek crew.\n    2. Describe how a trek crew should be organized.\n    3. Tell how you would minimize risk on a backpacking trek.\n    4. Explain the purpose of an emergency response plan.\n4. Do the following:\n    1. Describe the importance of using Leave No Trace principles while backpacking, and at least five ways you can lessen the crew’s impact on the environment. \n    2. Describe proper methods of handling human and other wastes while on a backpacking trek. Describe the importance of and means to assure personal cleanliness while on a backpacking trek.\n    3. Tell what factors are important in choosing a campsite.\n5. Do the following:\n    1. Demonstrate two ways to treat water and tell why water treatment is essential. \n    2. Explain to your counselor the importance of staying well hydrated during a trek.\n6. Do the following:\n    1. Demonstrate that you can read topographic maps. \n    2. While on a trek, use a map and compass to establish your position on the ground at three different locations, OR use a GPS receiver to establish your position on a topographic map and on the ground at three different locations.\n    3. Explain how to stay found, and what to do if you get lost.\n7. Tell how to prepare properly for and deal with inclement weather.\n8. Do the following:\n    1. Explain the advantages and disadvantages of the different types of backpacking stoves using at least three different types of fuel.\n    2. Demonstrate that you know how to operate a backpacking stove safely and to handle liquid fuel safely.\n    3. Prepare at least three meals using a stove and fuel you can carry in a backpack.\n    4. Demonstrate that you know how to keep cooking and eating gear clean and sanitary , and that you practice proper methods for food storage while on a backpacking trek.\n9. Do the following:\n    1. Write a plan that includes a schedule for a patrol/crew backpacking hike of at least 2 miles.\n    2. Conduct a prehike inspection of the patrol and its equipment.\n    3. Show that you know how to properly pack your personal gear and your share of the crew’s gear and food. \n    4. Show you can properly shoulder your pack and adjust it for proper wear.\n    5. While using the plan you developed for requirement 9a, carry your fully loaded pack to complete a hike of at least 2 miles.\n10. Using Leave No Trace principles, participate in at least three backpacking treks of at least three days each and at least 15 miles each, and using at least two different campsites on each trek. Carry everything you will need throughout the trek.\n11. Do the following:\n    1. Write a plan for a backpacking trek of at least five days using at least three different campsites and covering at least 30 miles. Your plan must include a description of and route to the trek area, a schedule (including a daily schedule), a list of food and equipment needs, a safety and emergency plan, and a budget. \n    2. Using Leave No Trace principles, take the trek you have planned and, while on the trek, complete at least one service project approved by your merit badge counselor.\n    3. Keep a daily journal during the trek that includes a day-by-day description of your activities, including notes about what worked well and thoughts about improvements that could be made for the next trek.\n## Articles\n- [Pack light, pack right on your next backpacking trip](https://scoutingmagazine.org/2018/08/pack-light-pack-right-on-your-next-backpacking-trip/)\n- [Scout Outdoor Essentials Checklist – Scout Life magazine](https://scoutlife.org/outdoors/outdoorarticles/6976/scout-outdoor-essentials-checklist/)\n\n## Files\n### Backpacking Trek Planning Workbook\n![[Backpacking Trip Plan.docx]]\n### USScouts.org - Backpacking Merit Badge Workbook\n![[Backpacking-Workbook.pdf]]\n\n### Full Pamphlet 2009 (OLD)\n![[Backpacking Merit Badge Pamphlet 2035863.pdf]]\n\nPamphlet Overview\n![[Backpacking.pdf]]\n![[tripplan.pdf]]\n![[emergencyresponseplan.pdf]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"83.08.00 - Purchasing Strategy","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Purchasing/83.08 - Purchasing/83.08.00 - Purchasing Strategy/83.08.00 - Purchasing Strategy.md","lastModified":"2023-08-28T16:48:38.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 83.08.00 - Purchasing Strategy\n \n\n \n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2023-08-23 - IS&S Project Roadmap","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Journal/_Calendar_/2023-08-23 - IS&S Project Roadmap.md","lastModified":"2023-08-26T14:21:01.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2023-08-23 - IS&S Project Roadmap\n![[2023-08-23 - IS&S Project Roadmap.jpg]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2023-06-06 - Tuesday","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Journal/_Calendar_/2023-06-06 - Tuesday.md","lastModified":"2023-08-23T12:46:38.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2023-06-06 - Tuesday\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"83.10.05 - Dell","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Vendor Management/83.10.05 - Dell/83.10.05 - Dell.md","lastModified":"2023-08-23T12:23:20.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 83.10.05 - Dell","bookmarked":false},{"title":"83.10.04 - Mimecast","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Vendor Management/83.10.04 - Mimecast/83.10.04 