te another person will receive a refund less a $300 processing fee if notification is submitted in writing via a completed [Black Hat Registration Update Form](http://www.blackhat.com/docs/us-14/blackhat-reg-form.pdf) on or before June 30, 2014. All Fees are non-refundable after June 30, 2014.\n• Request for Taxpayer ID Number: Please email your W-9 requests to [blackhatregistration@ubm.com](mailto:blackhatregistration@ubm.com). The Federal Tax ID number for Black Hat USA 2014 is 11-2240940.\n• If a Letter of Invitation is needed for a visa, please contact the Black Hat Registration Team. The Letter of Invitation will only be issued to registrants with paid Briefings and/or Training records.\n• Registration fees are per item. There is a separate line item cost for each Training course.\n• DO NOT register twice if you have registered for either the Briefings or the Training and would like to add an item. Use the Black Hat Registration Update Form to make additions to your existing registration. Duplicate registrations for the same person will result in delays at the time you pick up your credentials at the show or a cancellation of all orders from the same person. Black Hat reserves the right to cancel your duplicate, unpaid registrations without notice.\n• Black Hat reserves the right to cancel your unpaid registration after June 30, 2014. Registrations and training seats are only guaranteed once they are paid in full.\n• Registration fees do not include travel, lodging or parking validation. All delegates are responsible for making their own arrangements and any associated fees.\n• Age Limit - Due to safety concerns, no one under the age of 18 (including infants in strollers) will be permitted on the premise at any time during Black Hat USA 2014.\n• If you have a disability and require special assistance, please contact the operations manager at [cassandra.reyes-jones@ubm.com](mailto:cassandra.reyes-jones@ubm.com) by June 20th, 2014.\n•Near Field Communication badges will be in use at Black Hat USA 2014.**Badges:**\nAll persons on the conference floor must have a badge visible on their person at all times. Spouses, friends, peers, etc. are not granted access to the show floor without a badge. If you wish for them to accompany you to any of the conference events including meals, reception, breaks or sessions, you must register them and pay the appropriate fees. Lost, misplaced, stolen, or forgotten badges will incur a replacement fee equal to the original purchase amount of your pass. If your badge was complimentary, the fee will be the current, on-site rate.\nBlack Hat believes our community should be open for everyone. As such, we are committed to providing a friendly, safe and welcoming environment. By participating you agree to abide by the Code of Conduct which can be viewed at [http://blackhat.com/code-of-conduct.html](http://blackhat.com/code-of-conduct.html)**Attendee & Business Hall Registration Hours:**\nDiamond Cutout - Second Floor Lobby: Mandalay Bay Convention Center\nMandalay Bay Convention Center\n3950 S Las Vegas Blvd\nLas Vegas, NV 89119\nFriday, August 1 – 17:00-20:00 (First Floor Lobby)\nSaturday, August 2 – 07:00-16:00 (First Floor Lobby)\nSunday, August 3 – 08:00-18:00 (Second Floor Lobby)\nMonday, August 4 – 07:30-17:00\nTuesday, August 5 – 08:00-20:00\nWednesday, August 6 – 07:00-19:00\nThursday, August 7 – 08:30-17:00**Training Course Hours**\nSaturday, August 2 – 10:00-18:00\nSunday, August 3 – 09:00-18:00\nMonday, August 4 – 09:00-18:00\nTuesday, August 5 – 09:00-18:00**Briefings Hours**\nWednesday, August 6 – 09:00-18:00\nThursday, August 7 – 09:00-18:00**Business Hall Hours**\nWednesday, August 6 – 10:00-19:00\nThursday, August 7 – 10:00-17:00**Hotel Info:**\nPlease visit [www.blackhathotels.com](http://www.blackhathotels.com/) to book your hotel through our partner, Convention Housing Partners (CHP), the official housing company for Black Hat USA. We encourage you to secure your room(s) early for best selection and availability.\nLinks:\nNeed to access your registration? Login [here](https://blackhat.tech.ubm.com/usa/2014/) to review your information or make changes.[Registration Terms & Conditions](https://www.blackhat.com/us-14/registration-terms.html)[Black Hat USA](http://www.blackhat.com/us-14/)[Privacy Policy](http://legal.us.ubm.com/privacy-policy/)\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \t\t\t   \t\t\t \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBlack Hat c/o UBM Tech\n303 Second St., Suite 900 South Tower, San Francisco, CA 94107.\nPlease do not reply to this message as responses are not monitored.\n© UBM Tech 2014. All Rights Reserved. [Privacy Policy](http://legal.us.ubm.com/privacy-n[Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled](_Backlog/TheCollective-OLD/NotionExport/Inbox%20a37842c662624921b6a0b5a70b4c76a5/Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled)82[Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled%201](_Backlog/TheCollective-OLD/NotionExport/Inbox%20a37842c662624921b6a0b5a70b4c76a5/Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled%201)0d[Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled%202](_Backlog/TheCollective-OLD/NotionExport/Inbox%20a37842c662624921b6a0b5a70b4c76a5/Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled%202)0d[Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled%203](_Backlog/TheCollective-OLD/NotionExport/Inbox%20a37842c662624921b6a0b5a70b4c76a5/Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled%203)0d[Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled%204](_Backlog/TheCollective-OLD/NotionExport/Inbox%20a37842c662624921b6a0b5a70b4c76a5/Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled%204)0d[Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled%205](_Backlog/TheCollective-OLD/NotionExport/Inbox%20a37842c662624921b6a0b5a70b4c76a5/Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/untitled%205)0d[smime.p7s](_Backlog/TheCollective-OLD/NotionExport/Inbox%20a37842c662624921b6a0b5a70b4c76a5/Black%20Hat%20USA%202014%20Registration%20Invoice%205fe9854ef82240da950fb6ca88c447ba/smime.p7s)2240da950fb6ca88c447ba/smime.p7s)","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Birthday Paradox","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Oddities/Birthday Paradox.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T17:16:30.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Birthday Paradox \n\nThe name is based on fact that in a room with 23 people or more, the odds are greater than 50% that two will share the same birthday\n\nIf you are in a room full of 23 people, you have a 1 in 365 chance of sharing a birthday with each of the 22 other people in the room, for a total of 22/365 chances.\n\nIf you fail to match, you leave the room and Joe has a 21/365 chance of sharing a birthday with the remaining people.\n\nIf Joe fails to match, he leaves the room and Morgan has a 20/365 chance, and so on.\n\nIf you add 22/365 + 21/365 + 20/365 + 19/365 … + 1/365, you pass 50% probability.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Ren and Stimpy","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/TV Shows/Ren and Stimpy.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T17:11:34.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Ren and Stimpy ","bookmarked":false},{"title":"CHL's Ultralight Backpacking Primer","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/40 - Hobbies/41 - Outdoors/41.01 - Backpacking/CHL's Ultralight Backpacking Primer.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T17:09:50.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# CHL's Ultralight Backpacking Primer\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1AXzjCfJ4P9w8in3DJMsefvwgs_4RBT3j9IJfpcOXNIs/edit](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1AXzjCfJ4P9w8in3DJMsefvwgs_4RBT3j9IJfpcOXNIs/edit)","bookmarked":false},{"title":"ultralight backpackin' tips caramelized onion sauce","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/40 - Hobbies/41 - Outdoors/41.01 - Backpacking/Meals/ultralight backpackin' tips caramelized onion sauce.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T17:08:41.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# ultralight backpackin' tips caramelized onion sauce\n# caramelized onion sauce\n\nThis is a recipe that is NOT included in the book, but it's heart wrenchingly wonderful. I'm adding it here to this blog as a way to share the love!\n\n**CARAMELIZED ONION SAUCE**\n\n3 yellow onions (finely chopped)5 cloves of garlic (finely chopped)1 red pepper (finely chopped)4 oz olive oil2 oz peanut oil (or any high heat oil)1 oz soy sauce1 oz hot saucetablespoon tahinitea spoon salttea spoon pepperdash of vinegardash of sugar\n\n(all weights above are measures, not weight)\n\nStart by cooking the finely chopped onions in a large skillet on low heat with the peanut oil. Stir frequently for approximately 20 minutes, until the onions are caramelized and brown.Add the finely chopped garlic and red pepper let cook approximately 10 minutes.Add the soy sauce, hot sauce, salt, pepper, vinegar and sugar. Let this cook another 10 minutes or so. The stuff in your pan should be brown and gooey.Take off the heat and let cool for a few minutes.Put the warm concoction in a blender or food processor with the olive oil and tahini. Blend until smooth.You will now have a brown flavor packed sauce that can be added to your camping meals. Carry it in a small lightweight plastic bootle. Approx. 2 ounces\n\n(in weight)\n\nper person per meal will bring tears of joy at dinner time.\n\n**PLEASE NOTE:**\n\nI'm a cook that ignores recipes, I pretty much just wing it in the kitchen. I encourage anyone reading this to get creative and tweak the above recipe to meet their own needs, and to match whatever you might have on hand in your pantry!\n\nBon Appetit!","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Steven Richardson (N4STR)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Steven Richardson (N4STR).md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T17:07:07.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Steven Richardson (N4STR)\n\nCreated: Mar 15, 2016 5:15 PM\n\n### **Richardson, Steven T, N4STR**\n\n920 Harbins View Dr\nDacula, GA 30019\nPrevious call sign: KJ4STR\nPrevious license class: Technician\nLicensee ID: L00583938\nLicense Class: General\nFRN: 0007826522\nRadio Service: HV\nIssue Date: 06/25/2010\nExpire Date: 06/25/2020\n\nDate of Last Change: 06/26/2010 (Administrative Update Applied)\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"n","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/40 - Hobbies/42 - Radio/Ham/Hams/n.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T17:06:09.119Z","tags":[],"content":"#  n\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"American Horror Story","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/TV Shows/American Horror Story.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:59:19.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# American Horror Story \n\n![http://profile.ak.fbcdn.net/static-ak/rsrc.php/v1/yf/r/vd1WlANxPY9.png](http://profile.ak.fbcdn.net/static-ak/rsrc.php/v1/yf/r/vd1WlANxPY9.png)\n\nPlot An example of the type of fear and mystery follow in the American Horror Story, Nip / Tuck creator Ryan Murphy and Glee'nin a project started. Do not have very detailed information about the series, the mystery seems to protect Until the publication of the pilot episode. ... How powerful, though, the therapist, I actually have a structure sensitive Harmon, fragile wife, Vivien, and 16-year-old daughter, Violet; backgrounds of some painful experiences in order to forget a little bit though, moved from Boston to Los Angeles. Violet, 17-year-old seductive but dangerous at the same time establishes a friendship with one of the Goth. Names on the back of both strong, both the cast, as well as photos and teasers released so far, with the curiosity of the viewer-watering American Horror Story, starred, Connie Britton, Dylan McDermott, Jessica Lange, Denis O'Hare, and there we saw last season Blood'da True. American Horror Story, part of the pilot to be shown on October 5 FX'de.\n\nCast Dylan McDermott as Dr. Benjamin \"Ben\" Harmon Connie Britton as Vivien Harmon Evan Peters as Tate Langdon Taissa Farmiga as Violet Harmon Denis O'Hare as Larry Harvey Jessica Lange as Constance\n\nDescription American Horror Story Es una serie televisiva de horror-drama creada y producida por Ryan Murphy y Brad Falchuk. La serie se centra en la familia Harmon, que se muda de Boston a Los Ángeles; fue estrenada el 5 de octubre del 2011 y fue transmitida por FX en los Estados Unidos.SinopsisHistoria estadounidense de terror que sigue a la familia Harmon: Ben (Dylan McDermott), Vivien (Connie Britton) y Violet (Taissa Farmiga), que se trasladan de Boston a Los Ángeles después de que Vivien de a luz a un bebé muerto y Ben tenga un romance con una de sus estudiantes. La familia se muda a una mansión restaurada, sin saber que la casa está encantada, donde Ben y Vivien tratan de reavivar su relación, mientras que Violet sufre una depresión. Esta familia se enfrentará a distintos problemas y horrores que viven en la casa.RepartoPrincipal Dylan McDermott como Dr. Benjamin \"Ben\" Harmon Connie Britton como Vivien Harmon Evan Peters como Tate Langdon Taissa Farmiga como Violet Harmon Denis O'Hare como Larry Harvey Jessica Lange como Constance\n\nWriters Various\n\nDirectors Various","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Sawnee Mountain","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/40 - Hobbies/41 - Outdoors/Maps/Sawnee Mountain/Sawnee Mountain.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:57:39.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Sawnee Mountain\n\n![[ae3094_ee89d34cb42f984b85ce7a20622a187f.pdf]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Panthertown Valley","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/40 - Hobbies/41 - Outdoors/Maps/Panthertown Valley/Panthertown Valley.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:52:08.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Panthertown Valley\n\n![[panthertownlatest_june22_0911x17_usemap.pdf]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"GaTech Pi Mile","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Fun/GaTech Pi Mile/GaTech Pi Mile.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:42:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# GaTech Pi Mile\n\n![[pimile_map.pdf]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Shipping Alcohol Fuel via USPS Ground (only)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Backpacking Tips/Shipping Alcohol Fuel via USPS Ground (only).md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:40:39.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Shipping Alcohol Fuel via USPS Ground (only) \n\n[http://pe.usps.com/text/pub52/pub52c3_020.htm](http://pe.usps.com/text/pub52/pub52c3_020.htm)\n\n343.2 Mailability and Packaging 343.21 Requirements for Flammable Liquids a. … b. ... c. Domestic Mail via Surface Transportation. Flammable liquid with a flashpoint of 20° F (–7° C) or below is prohibited. Other flammable liquid is permitted if the material can qualify as an ORM–D material and meet the criteria in Exhibit 343.21. A mailable flammable liquid must be prepared according to Packaging Instruction 3A in Appendix C, as applicable.\n\n“ORM-D” is basically \"limited quantity consumer commodity\"\n\nHere’s the Packaging Instruction 3A:\n\n[http://pe.usps.com/text/pub52/pub52apxc_010.htm](http://pe.usps.com/text/pub52/pub52apxc_010.htm)\n\nTL;DR\n\nIt looks like you can ship up to 1 quart of alcohol fuel (in a metal screw top container) per package.\n\n[[41.01 - Backpacking]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"41.01 - Backpacking","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/40 - Hobbies/41 - Outdoors/41.01 - Backpacking/41.01 - Backpacking.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:40:39.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 41.01 - Backpacking\n\n## Smoky Mountains\n[[Fontana Dam]]\n[[Clingman’s Dome]]\n[[Lakeview Drive]]\n[[Road to Nowhere ]]\n[[Fortney Creek Trail]]\n[[Jonas Creek Trail]]\n[[Welch Ridge Trail]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Potato Casserole","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Recipes/Potato Casserole.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:22:30.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Potato Casserole \n\nSauté onions in 1/2 cup butter.\tAdd 1 can cream of chicken soup and 16 oz sour cream.\tAdd 1 pkg frozen hash browns and\n\n2 cups shredded cheddar cheese.\n\nBake 350 for about 45 mins","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Pretzel Rolls","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Recipes/Pretzel Rolls.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:18:44.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Pretzel Rolls \n\nIngredients\n\n- 2 3/4 cups bread flour\n- 1 envelope quick-rising yeast\n- 1 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon sugar\n- 1 teaspoon celery seeds\n- 1 cup plus 2 tablespoons (about) hot water (125°F to 130°F)Cornmeal 8 cups water\n- 1/4 cup baking soda\n- 2 tablespoons sugar\n- 1 egg white, beaten to blend (glaze)\n- Coarse salt\n\nDirections\n\n1. Combine bread flour, 1 envelope yeast, 1 teaspoon salt, 1 teaspoon sugar and celery seeds in food processor and blend.\n2. With machine running, gradually pour hot water through feed tube, adding enough water to form smooth elastic dough.\n3. Process 1 minute to knead. Grease medium bowl.\n4. Add dough to bowl, turning to coat.\n5. Cover bowl with plastic wrap, then towel; let dough rise in warm draft-free area until doubled in volume, about 35 minutes.\n6. Flour baking sheet.\n7. Punch dough down and knead on lightly floured surface until smooth.\n8. Divide into 8 pieces.\n9. Form each dough piece into ball.\n10. Place dough balls on prepared sheet, flattening each slightly.\n11. Using serrated knife, cut X in top center of each dough ball.\n12. Cover with towel and let dough balls rise until almost doubled in volume, about 20 minutes.\n13. Preheat oven to 375°F.\n14. Grease another baking sheet and sprinkle with cornmeal.\n15. Bring 8 cups water to boil in large saucepan.\n16. Add baking soda and 2 tablespoons sugar (water will foam up).\n17. Add 4 rolls and cook 30 seconds per side.\n18. Using slotted spoon, transfer rolls to prepared sheet, arranging X side up.\n19. Repeat with remaining rolls.\n20. Brush rolls with egg white glaze.\n21. Sprinkle rolls generously with coarse salt.\n22. Bake rolls until brown, about 25 minutes. Transfer to racks and cool 10 minutes.\n23. Serve rolls warm or room temperature. (Can be prepared 6 hours ahead. Let stand at room temperature. Rewarm in 375°F oven 10 minutes.)","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Pat & Bern's Ham Salad","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Recipes/Pat & Bern's Ham Salad.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:17:05.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Pat & Bern's Ham Salad \n\nIngredients:\n- 2 parts Balogna\n- 1 part Spiced Ham\n- Mayonnaise\n- Pickle Relish\n\nDirections:\n1. \"Dab, dab scrape\" in the food processor or grinder\n2. Add mayonnaise to preferred consistency and relish to taste.\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Mamaw's Pepper Jelly","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Recipes/Mamaw's Pepper Jelly.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:15:44.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Mamaw's Pepper Jelly \n\nServings 6 half pint jars\n\nIngredients:\n- 6 large green peppers\n- 1 1/2 cups vinegar\n- 1 teaspoon crushed red pepper\n- 6 cups sugar\n- 1/2 teaspoon salt\n- 2 (3oz) packages liquid fruit pectin (Certo)\n\nDirections:\n1. Clean and seed peppers, chop coarsely.\n2. Place peppers and vinegar in electric blender (in batches if needed). Process on high speed until desired consistency.\n3. Combine with sugar and salt in a large Dutch oven. Bring to boil.\n4. Add pectin. Cook, stirring often, for about 30mins or to soft ball stage.\n5. Quickly pour jelly into sterilized jars.\n6. Cover with clean metal lids. Screw on tightly.(If preferred, you may add one drop of green or red food coloring after jelly is cooked.)","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Grandma Betty's Cole Slaw","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Recipes/Grandma Betty's Cole Slaw.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:13:26.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Grandma Betty's Cole Slaw\n\nIngredients:\n- 1 cup Vegetable Oil\n- 1 cup Sugar\n- 1/2 cup White Vinegar\n- 1 tsp Dry Mustard\n- 1 tsp Celery Seed\n- 1 tsp Salt\n- 1 small Onion\n- 2 bags Cole Slaw\n\nDirections:\n1. Finely chop onion.\n2. Mix onion with all ingredients except cole slaw and let stand 1 hour.\n3. Add cole slaw, toss and serve.\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Creamed Chipped Beef on Toast","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Recipes/Creamed Chipped Beef on Toast.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:11:51.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Creamed Chipped Beef on Toast\n\n![http://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/250x250/00/88/18/881871.jpg](http://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/250x250/00/88/18/881871.jpg)\n\nIngredients:\n- 2 tablespoons butter\n- 2 tablespoons all-purpose flour\n- 1 1/2 cups warm milk\n- 1 (8 ounce) jar dried beef\n- 1 pinch cayenne pepper\n\nDirections:\nIn a medium saucepan over low heat, melt butter. Whisk in flour all at once to form a roux. Whisk in milk, a little at a time, increase heat to medium-high, and cook, stirring, until thickened. Bring to a boil, stir in beef and cayenne, heat through and serve over toast.\n\nSource [http://allrecipes.com/recipe/creamed-chipped-beef-on-toast/](http://allrecipes.com/recipe/creamed-chipped-beef-on-toast/)","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Cocktail Weenies","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Recipes/Cocktail Weenies.md","lastModified":"2023-01-02T16:10:17.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Cocktail Weenies \n\nIngredients:\n- 2 packages Cocktail wieners, little smokies\n- 12oz bottle chili sauce\n- 1 cup grape jelly\n\nDirections Combine cocktail wieners or little smokies in Crockpot with chili sauce and grape jelly; cover and cook on LOW for 6 t