 Tech Center for Geographic Information System (https://cgis.gatech.edu/).  Siva (siva@design.gatech.edu (404-894-0129).) is the Technical Lead of the new Georgia Tech Property GIS.   \n    System is mostly created, there are a few features that are needed.\n    Plan is to turn off the XP VM by January 2018.\n\n    Machine contains Business Critical Data.\n\n## Systems and/or Networks to be Exempted:\n\n    VM host is pbf-rel-mj25m5m.ad.gatech.edu (130.207.41.22) Windows 7.\n    VM guest is pbf-af34-arcview.ad.gatech.edu (130.207.41.160) Windows XP.\n\n## Mitigations:\n\n    * VM is kept shut down, until needed.\n    * XP VM is activated on an ad hoc basis.\n    * Firewall- departmental PiX, VM Host firewall, and VM guest firewall.\n    * VM host system is configured for automatic updates from Windows, Adobe Flash.\n\n## Duration Requested:\n\n    10 months\n\n## Coorespondance:\n\nEntered on 03/08/2017 at 11:12:27 EST (GMT-0500) by blount@gatech.edu:\n\n    There is a VM running Windows XP in Real Estate (only seldom running) that we\n    would like to keep available through calendar year 2017.\n\n    Thanks,\n    Joe\n\nEntered on 04/25/2017 at 20:02:48 EDT (GMT-0400) by Charles Leggett:\n\n    Hello Joe, thanks for your patience.\n\n    We've reviewed the information in your policy exception request have agreed to\n    grant the exception through February 2018.\n\n    Please continue to work to resolve this issue ahead of the exception expiration\n    date.\n\n    Inform us of any significant progress and let us know when you've been able to\n    resolve the issue.\n\n    Reply to reopen if you have any questions.\n\n    Thanks.\n\n    --\n    Charles\n\nEntered on 04/25/2017 at 20:18:50 EDT (GMT-0400) by Charles Leggett:\n\n    Joe,\n\n    I noticed a firewall rule that was added in 2010 for port 3389 to be open to 130.207.41.160 from vpn-facstaff.\n\n    Can this rule be removed as a further mitigation?\n\n    Let me know.\n\n    Thanks.\n\n    --\n    Charles\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"README","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/80 - GGC/87 - GGC Security/87.03 - Security Operations/11 - Security Operations/Vulnerability Response/VulnerabilityManagement/CoE-CollegeOfEngineering/ME-MechanicalEngineering/GenzaleStudent/README.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:24:18.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# README\n\n## Tickets:\n\n    1) SD 508265\n    2) FIR 7395\n\n## Notes:\n\n* Calling this one complete. The device is blocked and will not be unblocked\n  without Cyber Security intervention.\n\n@cleggett 4/22:\n\n    Not sure what's going on with this one. They filed a policy exception and\n    then followed up with \"it's not mine\"\n\n@cleggett 4/23:\n\n    Obscurity:\n    \n      Exception entered in Obscurity on 2017-01-18, but is not approved.\n\n    Splunk:\n      \n      No longer showing up in EOL reports.\n      \n    Bok:\n\n      MAC: 00:0c:6e:d6:15:7f \n      Not MAC blocked.\n\n      Located In\tNorth Interconnect\n      Data Closet\t0407:cab3\n      Switch\t130.207.254.46\n      Unit\tUnit 1\n      Port\t0\n      Verified\t2017-04-23 06:30:45\n\n    fw.noc:\n\n      Firewall last updated: 27 Aug 2013 10:31:34 (mf139)\n\n      Scan Status: No Host Alive\n      Scan Status Updated: 23 Apr 2017 08:07:47\n      Scan Status Checked: 23 Apr 2017 08:07:47\n\n@cleggett 4/24:\n\n    This machine is still on the block list.\n\n    According to the tool data from yesterday, it appears to be physically connected, but not scannable.\n\n## Contacts\nTechnical Lead:\n\n    Stephen Fuller\n    stephen.fuller@me.gatech.edu\n    404-894-2039\n\nUnit Lead:\n\n    Mark Ellington\n    404-385-8611\n\nOther:\n\n    Caroline L. Genzale, Ph.D.\n    Assistant Professor\n    office: 404-894-5099\n    mobile: 608-770-9899\n\n## Exemption Request:\n\n    Need additional time to locate, order, and replace computer in question.\n\n## Systems and/or Networks to be Exempted:\n\n    128.61.140.83 imdlsrv \"Genzale Student”\n\n## Mitigations:\n\n    If we are able to update this machine to current version of Windows without\n    significant disruption of project work, this will be done as soon as possible.\n    Otherwise, a new machine with current operating system will be placed on order\n    as soon as feasible, with expected install by Summer 2017.\n\n## Duration Requested\n\n    6 months\n\n## Coorespondance:\n\nEntered on 01/18/2017 at 13:45:49 EST (GMT-0500) by caroline.genzale@me.gatech.edu:\n\n    Please find attached, a policy exception request for a student computer in\n    my group.\n\n    Thanks,\n    Caroline Genzale\n\n    Form Returned: Exception_Request_Form5.pdf\n\n    The attached file is the filled-out form. Please open it to review the data.  \")\n\nEntered on 01/19/2017 at 08:38:48 EST (GMT-0500) by Blake Penn:\n\n    Please update the request and indicate if the machine contains Sensitive or\n    Business Critical Data.  Thanks.\n\nEntered on 01/31/2017 at 13:32:28 EST (GMT-0500) by Charles Leggett:\n    \n    Caroline and Blake, I want to check to see if this request is still moving.\n    Who has the ball?\n\nEntered on 01/31/2017 at 13:55:11 EST (GMT-0500) by Blake Penn:\n\n    Kyle asked for more information on this ticket ??? adding this into the\n    ticket correspondence:\n\n    Hi Stephen,\n\n    The committee discussed your policy exception request for 128.61.140.83\n    (\"Genzale Student???) and they would like some more detail.\n\n    1) Could you give us more information about the machine and why more time is\n    needed?\n    2) What kind of data is housed on or accessed by the machine?\n    3) What kind of mitigating controls have been put into place until the machine\n    can be updated?\n\n    Thanks,\n    Kyle\n\nEntered on 02/06/2017 at 16:34:59 EST (GMT-0500) by Charles Leggett:\n\n    Kyle, have you heard back from Stephen? Is this still moving?\n\nEntered on 02/06/2017 at 16:40:05 EST (GMT-0500) by Kyle Koza:\n\n    I have not heard back. The