it Lead:\n\n    Michael Fisher\n    mfisher@devices.net\n    7747662793\n\nOther:\n\n    Erick Beebe\n    erickbeebe@gatech.edu\n    404/385-1468\n\n    Darren Okunlola\n    darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\n\n    Dershika Patel\n    Senior Project Engineer\n    Global Center for Medical Innovation (GCMI)\n    T3 Labs\n    Atlanta, Georgia\n    m: 678.749.1599\n\n## Exemption Request:\n\n    This is a piece of manufacturing equipment which requires Windows XP to function.\n\n    GCMI requires the machine to be accessible over our local network.\n    (Sensitive and/or Business Critical Data is not contained)\n\n## Systems and/or Networks to be Exempted:\n\n    128.61.110.174 pj6k-0382 Windows XP\n\n## Mitigations:\n\n    The machine is only accessible to computers on GCMI's local network. Login information\n    (username, and password) are required to access the machine. Physical access to our\n    facility requires buzzcard access.\n\n## Duration Requested\n\n    12 months\n\n## Coorespondance:\n\nDate: Aug. 5, 2016, 2:30 p.m.\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\" <darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    \"erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu\" <erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    Added by: nhutchinson7\n    Date: Aug. 5, 2016, 2:30 p.m.\n    Subject: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security has identified the following end of life devices on your network:\n\n    128.61.110.174\tpj6k-0382\tWindows XP\t\n\nAug. 5, 2016, 2:50 p.m.\n\n    From: erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Aug. 5, 2016, 2:50 p.m.\n    Subject: Re: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI INCIDENT=7364\n\n    The machine was rebuilt. \n\nOct. 14 & 19, 2016, 11:35 a.m.\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\" <darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    \"erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu\" <erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    Added by: hmorrell3\n    Date: Oct. 14, 2016, 11:35 a.m.\n    Subject: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n    Hello,\n\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security has identified the following end of life devices on\n    your network:\n\n    128.61.110.174 - pj6k-0382 - Windows XP\n\nOct. 19, 2016, 11:45 a.m.\n\n    From: erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Subject: Re: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n\n    I¹m working with GCMI to locate it at the moment.\n\nOct. 20, 2016, 2:05 p.m.\n\n    From: erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Oct. 20, 2016, 2:05 p.m.\n    Subject: Re: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n    We can¡¯t locate the machine. We checked the GCMI offices. It may have been\n    a laptop. Is there any more information you can give me that I can go on?\n\n    Thanks,\n\n    Erick Beebe\n\nOct. 20, 2016, 3 p.m.\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\" <darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    \"erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu\" <erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    Added by: hmorrell3\n    Date: Oct. 20, 2016, 3 p.m.\n    Subject: Re: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n    Hello,\n\n    It was still on the GCMI network at 2016-10-20T14:37:00.896901-0400,\n    connected over ethernet, and the MAC is 0018.7d1d.abc0. \n\n    For what it's worth, it did not alert on the scan performed this week,\n    though it has alerted on it in weeks past. It may have just been unplugged\n    though, if it is indeed a laptop as you believe.\n\n    Thanks,\n\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security\n\nOct. 25, 2016, 4:06 p.m.\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\" <darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    \"erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu\" <erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    Added by: hmorrell3\n    Date: Oct. 25, 2016, 4:06 p.m.\n    Subject: Re: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n    Hello,\n\n    Any progress on this?\n\n    Thanks,\n\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security\n\nDate: Oct. 25, 2016, 5:05 p.m.\n\n    From: erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Oct. 25, 2016, 5:05 p.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n\n    There's nothing to report. The machine in question isn't on the network\n    anymore and we couldn't find it. None of the machines in GCMI are on\n    anything lower than Windows 7 64bit - I set them all up. As best as we can\n    figure, the machine in question was brought in from outside of GT. I've\n    asked that in the future everyone from outside that comes into GCMI be aware\n    that Windows XP, or any machine not properly patched is forbidden.\n\nOct. 26, 2016, 10:31 a.m.\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\" <darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    \"erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu\" <erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    Added by: hmorrell3\n    Date: Oct. 26, 2016, 10:31 a.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n    Hello,\n\n    In that case, we will go ahead and close this ticket. We appreciate the notice. \n\n    Thanks,\n\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security\n\nNov. 10 & 15 & 22 & Dec. 1, 2016, 2:20 p.m.\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\" <darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    \"erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu\" <erick.beebe@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    Added by: hmorrell3\n    Date: Nov. 10, 2016, 2:20 p.m.\n    Subject: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n    Hello,\n\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security has identified the following end of life devices on your network:\n\n    128.61.110.174 - pj6k-0382 - Windows XP\n\nDec. 2, 2016, 11:40 a.m.\n\n    From: darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Dec. 2, 2016, 11:40 a.m.\n    Subject: Re: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n\n    Erick Beebe said this was taken care of before he retired from Georgia Tech\n    last month.  Apparently, itâ??s not. So on Monday I will go over to GCMI to\n    investigate where things are with this device and remove it and schedule it\n    for either retirement/surplus or a rebuild.  Will have an answer on Monday,\n    Tuesday at the latestâ?¦\n\n    Thanks\n\n    DarrenO!\n\nDec. 2, 2016, 11:47 a.m.\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\" <darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu>\n    \"mikeparks@gatech.edu\" <mikeparks@gatech.edu>\n    Added by: hmorrell3\n    Date: Dec. 2, 2016, 11:47 a.m.\n    Subject: Re: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n    Hello,\n\n    He reported that he couldn't find it and that it wasn't on the network anymore.\n    It also didn't show up on our scans for a week or two, but has since reappeared.\n    He suspected that it was a laptop.\n\n    It appears to be on switch 128.61.110.130 in data closet 1146D and seems to be\n    showing up on 45 and/or 48, according to BoK.\n\n    If you need any more information, I'd be happy to provide it.\n\n    Thanks,\n\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security\n\nDec. 2, 2016, 11:50 a.m.\n\n    From: darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Dec. 2, 2016, 11:50 a.m.\n    Subject: Automatic reply: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n\n    Thanks for your email. Unfortunately I am out of the office and won't be\n    returning till the 5th of December 2016.  Should you need immediate assistance,\n    please contact Mike Parks and Kimberly Blumberg Otherwise I'll respond upon my\n    return...\n\n    Thanks\n\n    DarrenO!\n\nDec. 2, 2016, 11:55 a.m.\n\n    From: darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Dec. 2, 2016, 11:55 a.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n\n    Currently out of town, but will use the info to investigate on Monday...\n\n    Thanks\n\n    DarrenO!\n\nDec. 9, 2016, 1 p.m.\n\n    From: darren.okunlola@innovate.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Dec. 9, 2016, 1 p.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL Notification for your department - GCMI\n\n    I went by GCMI and after some searching was able to find the culprit.  The\n    gentleman that normally manages this device is out, so I'll be contacting\n    him once he's back.  It's not a regular desktop/laptop but the root O/S on a\n    device that does high res printing I believe.  I'll know more when I speak\n    with the operator.  Based on my preliminary findings, it looks like they may\n    have to submit a policy exception form.  Again I'll have more answers once\n    the operator returns on Monday...\n\n    Thanks\n\n    DarrenO!\n\nDec. 15 & Jan 13, 2016, 7 p.m.\n\n    From: kyle.koza@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Dec. 15, 2016, 7 p.m.\n    Subject: Action Required - End of Life Operating Systems\n    Hello,\n\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security has identified the following end of life systems as\n    still requiring action from you in order to meet the over-due compliance\n    deadline of October 1st, 2016.\n\n    128.61.110.174\tpj6k-0382\tWindows XP\n\nFriday, January 13, 2017 3:39 PM\n\n    From: Kyle Koza [mailto:kyle.koza@security.gatech.edu]\n    Sent: Friday, January 13, 2017 3:39 PM\n    To: Parks, Michael W ; Okunlola, Darren A \n    Cc: Koza, Kyle J \n    Subject: Action Required - End of Life Operating Systems INCIDENT=7364\n\n    Hello,\n\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security has identified the following end of life systems\n    as still requiring action from you in order to meet the over-due compliance\n    deadline of October 1st, 2016.\n\n    IP              Host       OS\n    --------------  ---------  ----------\n    128.61.110.174  pj6k-0382  Windows XP\n\nJanuary 18, 2017 at 12:15:02 EST\n\n    From: \"Okunlola, Darren A\" \n    Subject: RE: Action Required - End of Life Operating Systems INCIDENT=7364\n    Date: January 18, 2017 at 12:15:02 EST\n    To: \"Koza, Kyle J\" \n    Cc: \"Koza, Kyle J\" \n\n    Hello Kyle,\n\n    The person to see about this is Erick Beebe.  He's taken over as the IT/CSR\n    contact for GCMI.  He can be reached at erickbeebe@gatech.edu\n\n    Thanks\n\n    DarrenO!\n\nJan. 18, 2017, 12:25 p.m.\n\n    From: kyle.koza@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Jan. 18, 2017, 12:25 p.m.\n    Subject: Fwd: Action Required - End of Life Operating Systems\n\n    Erick,\n\n    Please see below.\n\n    Kyle\n\n    > Begin forwarded message:\n    > \n    > From: \"Okunlola, Darren A\" Subject: RE: Action Required - End of Life\n    > Operating Systems INCIDENT=7364 Date: January 18, 2017 at 12:15:02 EST To:\n    > \"Koza, Kyle J\" Cc: \"Koza, Kyle J\" \n    > \n    > Hello Kyle,\n    > \n    > The person to see about this is Erick Beebe.  He's taken over as the\n    > IT/CSR contact for GCMI.  He can be reached at erickbeebe@gatech.edu\n    > \n    > Thanks\n    > \n    > DarrenO!\n\nJan. 31, 2017, 4:50 p.m.\n\n    From: erickbeebe@gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Jan. 31, 2017, 4:50 p.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL machines to be removed from the network tomorrow\n\n    This is a 3D printer that is used by GCMI. According to them, they contacted\n    GT security and explained the situation. It will continue to show up any\n    time this machine is used.\n\nFeb. 1, 2017, 12:35 p.m.\n\n    From: kyle.koza@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Feb. 1, 2017, 12:35 p.m.\n    Subject: Re: EOL machines to be removed from the network tomorrow\n\n    Hi Erick,\n\n    As far as I can tell, I do not have any documentation on this. Could you ask\n    them to send me the policy exception they submitted and who they spoke with?\n\n    I have a policy exception for a 3d printer, but it was from a different\n    group and the machine had a different IP address.\n\n    Thanks,\n    Kyle\n\nTuesday, February 07, 2017 5:47 PM\n\n    From: GT Security Operations Center\n    Sent: Tuesday, February 07, 2017 5:47 PM\n    To: Beebe, Erick B\n    Cc: Koza, Kyle J; GT Security Operations Center\n    Subject: EOL machines will be blacklisted from GT network INCIDENT=7364\n\n    Hello,\n\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security has identified the following end of life systems\n    on your network. We have been alerting you to these machines over the last\n    several months. Due to inaction, we have blocked these IP addresses from\n    communication with the Internet. If we still do not receive a policy\n    exception from you by 8am on Wednesday, February 8th, we will blacklist\n    these hosts from the campus network.\n\n    THE FOLLOWING MACHINES HAVE BEEN BLOCKED FROM THE INTERNET AND WILL BE\n    BLACKLISTED FROM THE GT NETWORK TOMORROW (2/8/17)\n\n    IP Host OS\n    -------------- --------- ----------\n    128.61.110.174 pj6k-0382 Windows XP\n\nOn Wed, Feb 8, 2017 at 8:57 AM, Beebe, Erick B wrote:\n    \n    Dersi,\n\n    Your equipment using Windows XP has now been blocked from using the network.\n    If you want any of them to have network access, I'm going to need to come\n    over there and work with you to fill out the paperwork for every 3D printer\n    and CNC machine that uses XP. I'll submit the paperwork once it's all\n    complete and everything will be taken care of.\n\nWednesday, February 08, 2017 8:59 AM\n\n    From: Dershika Patel\n    Sent: Wednesday, February 08, 2017 8:59 AM\n    To: Beebe, Erick B; Patrick Strane\n    Subject: Re: FW: EOL machines will be blacklisted from GT network INCIDENT=7364\n\n    Dear Erick,\n\n    That is the only one. Could you send us the paperwork?\n\n    Patrick / Erick, would Friday work for both of you to meet on this?\n\n    Thank you,\n\n    Dersi\n\nOn Wed, Feb 8, 2017 at 9:03 AM, Beebe, Erick B wrote:\n\n    Here is the form. Please fill it out and send it back. I'll take it from there.\n\n    Thanks,\n\n    Erick Beebe\n\nOn Wed, Feb 8, 2017 at 9:03 AM, Dershika Patel wrote:\n\n    Thanks Erick!\n\n    Dersi\n\nWednesday, February 08, 2017 1:34 PM\n    \n    From: Dershika Patel\n    Sent: Wednesday, February 08, 2017 1:34 PM\n    To: Beebe, Erick B\n    Cc: Patrick Strane\n    Subject: Re: FW: EOL machines will be blacklisted from GT network INCIDENT=7364\n\n    Dear Erick,\n\n    Please see attached. Let us know if we require additional details.\n\n    Warmest regards,\n\n    Dersi\n\nFeb. 9, 2017, 8:40 a.m.\n\n    From: erickbeebe@gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Feb. 9, 2017, 8:40 a.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL machines will be blacklisted from GT network\n\n    Here is the completed form.\n\nEntered on 02/09/2017 at 09:36:30 EST (GMT-0500) by erickbeebe@gatech.edu:\n\n    Hello,\n\n    The department that has this machine has a huge print job that needs to be\n    done today. The department says they spoke to OIT some time ago about not\n    blocking this machine. It is now blocked. Please unblock it ASAP.\n\n    Thank you,\n\n    Erick Beebe\n\nFeb. 9, 2017, 12:35 p.m.\n\n    From: kyle.koza@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Feb. 9, 2017, 12:35 p.m.\n    Subject: Re: EOL machines will be blacklisted from GT network\n\n    Erick,\n\n    Could you please include the cost that it would take to upgrade to a supported\n    operating system? Also, please detail the reason why network connectivity is\n    needed.\n\n    Thanks,\n    Kyle\n\nEntered on 02/13/2017 at 12:07:23 EST (GMT-0500) by Erick Beebe:\n\n    I sent a note from the vender to Kyle Koza. We will need an exemption for\n    the next 3 months at least.\n\nFeb. 16, 2017, 8:40 a.m.\n    \n    From: kyle.koza@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Feb. 16, 2017, 8:40 a.m.\n    Subject: Please remove 00187d1dabc0 from the blacklisted machines\n\n    Good morning, Graham,\n\n    GCMI has completed a policy exception and it was approved by the EOL OS\n    committee. Could you remove the network block on:\n\n    128.61.110.174 - 00187d1dabc0 - pj6k-0382\n\n    I believe it was connected to 128.61.110.130 GigabitEthernet1/0/45.\n\n    Thanks,\n    Kyle\n\nFeb. 16, 2017, 8:45 a.m.\n\n    From: kyle.koza@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Feb. 16, 2017, 8:45 a.m.\n    Subject: Re: SLA Updates\n\n    Erick,\n\n    This policy exception has been approved with an end date of 5/1/17. Please\n    follow up with us in April with the upgrade cost and we can readdress the\n    exception then.\n\n    It should be unblocked from the network today.\n\n    Thanks,\n    Kyle\n\nFeb. 16, 2017, 8:50 a.m.\n\n    From: pstrane3@gtvault.onmicrosoft.com\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Feb. 16, 2017, 8:50 a.m.\n    Subject: Re: SLA Updates\n\n    Good Morning Kyle, \n\n    Thank you for helping us get our SLA machine back online. I am reaching out\n    to 3D Systems representatives (the equipment manufacturer) to make sure that\n    GCMI is made aware when the hardware/software patch is available for\n    customer purchase. \n\n    Best, \n\n    Patrick \n\nFeb. 17, 2017, 10:40 a.m.\n\n    From: graham.thomas@oit.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Feb. 17, 2017, 10:40 a.m.\n    Subject: Re: Please remove 00187d1dabc0 from the blacklisted machines\n\n    Cleared\n\n    Graham\n\nSent: Tuesday, March 28, 2017 8:06:37 AM\n\n    From: Beebe, Erick B <erickbeebe@gatech.edu<mailto:erickbeebe@gatech.edu>>\n    Sent: Tuesday, March 28, 2017 8:06:37 AM\n    To: Patrick Strane\n    Subject: machine OS\n\n    Patrick,\n\n    Please send me an update on where we are with getting that 3D printer running XP\n    so I can submit the request for an extension.\n\n    Thanks,\n\n    Erick Beebe\n\nSent: Tuesday, March 28, 2017 9:01 AM\n\n    From: Strane, Patrick W\n    Sent: Tuesday, March 28, 2017 9:01 AM\n    To: Beebe, Erick B <erickbeebe@gatech.edu>; Patrick Strane <pstrane@devices.net>\n    Subject: Re: machine OS\n\n    Hey Erick,\n\n    Thank you for reaching out. Right now the update is still in R&D so it's not\n    available for consumer use. It is looking like we will need to extend the\n    temporary access, at least for a while, while the update is unavailable.\n\n    Best,\n\n    Patrick\n\nEntered on 04/06/2017 at 07:53:37 EDT (GMT-0400) by erickbeebe@gatech.edu:\n\n    Please extend this policy exemption another 3 months. We're still waiting for\n    the upgrade from Windows XP. Please contact me if you have any questions.\n\n    Thanks you,\n\n    Erick Beebe\n\nEntered on 04/07/2017 at 16:04:04 EDT (GMT-0400) by Charles Leggett:\n\n    NOTE: I am reviving this old ticket b/c I think that it's still the most\n    recent information.\n\n    Erick,\n\n    Kyle told me that you've heard back from the manufacturer about the 3D printer\n    in GCMI and that they haven't released an update.\n\n    If this is the case, we'll go back to the policy exception request that you\n    filed for a 12 month exception period.\n\n    Provided that the mitigation steps that you included in the attached document\n    are in place I can approve this from a technical point of view.\n\n    Blake Penn will review it to see if more specific policy language needs to be in\n    place before we grant the extension.\n\n    We'll be in touch soon.\n\n    --\n    Charles H. Leggett, CIS\n\nEntered on 04/11/2017 at 11:12:20 EDT (GMT-0400) by Blake Penn:\n\n    Erick,\n\n    We will run your exception request through the exception process.\n\n    Thanks.\n\nEntered on 04/25/2017 at 17:45:02 EDT (GMT-0400) by Charles Leggett:\n\n    Thank you for your patience Erick,\n\n    Since it sounds like there is no update coming soon from the manufacturer, we'd\n    like to call this policy exception closed and instead \n    add it to our risk register as an accepted risk.\n\n    This means that we recognize that this machine has the proper mitigations in\n    place and that while it's not in policy compliance, the \n    risk it presents is minimal enough that we're willing to accept it.\n\n    We'll add a pin in our calendar to review this decision periodically and ask\n    that you stay on the manufacturer for a fix and consider \n    the upgradability of the OS in future purchases from this or any other\n    manufacturer.\n\n    Let me know if you have any questions, or if you agree that we can close this\n    ticket.\n\n    Thanks.\n\n    --\n    Charles\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Untitled 16a0b8c307ff416eb07d6c130d9d94a8","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/30 - Social/33 - Travel & Events/2015 RIMM/Untitled Database 885b64a1bda443feb7750699477e5d12/Untitled 16a0b8c307ff416eb07d6c130d9d94a8.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:24:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Untitled 16a0b8c307ff416eb07d6c130d9d94a8\n\nDay 1 (Symphony 3): Jul 14, 2019 8:00 AM-8:15 AM","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Untitled 1df099f44e22450c9803cc3a5a93e55e","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/30 - Social/33 - Travel & Events/2015 RIMM/Untitled Database 885b64a1bda443feb7750699477e5d12/Untitled 1df099f44e22450c9803cc3a5a93e55e.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:24:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Untitled 1df099f44e22450c9803cc3a5a93e55e\n\nDay 1 (Symphony 3): Jul 14, 2019 10:15 AM-11:15 AM","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Untitled 24d756d10ea54209abd888436877e15b","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/30 - Social/33 - Travel & Events/2015 RIMM/Untitled Database 885b64a1bda443feb7750699477e5d12/Untitled 24d756d10ea54209abd888436877e15b.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:24:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Untitled 24d756d10ea54209abd888436877e15b\n\nDay 1 (Symphony 3): Jul 14, 2019 3:30 AM-3:45 AM","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Untitled 4469517ae00249b3b07e2d4efc3f948e","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/30 - Social/33 - Travel 