iers and seek out new ones to make sure we have the best and lightest fabrics for  all of our applications. We will only use the very best what ever the price of raw good because that adds  cost effective long term value in the field.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Untitled b8bfe5641a13430096437d96fecdf9b9","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/40 - Hobbies/41 - Outdoors/MYOG/MYOG 311a87ee05654ab591e1914e49c93df4/Mountain Laurel Designs - Fabric Mojo, Catenary Cu cdd1382f87dd4c7ba6a5959a921a2d4e/Untitled Database 4cb1b5a5bb1142078f8655f4919f8068/Untitled b8bfe5641a13430096437d96fecdf9b9.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:24:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Untitled b8bfe5641a13430096437d96fecdf9b9\n\n6: Shop  |  \n\tFabric Mojo  |  \n\tInfo  |  \n\tHome","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Untitled fd90876deaf74ee49a556aaba0b2c7c7","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/40 - Hobbies/41 - Outdoors/MYOG/MYOG 311a87ee05654ab591e1914e49c93df4/Mountain Laurel Designs - Fabric Mojo, Catenary Cu cdd1382f87dd4c7ba6a5959a921a2d4e/Untitled Database 4cb1b5a5bb1142078f8655f4919f8068/Untitled fd90876deaf74ee49a556aaba0b2c7c7.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:24:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Untitled fd90876deaf74ee49a556aaba0b2c7c7\n\n6: MLD TESTING AND DEVELOPMENT\n\nWe are one of the only ultralight weight manufacturers to own and use a wide range of testing equipment - included this +$1,000 Suter HydroStatic Tester.  We have been testing for ten years and have developed a range of standard and proprietary tests specifically applicable and correlated to how UL backpackers use the gear in the field. All of the current standards like ASTM,  UL, etc. for outdoor gear were primarily set by the very large outdoor gear companies and speciality big box store reps over a decade ago - before the new wave of UltraLight backpackers and adventure athletes started breaking new ground and pushing limits. We do not feel these standards are accurate or represent many of the current users expectations for our new sport. At MLD we have thousands of users reports from the field over the last decade and we go our own way.  \n\nA special note on Cuben Fiber Shelters: \nCuben Fiber is Amazing - strong, light and totally waterproof.  We have been making CF shelters for a long time - in fact - we have offered cuben fiber backpacking products longer than any other company. Adding up all the MLD Cuben Shelters and all the other gear companies cuben shelters plus DYI'ers, there are well over 35,000 cuben shelter users worldwide with well over 350,000 nights of use. There are next to zero reports online anywhere about these Cuben shelters failing due the waterproofness or strength of the fabric. That's a LOT of Common Sense to support that CF is extremely dependable. Anyone claiming otherwise is just not credible.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Untitled 11d6a5bf7912402bb5fc6f1c8a0fa436","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/50 - Maintenance/54 - Tools & Appliances/Ryobi Blower (RY09460) 35782cfe968040d9a6c7fb07f5deace6/Ryobi RY09460 Blower Label 498aca8ccce24ec5addc8ed1a233fdda/Untitled Database 6ca9da976f064f11a93d46a69a057baa/Untitled 11d6a5bf7912402bb5fc6f1c8a0fa436.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:24:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Untitled 11d6a5bf7912402bb5fc6f1c8a0fa436","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Untitled 2453615609414f6cb995db711b9627fa","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/50 - Maintenance/54 - Tools & Appliances/Ryobi Blower (RY09460) 35782cfe968040d9a6c7fb07f5deace6/Ryobi RY09460 Blower Label 498aca8ccce24ec5addc8ed1a233fdda/Untitled Database 6ca9da976f064f11a93d46a69a057baa/Untitled 2453615609414f6cb995db711b9627fa.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:24:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Untitled 2453615609414f6cb995db711b9627fa","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Untitled 53fd18328a5c41769c3695786306ff23","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/50 - Maintenance/54 - Tools & Appliances/Ryobi Blower (RY09460) 35782cfe968040d9a6c7fb07f5deace6/Ryobi RY09460 Blower Label 498aca8ccce24ec5addc8ed1a233fdda/Untitled Database 6ca9da976f064f11a93d46a69a057baa/Untitled 53fd18328a5c41769c3695786306ff23.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:24:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Untitled 53fd18328a5c41769c3695786306ff23","bookmarked":false},{"title":"README","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/80 - GGC/87 - GGC Security/87.03 - Security Operations/11 - Security Operations/Vulnerability Response/VulnerabilityManagement/CoC-CollegeOfComputing/CoC-2003AD/README.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:24:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# README\n\n## Tickets:\n\n    1) FIR 7371\n    2) SD 511584\n    3) SD 535023\n\n## Notes:\n\n* We're adding this to the risk register as a high risk.\n* CoC has had multiple extensions on this\n* They have submitted multiple progress reports w/o much progress\n* They have a \"simple\" out of upgrading the AD with new DCs, but they are stuck\n  on moving to campus AD (this is the right solution long term)\n* We granted a policy excetion on 1/31 through 3/31 with Mitigation Stipulations\n\n## Contacts\n\nTechnical Lead:\n\n    Keith Watson\n    krwatson@cc.gatech.edu\n    (678) 992-9101\n\nUnit Lead:\n\n    Uwanna Smith\n    uwanna@cc.gatech.edu\n    (678) 992-9111\n\nOther:\n\n    Dan Forsyth\n    dan.forsyth@cc.gatech.edu\n    404 894-9014\n\n    Debbie Davis\n    debbie@cc.gatech.edu\n    404 385-7155\n\n    Matthew Balaun\n    mbalaun@cc.gatech.edu\n\n## Exemption Request:\n\n    We need additional time to coordinate with Microsoft and OIT to upgrade the\n    Windows Domain Controllers to 2008.\n\n    We have more than 500 Windows, Linux, and Mac systems left that authenticate to\n    our active directory. We need more time to migrate these clients, which are\n    critical to our business processes, to the campus Active Directory.``\n\n## Systems and/or Networks to be Exempted:\n\n    130.207.2.12 gford.cc.gt.buzz Windows 2003 Forest root domain controller Business Critical\n    130.207.2.13 nixon.gt.buzz Windows 2003 Forest root domain controller Business Critical\n    130.207.2.14 kennedy.gt.buzz Windows 2003 Forest root domain controller Business Critical\n    130.207.2.15 hoover.gt.buzz Windows 2003 Domain controller Business Critical\n    130.207.2.11 carter.cc.gt.buzz Windows 2003 Domain controller Business Critical\n    130.207.17.136 legion.cc.gt.buzz Windows 2003 File server Sensitive data\n\n## Mitigations:\n\n    1. Firewalls are configured to only allow access from College of Computing subnets and departmental VPN\n    2. Active Directory is the only service running on the domain controllers\n    3. Users can't login to the servers\n    4. None of the servers are used to receive email or access the Internet\n    5. All of the servers are on subnets that do not contain user workstations\n\n## Duration Requested:\n\n    30 days\n\n## Coorespondance:\n\nDate: 8/5 & 10/6 & 10/13 & 10/19 2016\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"cert@cc.gatech.edu\" <cert@cc.gatech.edu>\n    Added by: hmorrell3\n    Date: Oct. 6, 2016, 3:10 p.m.\n    Subject: EOL Notification for your department - COC\n    Hello,\n\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security has identified the following end of life devices on\n    your network:\n\n    Some of your end of life machines have ports open to the world. Please\n    prioritize these machines.\n\n    Machines with ports open to the world: (All of following are open on port 22)\n    mellifera.cc.gatech.edu (130.207.121.63)\n    jola.cc.gatech.edu (130.207.122.53)\n    helium.cc.gatech.edu (130.207.122.95)\n    lithium.cc.gatech.edu (130.207.122.97)\n    orchid.cc.gt.atl.ga.us (143.215.128.16)\n    beast.cc.gt.atl.ga.us (143.215.128.77)\n    llama.cc.gt.atl.ga.us (143.215.128.98)\n    burgundy.cc.gt.atl.ga.us (143.215.129.54)\n    panda.cc.gt.atl.ga.us (143.215.131.119)\n    the_device.cc.gt.atl.ga.us (143.215.131.70)\n\n    Machines without ports open to the world:\n    eisfiler.ad.gatech.edu (130.207.164.250)\n    arnold.cc.gatech.edu (130.207.17.11)\n    theamericanway.cc.gatech.edu (130.207.17.11)\n    legion.cc.gt.buzz (130.207.17.136)\n    carter.cc.gt.buzz (130.207.2.11)\n    gford.cc.gt.buzz (130.207.2.12)\n    nixon.gt.buzz (130.207.2.13)\n    kennedy.gt.buzz (130.207.2.14)\n    hoover.gt.buzz (130.207.2.15)\n    jackson.gt.buzz (130.207.2.35)\n    luxor.cc.gt.atl.ga.us (143.215.131.169)\n    g-kpc.cc.gt.atl.ga.us (143.215.131.45)\n\nDate: Oct. 19, 2016, 11:55 a.m.\n\n    From: dan.forsyth@cc.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Oct. 19, 2016, 11:55 a.m.\n    Subject: Re: EOL Notification for your department - COC\n    Folks,\n\n    We're not ignoring these reports, but do not have a complete plan ready for\n    you yet.  It is coming though.\n\n    Dan\n\nDate: Oct. 27, 2016, 6:15 p.m.\nReferences: CyberSecurity-CoCEOLlist.xlsx\n\n    From: debbie@cc.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Oct. 27, 2016, 6:15 p.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL Notification for your department - COC\n    Hello,\n\n    I was tasked with gathering info about the list recently and providing an update\n    for you.  Attached is the current status of all of the systems. The plan is to\n    have all the systems upgraded or removed from the network by 12/30/2016.\n    Several systems have already been removed from the network.\n\n    If another scan could be run around November 15, I think most of the desktop\n    systems should be upgraded by then.\n\n    BTW, eisfiler.ad.gatech.edu 130.207.164.250 is not a CoC system. According\n    to BoK, that subnet belongs to EIS.\n\n    Thank you,\n\n    Debbie\n\nDate: Oct. 28, 2016, 2:08 p.m.\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"cert@cc.gatech.edu\" <cert@cc.gatech.edu>\n    Added by: hmorrell3\n    Date: Oct. 28, 2016, 2:08 p.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL Notification for your department - COC\n    Hello,\n\n    We appreciate the notice. Also, we do weekly scans, so we'll keep that November\n    date in mind.\n\nDate: Nov. 10, 2016, 3:20 p.m.\n\n    From: debbie@cc.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Nov. 10, 2016, 3:20 p.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL Notification for your department - COC\n    Hello,\n\n    Can you please email cert@cc the results of any remaining outstanding EOL\n    computers in the CoC?  Thanks.\n\n    Debbie\n\nDate: Nov. 15, 2016, 2:41 p.m.\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"cert@cc.gatech.edu\" <cert@cc.gatech.edu>\n    Added by: hmorrell3\n    Date: Nov. 15, 2016, 2:41 p.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL Notification for your department - COC\n    Hello,\n\n    As of today, the following machines have recently showed up on our scans:\n\n    130.207.116.27 - shanghai.cc.gt.buzz - Windows XP\n    130.207.121.63 - mellifera.cc.gatech.edu - Tandberg Device\n    130.207.122.53 - jola.cc.gatech.edu - Linux 2.4-2.6\n    130.207.17.128 - theamericanway.cc.gatech.edu - VMware ESX 4.0.0 build 360236\n    130.207.17.136 - legion.cc.gt.buzz\t - Windows 2003 R2 Service Pack 2\n    130.207.2.11 - carter.cc.gt.buzz - Windows 2003 Service Pack 2\n    130.207.2.12 - gford.cc.gt.buzz - Windows 2003 Service Pack 2\n    130.207.2.13 - nixon.gt.buzz - Windows 2003 Service Pack 2\n    130.207.2.14 - kennedy.gt.buzz - Windows 2003 Service Pack 2\n    130.207.2.15 - hoover.gt.buzz\t - Windows 2003 Service Pack 2\n    130.207.2.35 - jackson.gt.buzz - Windows 2003 Service Pack 2\n    143.215.129.54 - burgundy.cc.gt.atl.ga. - Linux 2.6\n    143.215.131.119 - panda.cc.gt.atl.ga.us - Tandberg Device\n    143.215.131.45 - g-kpc.cc.gt.atl.ga.us - Tandberg Device\n\nDate: Nov. 22, 2016, 2:50 p.m.\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"cert@cc.gatech.edu\" <cert@cc.gatech.edu>\n    Added by: hmorrell3\n    Date: Nov. 22, 2016, 2:50 p.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL Notification for your department - COC\n    Hello,\n\n    As of today, the following machines are still showing up:\n\n    130.207.121.63 - mellifera.cc.gatech.edu\n    130.207.122.53 - jola.cc.gatech.edu\n    130.207.17.128 - theamericanway.cc.gatech.edu\n    130.207.17.136 - legion.cc.gt.buzz\n    130.207.2.11 - carter.cc.gt.buzz\n    130.207.2.12 - gford.cc.gt.buzz\n    130.207.2.13 - nixon.gt.buzz\n    130.207.2.14 - kennedy.gt.buzz\n    130.207.2.15 - hoover.gt.buzz\n    130.207.2.35 - jackson.gt.buzz\n    143.215.129.54 - burgundy.cc.gt.atl.ga.us\n    143.215.131.119 - panda.cc.gt.atl.ga.us\n\nDate: Dec. 20, 2016, 5:35 p.m.\n\n    From: debbie@cc.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Dec. 20, 2016, 5:35 p.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL Notification for your department - COC\n    Hi Cyber Security,\n\n    On the last scan we received on 11/22, we realized Jackson was turned off on 11/16 so perhaps the scan wasn't done on 11/22?  For the four below, we've been told they have been upgraded or would be upgraded by this point. If they are still showing up on your scan for EOL, the users are requesting more details.  I was told that jola was patched a while back but perhaps something was missed on our part?  Any additional details would be helpful.\n\n    130.207.121.63 - mellifera.cc.gatech.edu\n    130.207.122.53 - jola.cc.gatech.edu\n    143.215.129.54 - burgundy.cc.gt.atl.ga.us\n    143.215.131.119 - panda.cc.gt.atl.ga.us\n\n\n    With Matt Balaun out due to the baby, we've fallen behind on decommissioning our Windows Server 2003 systems but the plan is to tackle that in January.\n    130.207.2.11 - carter.cc.gt.buzz     CoC AD\n    130.207.2.12 - gford.cc.gt.buzz    CoC AD\n    130.207.2.13 - nixon.gt.buzz    CoC AD\n    130.207.2.14 - kennedy.gt.buzz     CoC AD\n    130.207.2.15 - hoover.gt.buzz    CoC AD\n    130.207.17.128 - theamericanway.cc.gatech.edu - need to migrate data elsewhere and will decommission on 12/23/2016.\n    130.207.17.136 - legion.cc.gt.buzz - replacement server built but still need to migrate user data.\n\n    Decommissioned\n    130.207.2.35 - jackson.gt.buzz\n\n    Debbie\n\nEntered on 01/31/2017 at 11:51:42 EST (GMT-0500) by Kyle Koza:\n\n    Incident Number: 511584\n\n    We are granting a policy exception for these hosts until 3/31/17 with the\n    following stipulations: Please immediately review the firewall rules for\n    these hosts and subnets immediately. The rules in place haven't been\n    modified in several years. Please complete this by close of business\n    tomorrow (2/1).  Please sent us an official timeline for the retirement of\n    these machines as soon as possible, but no later than February 8th We would\n    like updates on the progression of this timeline every two weeks\n\n    Thanks,\n    Kyle\n\nDate: Jan. 31, 2017, 4:45 p.m.\nRe: 130.207.17.128  theamericanway.cc.gatech.edu VMware ESX 4.0.0 build 360236\n\n    From: debbie@cc.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    Added by: scripts\n    Date: Jan. 31, 2017, 4:45 p.m.\n    Subject: RE: EOL machines to be removed from the network tomorrow\n    It's been taken offline.\n\n    Debbie\n\n    -----Original Message-----\n    From: GT Security Operations Center [mailto:soc@security.gatech.edu]\n    Sent: Tuesday, January 31, 2017 4:21 PM\n    To: College of Computing\n    Cc: Koza, Kyle J; GT Security Operations Center\n    Subject: EOL machines to be removed from the network tomorrow INCIDENT=7371\n\n\n    Hello,\n\n    Georgia Tech Cyber Security has identified the following end of life systems as still requiring action from you in order to meet the over-due compliance deadline of October 1st, 2016.\n\n    THESE MACHINES WILL BE REMOVED FROM THE NETWORK TOMORROW\n\n    IP              Host                          OS\n    --------------  ----------------------------  -----------------------------\n    130.207.17.128  theamericanway.cc.gatech.edu  VMware ESX 4.0.0 build 360236\n\nEntered on 02/01/2017 at 15:20:55 EST (GMT-0500) by krwatson@cc.gatech.edu:\n\n    We reviewed and modified the firewall rules for the Windows servers.\n\n    keith\n\nEntered on 02/14/2017 at 08:21:14 EST (GMT-0500) by Kyle Koza:\n\n    Keith,\n    We have not received a timeline for the removal of these systems. Do you have an update for us?\n\n    Thanks,\n    Kyle\n\nEntered on 02/14/2017 at 09:56:51 EST (GMT-0500) by krwatson@cc.gatech.edu:\nReferences: Windows_Server_2003_Decommissioning_Project_DF_20170214095647_482660.DOCX\n\n    See attached plan\n\n    keith\n\nEntered on 03/08/2017 at 11:25:44 EST (GMT-0500) by Blake Penn:\n\n    Assigning for process review.\n\nEntered on 04/04/2017 at 09:40:11 EDT (GMT-0400) by krwatson@cc.gatech.edu:\nReferences: Windows Server 2003 Decommissioning Project Status Report 20170404_20170404094004_894029.pdf\n\n    Please see attached policy exception extension request and \"Windows Server 2003 Decommissioning Project Status Report 20170404.pdf\"\n\n    keith\n\nEntered on 04/07/2017 at 07:59:48 EDT (GMT-0400) by Charles Leggett:\n\n    Thanks Keith. We'll review the updated timeline and get back to you about it\n    soon.\n\nDate: April 7, 2017, 2:17 p.m.\nReferences: Mitigation Plan V1.docx\nReferences: Mitigation Plan V2.pdf\n\n    From: soc@security.gatech.edu\n    To:\n    \"Uwanna A Smith\" <uwanna.smith@cc.gatech.edu>\n    \"Keith R Watson\" <krwatson@cc.gatech.edu>\n    Added by: ntao6\n    Date: April 7, 2017, 2:17 p.m.\n    Subject: Windows 2003 Domain Controller Upgrades - EOL Updates\n    Hey Uwanna, Keith,\n\n    Hope you are doing well and had a good week!\n\n    I wanted to reach out to you and update you on the situation regarding EOL\n    machines in the College of Computing. Earlier this week, the CoC team\n    reached out to the security team regarding the EOL machines still on their\n    network because the policy exception you filed in January (attached) expired\n    on March 31.\n\n    They submitted an updated mitigation plan (V1 and V2 attached), but to be\n    honest we have seen very little progress over the past two months. I\n    understand that this is a difficult technical issue, but since these\n    machines run your AD and we've seen a number of active zero-days, I want to\n    prioritize this issue.\n\n    I look forward to your response and working with you to try to address this\n    security concern as soon as possible while keeping the CC resources up.\n\n    Thanks,\n\n    Nancy Tao\n\nDate: April 25, 2017, 1:07 p.m.\n\n    [12:27] Kyle Koza\n    Have you all made any progress on the DCs?\n\n    [13:01] Matthew Balaun\n    Hey, I'm out today, but yes and no.\n\n    [13:02]\n    Microsoft refused to help us even if we paid them. But, I was able in test to run adprep successfully. Unfortunately I was not able to add any new computer to the upgraded test domain. So I'm rebuilding test to try again.\n\n    [13:03]\n    If it works, we can upgrade and replace and be off 2003 entirely.\n\n    [13:03]\n    If it fails, we are stuck with getting off of our AD altogether, which is a big deal.\n\n    [13:03] Kyle Koza\n    Ok, thanks for the update\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"README","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/80 - GGC/87 - GGC Security/87.03 - Security Operations/11 - Security Operations/Vulnerability Response/VulnerabilityManagement/IPaT-InstituteForPeopleAndTechnology/CIS-RHELv5/README.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:24:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# README\n\n## Tickets:\n\n    SD 533660\n\n## Notes:\n\n* Granted policy exception through 5/31/2017\n\n## Contacts\n\nTechnical Lead:\n\n    Paul Diederich\n    paul.diederich@gatech.edu\n    404-385-3714\n\nUnit Lead:\n\n    Matt Sanders\n    msanders@gatech.edu\n    (404) 894-9107\n\n## Exemption Request:\n\n    We have 3 Red Hat Enterprise Linux v5 systems\n    that will need to continue running for a few more \n    weeks after the OS'es EOL which is March 31st 2017.\n    The three systems are m0.cip.gatech.edu,\n    shepherd.cip.gatech.edu and db.cip.gatech.edu.\n    They provide the m.gatech.edu service for the campus\n    which we are currently working on porting over to RHEL 7\n    but need more time to finish.\n\n    Shepherd has GTED credentials to look up directory\n    information not normally available to students (GT Data\n    Stewart on file) and allows proxying requests from m0\n    to look up information like class details on behalf of a\n    student using CAS.\n\n## Systems and/or Networks to be Exempted:\n\n    m0.cip.gatech.edu (128.61.158.122)\n    shepherd.cip.gatech.edu (128.61.158.104)\n    db0.cip.gatech.edu (128.61.158.117)\n\n## Mitigations:\n\n    SSH has been restricted to VPN, only staff/faculty have access to\n    shepherd. Once the majority of m.gatech.edu can run on the new host,\n    all traffic will be limited to VPN, the local subnet they are on and\n    the new host (docker00.rnoc.gatech.edu and docker01.rnoc.gatech.edu)\n    while we hammer out the remaining issues with the migration.\n\n    db0 is already restricted to just the local subnet and docker00/01.   Mitigations proposed\n\n## Duration Requested:\n\n    30 days\n\n## Coorespondance:\n\nEntered on 03/30/2017 at 20:18:35 EDT (GMT-0400) by paul.diederich@gatech.edu:\n\n    Form Returned: Exception_Request_Form.pdf\n\n    The attached file is the filled-out form. Please open it to review the data. \n\nEntered on 04/06/2017 at 08:03:30 EDT (GMT-0400) by Charles Leggett:\n\n    Paul, sorry for our delayed response.\n\n    We're reviewing the Policy Exception and will update you if we need any\n    additional mitigating controls or documentation.\n\n    Thanks.\n\nEntered on 04/25/2017 at 20:33:32 EDT (GMT-0400) by Charles Leggett:\n\n    Hello Paul, thank you for your patience\n\n    We've reviewed your policy exception request and are able to grant the exception through the end of May.\n\n    This is beyond your initial request of 30 days since it took us so long to process it.\n\n    You may have already made progress between then and now.\n\n    Reply to reopen this case and update