s/giles-3.0.2.tar.gz)\n\ndesc “Giles is a compiler for production systems. Production systems\n\nare useful computational systems for such domains as event\n\ncorrelation engines, expert systems, and action-selection\n\nmechanisms.\"\n\ndepends_on “python3\"\n\ndepends_on “sqlite\"\n\nno ./configure?\n\npip3 install pyyaml\n\npip3 install jinja2","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2014 SplunkLive Conference in Atlanta, GA 528c8d26a2ba45b9878360a465d89887","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/30 - Social/33 - Travel & Events/2014 SplunkLive Conference in Atlanta, GA 528c8d26a2ba45b9878360a465d89887.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:48.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2014 SplunkLive Conference in Atlanta, GA 528c8d26a2ba45b9878360a465d89887\n\n8:00am – Registration\n\n9:00am – Welcome, Agenda, Overview9:05am – Splunk Overview and Demo\n\n- Presented by [Manish Kalra](http://www.linkedin.com/in/mkalra), Director Product Marketing, Splunk\n\n10:00am – Customer Presentations\n\n- Marquis Montgomery, CISSP, SSCP, GSEC, SCA, Senior Security Architect, Corporate Security, CedarCrestone\n- [George Starcher](http://www.georgestarcher.com/), Enterprise Information Security Engineer, University of Alabama at Birmingham\n- James J. Taylor, CISSP, CISA, Manager, IT Internal Audit, Large Telecommunications Company\n\n12:00pm – Lunch\n\n1:15pm – Breakout Sessions, 1-2\n\n- Getting Started with Splunk Enterprise - Skill Level: Beginner\n- New to Splunk? This session is for you! You'll learn about searching, alerting, reporting, dashboards, deployment and integration.\n- Splunk for Security - Skill Level: All\n- Join our Security Expert and learn about the new Splunk App for Enterprise Security 3.0. See a demo of how this App is used by hundreds of Splunk customers as a next generation, big data SIEM for incident investigation and response, forensics, security and compliance reporting, and real-time detection of both known and unknown threats. The App contains security-related, pre-built reports, dashboards, searches, an incident review and management framework, and free threat intelligence feeds. This session is a must for all Security Experts.\n\n2:30pm – Breakout Sessions, 3-4\n\n- Data Models 101 - Skill Level: Advanced\n- Expand the usage of Splunk within your company with Splunk Enterprise Analytic features. Learn how to interact with your data in new ways and empower a new class of non-technical users. We will cover data models, pivot and more!\n- Combatting Advanced Cyberthreats using Spunk and Live Threat Intelligence - Skill Level: All\n- Need to rapidly detect and respond to advanced cyberthreats? This session is for you. Join Mike Jawetz, from Norse, and learn how to use integrated live threat intelligence with Splunk to rapidly detect indicators of compromise, streamline and prioritize your incident response process, and improve security analyst productivity.\n\n3:30pm – Happy Hour sponsored by [AppDynamics](http://www.appdynamics.com/), [Compuware](http://www.compuware.com/en_us/application-performance-management/solutions/big-data/splunk.html), [Extrahop](http://www.extrahop.com/), [MapR](http://www.mapr.com/) and [Norse](http://norse-corp.com/)","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Performance Management Invite 2fc1c560636e49f5bc4cb489c3f049a4","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Performance Management/_Forms & Templates/Performance Management Invite 2fc1c560636e49f5bc4cb489c3f049a4.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":["#summary/CUSTOMER_DEFINED/CDE"],"content":"# Performance Management Invite 2fc1c560636e49f5bc4cb489c3f049a4\n\nHello,\n\nAs you know, our performance management session is coming up soon.\n\nGGC provides training on this process:\n\n[https://grizzlylearningpathway.skillport.com/](https://grizzlylearningpathway.skillport.com/skillportfe/main.action?path=summary/CUSTOMER_DEFINED/_scorm12_sppubgrizzlylearningpathway_pm_staff#summary/CUSTOMER_DEFINED/CDE$117356:_cust_course:sppubgrizzlylearningpathway/_scorm12_sppubgrizzlylearningpathway_pm_staff)\n\nFrom that training module, your role in this process is to: \n\n- Take accountability for your self development and be open about career goals.\n- Understand what is expected of you and ask for clarification if needed.\n- Participate in setting annual goals in collaboration with your manager.\n- Seek out and be open to feedback. Give your manager feedback as well.\n- Share progress and/or barriers to your goals regularly.\n- Work with your manager to plan and prepare check-ins.\n\nHere's a link to your Performance Management form:\n\n<link>\n\nPlease review it before our meeting and come prepared to update it collaboratively with me.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Microsoft Licensing - Student to Faculty Ratio","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Purchasing/83.08.08 - Microsoft Licensing/Microsoft Licensing - Student to Faculty Ratio.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Microsoft Licensing - Student to Faculty Ratio\n40:1\n40 \"student use benefit\" to every 1 faculty","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Certified Information Security Professional (CISSP)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Certifications/Certified Information Security Professional (CISSP).md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Certified Information Security Professional (CISSP)\n[[Certifications]] - [[ISC^2]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Blackbaud","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Companies/Blackbaud.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Blackbaud\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Salude","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Companies/Salude.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Salude\nSkilled [[Nursing]] Facility\n\nhttps://www.salude.com/\n\n2019.01.27 - Mom suggested this place to Joanne for rehab on Betty’s hip.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Dual Boot Windows 10 and Kali","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Configurations/Dual Boot Windows 10 and Kali.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Dual Boot Windows 10 and Kali\n## Disable Secure Boot\nThe Kali OS is not \"signed\" or whatever's necessary to support Secure Boot, so it must be disabled it in BIOS (F12 on Dell).\n\nNOTE: This may not be an issue for other Linux distros.\n\n## Disable BitLocker (temporarily)\nIn Win10, you have to disable BitLocker so that that the Kali installer can see the disk.\n\n## Shrink Partition\nIn Win10, use Disk Management to shrink the windows partition to give up some room for Kali\n\n## SATA Controller\nFor me, Kali required ACHI mode to work, but the Win10 laptop that I got from GGC was configured with the SATA Controller configured to be \"RAID ON\"  \n\nThis person was the champion of the day for me: https://gist.github.com/chenxiaolong/4beec93c464639a19ad82eeccc828c63\n\n### Switching from RAID ON to AHCI\n1. In Win10, set the default boot mode to Safe Mode, use msconfig.exe or open an admin cmd/PowerShell window and run:\n> bcdedit /set '{current}' safeboot minimal\n2. Reboot and hit F12 to enter the BIOS.\n3. Change the SATA Controller mode to AHCI.\n4. Save and reboot.\n5. After Windows successfully boots into Safe Mode, disable Safe Mode with msconfig.exe or open an admin cmd/PowerShell window and run:\n> bcdedit /deletevalue '{current}' safeboot\n6. Reboot one last time. If you open the Device Manager, there should now be a Standard NVM Express Controller device under Storage Controllers.\n\n## Install Kali\nAfter all of that prep, it's finally time to install Kali.\n\n## Enable BitLocker\nYou can now reenable BitLocker in Windows\n\n## Enable Secure Boot?\nThe Kali OS is not \"signed\" or whatever's necessary to support Secure Boot, so it must stay disabled it in BIOS.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Hilton Head Island","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Places/Hilton Head Island.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Hilton Head Island\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Places to Visit","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Places/Places to Visit.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Places to Visit\n- Georgia\n\n    Raven Cliff Falls\n\n    Red Top Mountain State Park\n\n    Chattahoochee River National Recreation Area (U.S. National Park Service)\n\n    Stone Mountain\n\n    Fort Yargo\n\n    Hard Labor Creek\n\n    Payne's Creek (near Hartwell)\n\n    Stonewall Falls in Tiger, GA\n\n    Gibbs Gardens\n\n- Southeast\n\n    Bluffton, SC\n\n    Asheville, NC\n\n    Fire's Creek Rim Trail\n\n    The Great Smoky Mountains\n\n    The Florida Keys\n\n    Linville Gorge in NC\n\n    Max Patch near Hot Springs, NC\n\n    New Orleans, LA\n\n- US\n\n    Columbia River Gorge, OR\n\n    Washington, DC\n\n    NYC\n\n    Fairbanks, Alaska\n\n    Cape Cod\n\n    Seattle, WA\n\n    Glacier National Park\n\n    Arches National Park\n\n    Craggy Gardens National Park\n\n- International\n\n    Costa Rica\n\n    France\n\n    England\n\n    Italy","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Beards & Tequila","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Quotes/Beards & Tequila.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Beards & Tequila\n[[Beards]] are like Tequila, they'll make your clothes fall off.\n\n[[Funny Stuff]] - [[Andy Schlenker]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Microsoft Teams Diagnostic","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Technologies/Microsoft Teams Diagnostic.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Microsoft Teams Diagnostic\nClick systray icon 6 times then right-click","bookmarked":false},{"title":"PowerShell - TLS Fix","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Technologies/PowerShell - TLS Fix.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# PowerShell - TLS Fix\nFrom https://stackoverflow.com/questions/43323123/warning-unable-to-find-module-repositories ...\n\nWith the [deprecation of TLS 1.0 and 1.1 for PowerShell Gallery](https://devblogs.microsoft.com/powershell/powershell-gallery-tls-support) as of April 2020, the cmdlets Update-Module and Install-Module became broken. Thus, [according to this article](https://dev.to/darksmile92/powershell-disabled-support-for-tls-1-0-for-the-gallery-update-module-and-install-module-broken-1oii), some commands need to be executed to bring them alive again:\n\n> [Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol = [Net.SecurityProtocolType]::Tls12 \nInstall-Module PowerShellGet -RequiredVersion 2.2.4 -SkipPublisherCheck\n\nIf that still doesn't work, then run the following commands:\n\n> [Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol = [Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol -bor [Net.SecurityProtocolType]::Tls12\nRegister-PSRepository -Default -Verbose\nSet-PSRepository -Name \"PSGallery\" -InstallationPolicy Trusted","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2019 EDUCAUSE HEISC Metrics Working Group","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/30 - Social/33 - Travel & Events/2019 EDUCAUSE HEISC Metrics Working Group.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2019 EDUCAUSE HEISC Metrics Working Group\nCompletely lost touch and progress.\n\nMembers:\nHaylea Berry - hberry@uoregon.edu\ncarranza@cs.cmu.edu\nanthony.valentino@biola.edu\ncleggett1@ggc.edu\nkreml.1@osu.edu\njames.chandler@wgu.edu\ndavid.mcmorries@oregonstate.edu\ndavid.mcmorries@oregonstate.edu\nmardecia_bell@ncsu.edu\nmardecia_bell@ncsu.edu\nbkelly@educause.edu\nvvogel@educause.edu\nLeo Howell - lfhowell@uoregon.edu\n\n[[EDUCAUSE]] - [[HEISC]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Electronics","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/40 - Hobbies/45 - Electronics/Electronics.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Electronics\n[[Hobbies & Entertainment]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Cybersecurity Internship","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/80 - GGC/87 - GGC Security/87.00 - Program/Cybersecurity Internship.md","lastModified":"2022-12-21T16:23:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Cybersecurity Internship\nIf I ever have the cycles to get a Cybersecurity Internship Program off the ground, I plan to use this framework:\n\nhttps://www.nist.gov/itl/applied-cybersecurity/nice/nice-framework-resource-center\n\n[[Training]] - [[Cybersecurity]] - [[Internship Program]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Institutions/National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST).md","lastModified":"2022-12-20T20:09:34.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST)\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Munchkin","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Games/Munchkin.md","lastModified":"2022-12-20T19:46:05.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Munchkin\n[[01.27 - Games]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"64.01 - Wood Badge S9-101-38","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Training/64.01 - Wood Badge S9-101-38/64.01 - Wood Badge S9-101-38.md","lastModified":"2022-12-08T17:01:34.000Z","tags":["#1","#2","#3","#4","#5"],"content":"# 64.01 - Wood Badge S9-101-38\n## Ticket\n[[S9-101-38 Ticket.pdf]]\n\n## Schools\n### Elementary Schools and Packs in High School Clusters\n- Mountain View High School Cluster\n\t- Dyer Elementary - Pack 500\n\t- Freeman's Mill - Pack 1510\n\t- Woodward Mill Elementary - Pack 510\n- Mill Creek High School Cluster\n\t- Duncan Creek Elementary - Pack 1597\n\t- Fort Daniel Elementary - Pack 598\n\t- Puckett's Mill Elementary - Pack 597\n- Seckinger High School Cluster\n\t- Harmony Elementary - Pack 598\n\t- Ivy Creek Elementary - Pack 542\n\t- Patrick Elementary - Pack 589\n- Dacula High School\n\t- Alcova Elementary - Pack 503\n\t- Dacula Elementary - Pack 503\n\t- Mulberry Elementary - Pack 500\n\n### School Pack Assignments\n[[schoolPackAssignments.jpg]]\n\n## Ticket Updates\n### Fall 2022\nLeggett S9-101-38 Ticket Update\n\nHello Lisa (and Dean),\n\nI’d like to update you on my progress working my ticket and hopefully move some beads. ;-)\n\nHere is an update on my ticket with reminders on each goal:\n\nVision\nAll families who are interested in participating in Cub Scouts, in or near the Mountain View High School (MVHS) cluster, are participating in a sustainable pack within one month of their registration.\n\nIt turns out that there are only three elementary schools in the MVHS cluster. At the time that I wrote my goals, I thought that there were five or six, so I have extended my scope to include some of the packs in neighboring clusters. You’ll see more specifics on this in Goal #2 below.\n\nGoal #1\nCollaborate with all packs in the MVHS cluster to ensure that 80% or more of their http://beascout.scouting.org pins are current prior to August 1st 2022 and again prior to August 1st 2023.\n\n\n\nGoal #2\nAttend 50% of fall roundups in the MVHS cluster in 2022 to network with leaders and ensure that families are matched with packs that meet their needs. e.g. meeting night, female dens, accessibility, etc.\n\nGoal #3\nBuild and share a Google Drive with templates and resources organized by role to be shared with packs starting August 1st 2022.\n\nAccomplishing this goal prior to the beginning of the 2022 scouting season turned out to be overly optimistic. My plan was to prepare the share as I updated \n\nGoal #4\nPrepare packing lists for the various pack events throughout the year to allow for “grab and go” preparedness. e.g. camping, pinewood derby, round-ups, etc.\n\nGoal #5\nTeach “Welcome to Cub Scout Leadership” course at 2022 University of Scouting and/or BALOO and share the previous digital and physical systems.\n\nPlease let me know if and how many beads you think I am ready to move over.\n\nThanks.\n\n--\nCharles \"Turtle” Leggett\nPack 1510 - Cubmaster \nS9-101-38 - Eagle\n\ncleggett@gmail.com\n706.255.8521\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Diverse Computing","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Companies/Diverse Computing.md","lastModified":"2022-11-03T16:21:50.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Diverse Computing\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Scoutland","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Places/Scoutland.md","lastModified":"2022-10-19T13:01:03.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Scoutland\n\n![[Scoutland Map.pdf]]\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Firefox","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Movies/Firefox.md","lastModified":"2022-10-10T22:58:24.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Firefox\n\n[Firefox (film) - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox_(film))","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Yellow River Park","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Places/Yellow River Park.md","lastModified":"2022-10-10T22:53:08.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Yellow River Park\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Tribble Mill Park","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Places/Tribble Mill Park.md","lastModified":"2022-10-10T22:53:00.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Tribble Mill Park\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Eric Bourdon","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Eric Bourdon.md","lastModified":"2022-10-10T15:01:16.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Eric Bourdon\n\n[[Stanley Black & Decker (sbdinc.com)]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"33.02 - 2015.05.02 - EDUCAUSE SPC & REN-ISAC","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/30 - Social/33 - Travel & Events/33.02 - 2015.05.02 - EDUCAUSE SPC & REN-ISAC/33.02 - 2015.05.02 - EDUCAUSE SPC & REN-ISAC.md","lastModified":"2022-09-27T16:41:35.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 33.02 - 2015.05.02 - EDUCAUSE SPC & REN-ISAC\n\nMay 2, 2015 - May 6, 2015\n\n# Hotel\nHilton Minnea