,"content":"# Audry Schlenker\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Melanie Schlenker","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Melanie Schlenker.md","lastModified":"2021-12-13T02:27:49.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Melanie Schlenker\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Danny Schlenker","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Danny Schlenker.md","lastModified":"2021-12-13T02:27:03.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Danny Schlenker\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Renee Schlenker","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Renee Schlenker.md","lastModified":"2021-12-13T02:20:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Renee Schlenker\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2021-06-25 - Mohammed and Jessica's Conflict over Quantum Outage","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/80 - GGC/81 - GGC Teams/81.08 - GGC Mohammed/2021/2021-06-25 - Mohammed and Jessica's Conflict over Quantum Outage.md","lastModified":"2021-12-13T02:17:33.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2021-06-25 - Mohammed and Jessica's Conflict over Quantum Outage\nConversation started at 6:05pm on 6/25.\n\n[6/24/2021 18:05] Jessica Walker\n\nMohammed Issah looks like whatever change was made on the Quantum side has not touched our issue with dropping frames/ video in Ocularis\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:08] Mohammed Issah\n\nLet's try to reboot the recorders, then we try to capture the errors and send back to Quantum.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:09] Jessica Walker\n\nOkay I will reboot them shortly\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:10] Jessica Walker\n\nWell, I will reboot oc-dm09N. That has been the machine we have been focused on, that way if we can get that machine working correctly we can apply the needed changes to the others\n\n(1 liked)\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:27] Jessica Walker\n\nMohammed Issah whatever was done, after the reboot... ALL camera footage on ALL cameras on oc-dm09N was lost\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:27] Jessica Walker\n\nI cant say whether or not it has resolved the issue yet as it has not been running long enough. But if PD needs it - do we have a back-up of the lost footage?!\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:29] Jessica Walker\n\nIm about to go log-in to all of the other device managers now and make sure they are NOT set for auto updates/ reboots\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:32] Jessica Walker\n\n***EDIT: I should say, the footage is still showing on the device manager under the D drive, but it has now lost its connection to Ocularis so playback is impossible\n\n[6/24/2021 18:39] Charles H. Leggett\n\nI am about to go on a hike with some Cub Scouts. Keep me posted on to progress and I’ll catch up in an hour or two.\n\n(1 liked)\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:43] Jessica Walker\n\nIf I don’t hear back from Mohammed so we can troubleshoot, just know none of the camera servers are set to restart tonight so we can revisit in the morning if needed. Enjoy your hike!\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:45] Jessica Walker\n\nI have to go pick up my groceries before my time frame is up … but when I get back I will contact onSSI to see if we can get the footage reconnected to the cameras for playback. It would be extremely helpful to know exactly what was done with Quantum today\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:52] Mohammed Issah\n\nWhat was done in Quantum is what I posted in Teams and in an email. We can get Quantum back but we need Occularis to reconnect the recorders.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:53] Jessica Walker\n\nThe recorder is connected. It’s just the old footage is no longer accessible.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 18:57] Mohammed Issah\n\nThe old footage should be able to retrieve from the library if the police need it. Let’s proceed with new recording and see if the problem is fixed.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 19:20] Jessica Walker\n\nYes we will on the current server oc-dm09n that I restarted. But before any of the other servers are restarted I/we need to confirm that we can reconnect the the playback footage for access via Ocularis. Otherwise we can NOT let the other servers restart without a change request and communication with PD\n\n\n[6/24/2021 19:21] Jessica Walker\n\nLooking back on it, I don’t think we should have made any changes to Quantum or restarted any of the servers without a change request. So now we have all learned that lesson.\n\n(1 liked)\n\n\n[6/24/2021 19:25] Mohammed Issah\n\nlet's get Occularis and confirm with them, and see how we read the old recording\n\n\n[6/24/2021 19:28] Jessica Walker\n\nYep. That’s the plan. Repair the damage done before moving forward with anything else\n\n\n[6/24/2021 19:39] Mohammed Issah\n\nNothing is destroyed, we are dealing with a physical and application layer issue with two different vendors. We have had this issue last year.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 19:41] Jessica Walker\n\nI understand nothing is destroyed. But currently information that should be accessible is not. So before moving forward with anything else that “damage” (causing something that should be available to not be) needs to be resolved.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 19:41] Jessica Walker\n\nAnd in the future we should open a change request before moving forward with anything camera or other service related before we make changes like this. I was not supposed to be at home working right now. I was supposed to be at the hospital with my grandmother.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 19:43] Jessica Walker\n\nI am waiting to hear back from onSSI support. If I need anything further from you tonight I will message you on Teams or give you a call. Thank you for responding after hours.\n\n(1 liked)\n\n\n[6/24/2021 19:44] Mohammed Issah\n\nI am getting Quantum back and already told them what happened.\n\n(1 liked)\n\n\n[6/24/2021 20:16] Charles H. Leggett\n\nMohammed, where do we stand? Have you been able to reach Quantum?\n\n\n[6/24/2021 20:18] Jessica Walker\n\nCharles H. Leggett I have been able to get the footage back. I am trying to figure out if alarm recording is working or not at this time (I just got the footage back about a minute ago so hadn't had time to update yet)\n\n[6/24/2021 20:20] Jessica Walker\n\nAlright Mohammed Issah and Charles H. Leggett looks like we are back to where we started - footage is reconnected (was a simple fix of refreshing the server via the OC aministrator) .... however we are still getting skips in footage/ dropped frames\n\nEdited\n\n\n[6/24/2021 20:21] Jessica Walker\n\nSo we can address that later on (at least not tonight)\n\n(1 liked)\n\nEdited\n\n\n[6/24/2021 20:26] Mohammed Issah\n\nQuantum, I am waiting for their call. Hopefully, Occularis can help us pin point what really need to done. Their software might have a problem.\n\n(1 liked)\n\n\n[6/24/2021 20:36] Charles H. Leggett\n\nAlright, so we’re stable for tonight. Right? Mohammed, please take the call with Quantum to confirm whether or not the change caused the issue and/or if it had the intended affect to fix the issue. Jessica is completely correct though, we need CAB approval to make any further changes, so please do not do anything with them other than check the config and logs. I am sorry that it didn’t occur to me to ask for a change request earlier today. Please make this your standard practice moving forward. No production changes without CAB approval.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 20:38] Charles H. Leggett\n\nJessica, how big of a gap do we have in our recording? How many cameras were affected? What (if anything) should I tell Llorens?\n\n\n[6/24/2021 20:45] Jessica Walker\n\nCurrently no gaps other than the brief time to restart the server and then services. Except for our standard missing frame gaps, that have a wide variety of length of time of video missing. At this point everything is exactly as it was so I do not believe we need to specifically reach out to Llorens. IIRC there are 58 cameras on oc-dm09n. So that would be the number that were affected during this brief disconnect between the cameras and their historical recordings\n\n\n[6/24/2021 20:46] Charles H. Leggett\n\nMohammed, please put in a Change Request for the work that you’ve already done on this and then we’ll use that same change moving forward to carry us through full resolution. Please share a link here when you’ve created the change.\n\n(1 liked)\n\n\n[6/24/2021 20:48] Charles H. Leggett\n\nOkay, thanks Jessica. I do want to update him when/if we have a solid plan on how to bring the NAS back into a healthy state.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 23:12] Mohammed Issah\n\n[https://helpdesk.ggc.edu/changes/1189566-file-too-large-to-store-on-ocularis-recorders](https://helpdesk.ggc.edu/changes/1189566-file-too-large-to-store-on-ocularis-recorders \"https://helpdesk.ggc.edu/changes/1189566-file-too-large-to-store-on-ocularis-recorders\")\n\n\n[6/24/2021 23:14] Mohammed Issah\n\nThe NAS don't have any problem. It is healthy and running. The error displaying is because of Tape library. They are sending a techinician to swap the blade in library tomorrow or Monday.\n\n[6/24/2021 23:16] Jessica Walker\n\nCan we please discuss as a team the swap and any risks or possible outages associated with it before the tech comes? We will likely need to inform PD of the downtime in recordings if any\n\n\n[6/24/2021 23:16] Mohammed Issah\n\nThe library connecting to the NAS has a problem but on the Veeam side is running ok. We should work with ocularis. Another suggestion is we spin out a new server move some of the cameras on it, then install recorder client and monitor it.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 23:17] Mohammed Issah\n\nNothing is been done, I am just updating what i am told.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 23:18] Jessica Walker\n\nMoving cameras to a new DM causes cameras to not have playback available. There are a couple of ways to test without causing that. Let’s discuss before a tech is scheduled to come out.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 23:18] Mohammed Issah\n\nThe tech is coming to work on the tape library not os the storage.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 23:19] Jessica Walker\n\nPlease let’s discuss this as a team before he/she comes and does anything to anything\n\n\n[6/24/2021 23:20] Jessica Walker\n\nThis issue has been ongoing for over a year, we do not need to jump into possible solutions without weighing the risks and informing the necessary parties first.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 23:21] Mohammed Issah\n\nAgain, the tape library is not connected to the cameras.  Thank you and good night.\n\n\n[6/24/2021 23:22] Jessica Walker\n\nI will let Charles chime in here once he sees the chat. Good night.\n \n\n[6/25/2021 05:21] Charles H. Leggett\n\nMohammed,\n\nLike Jessica said, \"let’s discuss this as a team before he/she comes and does anything to anything.\" Modifying the tape library is a change to a production system and needs to be approved by the CAB, communicated, and scheduled.\n\nAlso, the tape library is not the only error that we need to address. We need to work with them to understand all of the issues that the system is having and develop a solid plan on how we will use their help to resolve them all.\n\nFor example, the error that I saw about one of the disks having \"Excessive fragmentation\" needs to be addressed. I don't know enough about the system to know if it will take a downtime to defrag or if that's a background process.\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2021-09-27 - Ethics Complaint HR Matter","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/80 - GGC/81 - GGC Teams/81.01 - GGC Charles/2021/2021-09-27 - Ethics Complaint HR Matter.md","lastModified":"2021-12-13T02:13:27.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2021-09-27 - Ethics Complaint HR Matter\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"2021.10.07 - Conversations with Bijou and David","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/80 - GGC/81 - GGC Teams/81.01 - GGC Charles/2021/2021-USG Ethics Complaint/2021.10.07 - Conversations with Bijou and David/2021.10.07 - Conversations with Bijou and David.md","lastModified":"2021-12-13T02:13:12.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# 2021.10.07 - Conversations with Bijou and David\n[[2021-09-27 - Ethics Complaint HR Matter]]\n\n## Conversation with Bijou\n![[DavidAnon-1of5-Bijou.png]]\n![[DavidAnon-2of5-Bijou.png]]\n\n## Conv