ruth does not disappear.","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Quotes/When one averts one’s eyes from the truth, the truth does not disappear..md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T21:56:50.000Z","tags":[],"content":"[[Quotes]]\n\n# When one averts one’s eyes from the truth, the truth does not disappear.\n\n[[Mark Horstman]] of [[Manager Tools]] in [[Things I Think I Think]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"The only way to make sense out of change is to plunge into it, move with it, and join the dance.","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Quotes/The only way to make sense out of change is to plunge into it, move with it, and join the dance..md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T21:55:47.000Z","tags":[],"content":"[[Quotes]]\n\n# The only way to make sense out of change is to plunge into it, move with it, and join the dance.\n\n[[Alan Watts]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"“The secret of getting ahead is getting started. The secret of getting started is breaking your complex overwhelming tasks into small, manageable tasks, and then starting on the first one.”","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Quotes/“The secret of getting ahead is getting started. The secret of getting started is breaking your complex overwhelming tasks into small, manageable tasks, and then starting on the first one.”.md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T21:54:49.000Z","tags":[],"content":"[[Quotes]]\n\n# “The secret of getting ahead is getting started. The secret of getting started is breaking your complex overwhelming tasks into small, manageable tasks, and then starting on the first one.”\n\n[[Mark Twain]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"There's nothing like biting off more than you can chew, and then chewing it anyway.","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Quotes/There's nothing like biting off more than you can chew, and then chewing it anyway..md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T21:54:12.000Z","tags":[],"content":"[[Quotes]]\n\n# There's nothing like biting off more than you can chew, and then chewing it anyway.\n\n[[Mark Burnett]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Start the day running.","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Quotes/Start the day running..md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T21:52:36.000Z","tags":[],"content":"[[Quotes]]\n\n# Start the day running.\n\"Every morning in Africa, a gazelle wakes up. It knows it must run faster than the fastest lion or it will be killed. That same morning a lion wakes up. It knows it must outrun the slowest gazelle or it will starve to death. It doesn't matter whether you're a lion or gazelle – you better start the day running.\"\n\n[[Mark Horstman]] of [[Manager Tools]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"People don’t have hours anymore","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Quotes/People don’t have hours anymore.md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T21:52:24.000Z","tags":[],"content":"[[Quotes]]\n\n# People don’t have hours anymore\n“People don’t have hours anymore. They might say they work 8–10 hours a day. But they don’t. They work 15 minutes and 20 minutes and 25 minutes and 6 minutes and maybe 45 minutes if they’re lucky. And that just seems broken to me.”\n\n[[Jason Fried]] founder of [[Basecamp]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Invictus","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Poems/Invictus.md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T21:51:11.000Z","tags":[],"content":"[[Poetry]]\n\n# Invictus\n by [[William Ernest Henley]]\n \nOut of the night that covers me         \n     Black as the pit from pole to pole,   \nI thank whatever gods may be         \n     For my unconquerable soul.  \n   \nIn the fell clutch of circumstance         \n     I have not winced nor cried aloud.   \nUnder the bludgeonings of chance         \n     My head is bloody, but unbowed.    \n   \nBeyond this place of wrath and tears         \n     Looms but the Horror of the shade,   \nAnd yet the menace of the years         \n     Finds and shall find me unafraid.    \n   \nIt matters not how strait the gate,         \n     How charged with punishments the scroll,   \nI am the master of my fate,  \n     I am the captain of my soul.\n\t \n\t ![[Invictus-Comic.jpg]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"If","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Poems/If.md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T21:50:11.000Z","tags":[],"content":"[[Poetry]]\n\n# If\nby [[Rudyard Kipling]]\n\nIf you can keep your head when all about you     \n    Are losing theirs and blaming it on you,     \nIf you can trust yourself when all men doubt you,  \n    But make allowance for their doubting too;     \nIf you can wait and not be tired by waiting,  \n    Or being lied about, don’t deal in lies,  \nOr being hated, don’t give way to hating,  \n    And yet don’t look too good, nor talk too wise:  \n   \nIf you can dream—and not make dreams your master;     \n    If you can think—and not make thoughts your aim;     \nIf you can meet with Triumph and Disaster  \n    And treat those two impostors just the same;     \nIf you can bear to hear the truth you’ve spoken  \n    Twisted by knaves to make a trap for fools,  \nOr watch the things you gave your life to, broken,  \n    And stoop and build ’em up with worn-out tools:  \n   \nIf you can make one heap of all your winnings  \n    And risk it on one turn of pitch-and-toss,  \nAnd lose, and start again at your beginnings  \n    And never breathe a word about your loss;  \nIf you can force your heart and nerve and sinew  \n    To serve your turn long after they are gone,     \nAnd so hold on when there is nothing in you  \n    Except the Will which says to them: ‘Hold on!’  \n   \nIf you can talk with crowds and keep your virtue,     \n    Or walk with Kings—nor lose the common touch,  \nIf neither foes nor loving friends can hurt you,  \n    If all men count with you, but none too much;  \nIf you can fill the unforgiving minute  \n    With sixty seconds’ worth of distance run,     \nYours is the Earth and everything that’s in it,     \n    And—which is more—you’ll be a Man, my son!  \n  \n\n[[Poetry]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Alana DeAngelis","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Alana DeAngelis.md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T15:34:59.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Alana DeAngelis\n\n- Significant Other\n    - Matt\n- Favorites\n    - Hot Chocolate\n    - Moscow Mules","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Debee Lee","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Debee Lee.md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T15:34:42.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Debee Lee\n## Timeline\n- 2018.11 - Husband passed away\n- 2019.01 - Retired from GaTech","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Simon Sinek","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Simon Sinek.md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T15:34:11.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Simon Sinek\n[[Christopher Smith]] introduced you to his work in [[2018]]\n\n- [[Leaders Eat Last: Why Some Teams Pull Together and Others Don't]]\n\n[[Videos]]\n- \n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Russ Mathis","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Russ Mathis.md","lastModified":"2021-12-12T15:34:06.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Russ Mathis","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Information Security Economics","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Ideas/Information Security Economics/Information Security Economics.md","lastModified":"2021-12-11T23:59:09.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Information Security Economics","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Bruce Schneier","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Bruce Schneier.md","lastModified":"2021-12-11T23:50:25.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Bruce Schneier\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"CIA's Mysterious Kryptos Sculpture","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Oddities/CIA's Mysterious Kryptos Sculpture.md","lastModified":"2021-12-11T23:45:46.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# CIA's Mysterious Kryptos Sculpture\n\n[Finally, a New Clue to Solve 