":"Allison","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Allison.md","lastModified":"2021-11-13T12:18:58.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Allison\n[[Georgia Institute of Technology (GaTech)]] - [[OMS Cybersecurity Student Services Team]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Anthony Olamide Ogidi","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Anthony Olamide Ogidi.md","lastModified":"2021-11-13T12:18:58.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Anthony Olamide Ogidi\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Austin Kleon","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Austin Kleon.md","lastModified":"2021-11-13T12:18:58.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Austin Kleon\nAustin Kleon (@austinkleon) is a writer who draws. He’s the bestselling author of Steal Like An Artist and other books.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Brian Smart","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Brian Smart.md","lastModified":"2021-11-13T12:18:58.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Brian Smart\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Carl Woods","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Carl Woods.md","lastModified":"2021-11-13T12:18:58.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Carl Woods\nManager of Rec Center\n\n2020.08.06:\nis also managing Res Halls now that Kyle Boone has left","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Dr. TJ Arant","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Dr. TJ Arant.md","lastModified":"2021-11-13T12:18:58.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Dr. TJ Arant\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Eric Gibson Meyer","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Eric Gibson Meyer.md","lastModified":"2021-11-13T12:18:58.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Eric Gibson Meyer\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Jennifer","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/People/Jennifer.md","lastModified":"2021-11-13T12:18:58.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Jennifer\n[[Georgia Institute of Technology (GaTech)]] - [[OMS Cybersecurity Student Services Team]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"Top 10 Life Must Haves","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/10 - Personal/11 - Health & Fitness/Top 10 Life Must Haves.md","lastModified":"2021-10-09T11:56:28.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# Top 10 Life Must Haves\n\n1. Family & Friends\n2. Communitiy of Purpose\n3. Job Satisfaction\n4. Time in the Outdoors\n5. My Workshop & Projects\n6. Mental & Physical Health\n7. Good Food & Drink\n8. Fun\n9. Apple Products\n10. Enough $ to support the first 9\n","bookmarked":false},{"title":"SOTA & POTA","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/40 - Hobbies/42 - Radio/SOTA & POTA/SOTA & POTA.md","lastModified":"2021-06-30T13:38:36.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# SOTA & POTA\n[Summits on the Air](https://sotawatch.sota.org.uk/en/) is an amateur radio awards scheme. To participate in this scheme you do not become a \"member\", there are no dues to be paid or membership cards to be issued. You can join in straight away! Just go to [SOTAwatch](https://sotawatch.sota.org.uk/) to see what is happening right now in SOTA. To post to SOTA facilities you will need to [register an account](https://www.sotadata.org.uk/en/register). Then you will be able to add alerts and spots on SOTAwatch (which will likely help a lot, if you plan to activate) and upload your chases or activations to the SOTA database. There is no charge for registering. The [SOTA Reflector](https://reflector.sota.org.uk/) uses a separate user account system; so to join in with discussions there simply click on the “Sign Up” button. We recommend that you save a copy of your passwords in a safe place - every week we have to help people who have forgotten their passwords!\n\nYou can then Chase or Activate when you feel like it - SOTA is global, activations can take place throughout the 24 hours of the day. Once you transfer your log to the database there is a permanent record and you can check your entries against those of the stations that you contacted, and keep track of your progress towards awards. Later you might wish to purchase awards, trophies or goods from our on-line shop. These purchases and the occasional donation are the means of financing the SOTA facilities.\n\n[SOTAwatch](https://sotawatch.sota.org.uk/en/)\n\n## SOTA Frequencies (commonly mentioned on SOTAwatch)\n2m\n142.580\n144.000\n144.410\n144.500\n144.520\n144.550\n144.960\n145.000\n145.350\n145.375\n145.400\n145.412\n145.425\n145.450\n145.475\n145.500\n145.525\n145.550\n145.575\n146.000\n**146.460**\n**146.490**\n146.500\n**146.520** - National Simplex Calling Frequency\n**146.550**\n146.560\n**146.580** - North America Adventure Frequency\n\n70cm\n432.920\n432.980\n433.000\n433.020\n433.040\n433.080\n433.120\n433.180\n433.400\n433.500\n443.525\n**446.000** - National Simplex Calling Frequency\n\nBold were recommended by N1RBD - Richard\n\n## SOTA Primer by N4HNH - Douglas\n[[SOTA Primer by N4HNH.pdf]]","bookmarked":false},{"title":"neovim","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/Applications/neovim.md","lastModified":"2021-04-05T04:19:15.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# neovim\nhttps://github.com/rockerBOO/awesome-neovim","bookmarked":false},{"title":"FY21 CARES 2 Funding","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Areas/Management/Purchasing/83.08 - Purchasing/83.08.00 - Purchasing Strategy/FY21 CARES 2 Funding/FY21 CARES 2 Funding.md","lastModified":"2021-03-01T13:03:59.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# FY21 CARES 2 Funding","bookmarked":false},{"title":"GARS want, sale, swap and information net","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/30 - Social/32 - Clubs/32.03 - GARS/GARS want, sale, swap and information net.md","lastModified":"2021-03-01T13:03:57.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# GARS want, sale, swap and information net\n\nCreated: Dec 19, 2014 8:18 AM\n\nMonday nights at 20:00\n\n147.075+ pl82.5, 53.110- no pl, echo-link(w4gr-r), 442.100+ pl 100hz.","bookmarked":false},{"title":"W4GR - Gwinnett Amateur Radio Society (GARS)","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/30 - Social/32 - Clubs/32.03 - GARS/W4GR - Gwinnett Amateur Radio Society (GARS).md","lastModified":"2021-03-01T13:03:57.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# W4GR - Gwinnett Amateur Radio Society (GARS)\n\nCreated: Dec 19, 2014 8:36 AM\n\nThe Gwinnett Amateur Radio Society is an amateur radio club serving Gwinnett County, Georgia, in the North Metro Atlanta area. We are a Special Service club affiliated with the ARRL. With over 250 members, GARS is an active part of the Amateur Radio community, and plays an important role in Gwinnett County. We invite you to join us at our next meeting to learn more about us.\n\n[http://www.gars.org/w4gr/](http://www.gars.org/w4gr/)\n\nhttp://www.gars.org/w4gr/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=1&Itemid=243\n\nGARS (Gwinnett Amateur Radio Society) holds nets on Monday and Wednesday nights.\n\nOn Monday night at 2000 local time GARS holds the want, sale, swap and information net.\n\nOn Wednesday nights at 2030 local time GARS hold the Know It All Net.\n\nThis net is a discussion for all who check-in and discuss the topic for the night.\n\nThis could be JT-65, echo-link, grounding stations, HF operations, etc..\n\nThe net liason Phil, N4LNE can be reached at by email. [n4lne@arrl.net](mailto:n4lne@arrl.net)\n\nThe nets are run on 147.075+ pl82.5, 53.110- no pl, echo-link(w4gr-r), 442.100+ pl 100hz.\n\nhttp://www.gars.org/w4gr/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=87&Itemid=228","bookmarked":false},{"title":"GaTech Radio Frequencies","path":"/Users/cleggett1/Obsidian/TheCollective/Lists/_OLD/30 - Social/32 - Clubs/32.05 - W4AQL/GaTech Radio Frequencies.md","lastModified":"2021-03-01T13:03:57.000Z","tags":[],"content":"# GaTech Radio Frequencies\n\nCreated: Dec 19, 2014 8:25 AM\n\nContrary to Radio Reference's data (below) 463.8125 seems to be GT Facilities.\n\nRadio Reference:\n\n463.81250 WQLT405 RM GT Trans Parking & Transportation (Color Code 1, Repeater Slot 2, 